\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Ex-\uc2 Twitter\uc2  executives sue \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for $128m in unpaid severance\b0\par\par\uc2 Nick Robins-Early \par \uc2 446 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 March 2024\par 22:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Suit by former employees, including ex-CEO \uc2 Parag Agrawal\uc2 , follows a separate legal complaint by other workers seeking $500m\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is facing a $128m lawsuit from four former \uc2 Twitter\uc2  executives who allege the billionaire tech mogul failed to pay them severance after buying the social network. The suit, filed on Monday in California, follows a separate legal complaint last year by rank-and-file employees seeking $500m in unpaid severance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause Musk decided he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to pay Plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 severance benefits, he simply fired them without reason, then made up fake cause and appointed employees of his various companies to uphold his decision,\u8221\'20\'1D the suit alleges.\par \par \uc2 The four plaintiffs in the case include \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former CEO \uc2 Parag Agrawal\uc2 , former CFO \uc2 Ned Segal\uc2 , former general counsel \uc2 Sean Edgett\uc2  and former chief legal officer \uc2 Vijaya Gadde\uc2 . Musk fired all of them amid a string of mass layoffs after he acquired \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for $44bn in 2022, claiming at the time he did not need to pay the executives severance because they were terminated for cause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Cause\u8217\'20\'19 is not \u8216\'20\'18board-approved business decisions that Musk dislikes\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D the complaint reads. \u8220\'20\'1CHe claimed in his termination letters that each Plaintiff committed \u8216\'20\'18gross negligence\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18willful misconduct\u8217\'20\'19 without citing a single fact in support of this claim.\u8221\'20\'1D Musk and X have not issued any public comments on the case. Musk\u8217\'20\'19s frequent legal representative, the lawyer \uc2 Alex Spiro\uc2 , did not immediately return request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is one of several legal actions related to Musk\u8217\'20\'19s unwilling takeover of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and subsequent operation of the platform, which he renamed X. The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/technology/space/spacex-illegally-fired-workers-critical-elon-musk-us-labor-agency-says-2024-01-03/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a complaint}}}\uc2  earlier this year alleging that Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  rocket company illegally fired eight workers because they issued a letter criticizing his leadership.\par \par \uc2 Musk laid off about 80% of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  staff after he took over the company, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/live/world-us-canada-65247272/page/2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the BBC}}}\uc2  in an interview last year. The site has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/oct/27/elon-musk-x-twitter-takeover-revenue-users-advertising"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled in numerous ways since his acquisition}}}\uc2 , including facing declining ad revenues and researchers documenting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/oct/28/elon-musk-twitter-hate-speech-concerns-stock-exchange-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a surge in hate speech }}}\uc2  as Musk rolled back content moderation efforts. He originally tried to back out of the acquisition, but \uc2 Twitter\uc2  sued to force its completion.\par \par \uc2 Musk has blamed the decline of ad revenue on anti-hate monitoring groups that published reports detailing racist and extremist content on the platform. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/nov/17/anti-hate-group-says-lawsuit-from-elon-musks-x-riddled-with-deficiencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched suits}}}\uc2  against two of the organizations, Media Matters and the Center For Countering Digital Hate, which are currently ongoing. A California judge is expected to decide this week on whether to dismiss the suit against the Center For Countering Digital Hate.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240304ek34003jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
