\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Missouri bus drivers protest after colleague finds noose at work\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 561 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2024\par 14:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amin Mitchell, who is Black, posted about incident on social media and believes it was racist response to disagreement with manager\par \par \uc2 Bus drivers in Missouri staged a protest this week after a co-worker found a noose at his work station and posted about it on social media.\par \par \uc2 Amin Mitchell, a diesel mechanic, shared video of the noose on the floor of his employer \u8211\'20\'13 Missouri Central School Bus \u8211\'20\'13 on \uc2 Facebook{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/amin.mitchell/posts/pfbid0SuiXJ5rWZCAK3K3ZQ96BHw8yqjiiH64esaEAZUyaF8BJwvmLxpXGDjzDvn4fz8i4l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on 22 February}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEver since I been working here I\u8217\'20\'19ve been filing prejudice complaints on BOTH of my supervisors. I\u8217\'20\'19m making a HR complaint at least twice a week about equality with these two,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell wrote in his post. \u8220\'20\'1CTo the point where I voiced how uncomfortable I feel at work. Today I had enough! I came into work this morning and found a NOOSE!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mitchell, who is Black, told the St Louis Post-Dispatch that he believes the noose was a racist response to a disagreement with a manager and an intimidation tactic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody can tell me that I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about. That wasn\u8217\'20\'19t there when I left, it was there when I got there in the morning,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell told the local news station Fox2. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like I was meant to see it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Colleagues of Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s from Missouri Central School Bus and at least 100 other drivers, members of the \uc2 Laborers\u8217\'20\'19 International Union of North America\uc2 , stood by his side \u8211\'20\'13 calling in sick and stopping work. The work stoppage, which began on Monday, forced the cancellation of after-school activities at St Louis public schools and has disrupted more than 50 bus routes, drawing the attention of parents and students to the incident involving Mitchell.\par \par \uc2 The St Louis public school district posted an update about the situation on their website: \u8220\'20\'1CAs many of you may already be aware, this morning saw minimal progress in resolving the situation. Fifty-six bus routes remained uncovered due to the ongoing dispute between drivers and management at Missouri Central. It appears the number will be similar this afternoon. We are actively utilizing our communication channels to inform those affected by these disruptions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe encourage you to continue monitoring these communication channels for updates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We are cancelling most after-school activities today, Tue., 2/27. Exceptions: After-care programs will remain open on a normal schedule. Decisions regarding athletics will be made on a school-by-school basis. Contact your school\u8217\'20\'19s athletic director with questions about sports. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mkRbmCd4FB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mkRbmCd4FB}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Saint Louis Public Schools (@SLPS_INFO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SLPS_INFO/status/1762545712447848915?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In the update, the school district called the allegations against Mitchell \u8220\'20\'1Ctroubling\u8221\'20\'1D and said it hoped for a swift resolution.\par \par \uc2 Local NAACP chapters have demanded a federal or state investigation into the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe noose is a symbol of hate and sends a clear message of racial terror and the potential for violence,\u8221\'20\'1D the Missouri NAACP president, Nimrod Chapel Jr, said.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to Fox2, Missouri Central condemned discrimination and said it would also conduct a private investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt Missouri Central, our policy is to provide and foster a work environment that is welcoming to all regardless of age, race, ethnicity and sexual orientation,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is zero tolerance for any behavior that violates this policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240227ek2r002uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
