\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US man accused of making $1.8m from listening in on wife\u8217\'20\'19s remote work calls\b0\par\par\uc2 Kalyeena Makortoff \par \uc2 612 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2024\par 11:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Regulator charges Tyler Loudon with insider trading in case that could fuel arguments about working from home\u8226\'20\'22 Business live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 US regulators have accused a man of making $1.8m (\u163\'00\'A31.4m) by trading on confidential information he overheard while his wife was on a remote call, in a case that could fuel arguments against working from home.\par \par \uc2 The Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) said it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/news/press-release/2024-24"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged Tyler Loudon with insider trading}}}\uc2  after he \u8220\'20\'1Ctook advantage of his remote working conditions\u8221\'20\'1D and profited from private information related to the oil firm \uc2 BP\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to buy an Ohio-based travel centre and truck-stop business last year.\par \par \uc2 The SEC claims that Loudon, who is based in Houston, Texas, listened in on several remote calls held by his wife, a \uc2 BP\uc2  merger and acquisitions manager who had been working on the planned deal in a home office 20ft (6 metres) away.\par \par \uc2 The regulator said Loudon went on a buying spree, purchasing more than 46,000 shares in the takeover target, TravelCentres, without his wife\u8217\'20\'19s knowledge, weeks before the deal was announced on 16 February 2023. TravelCentres of America\u8217\'20\'19s stock soared by nearly 71% after the deal was announced. Loudon then sold off all of his shares, making a $1.8m profit.\par \par \uc2 Loudon eventually confessed to his wife, and claimed that he had bought the shares because he wanted to make enough money so that she did not have to work long hours anymore.\par \par \uc2 She reported his dealings to her bosses at \uc2 BP\uc2 , which later fired her despite having no evidence that she knowingly leaked information to her husband. She eventually moved out of the couple\u8217\'20\'19s home and filed for divorce.\par \par \uc2 Today we charged a Houston resident with insider trading for using non-public information he obtained from his wife, a manager with \uc2 BP\uc2 , without her knowledge, about the company\u8217\'20\'19s planned merger with \uc2 TravelCenters of America\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lJ9SjHBDcX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/lJ9SjHBDcX}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (@SECGov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SECGov/status/1760802801503076405?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Eric Werner, the regional director of the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s Fort Worth office in Texas, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe allege that Mr Loudon took advantage of his remote working conditions and his wife\u8217\'20\'19s trust to profit from information he knew was confidential. The SEC remains committed to prosecuting such malfeasance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The case is expected to fuel arguments \u8211\'20\'13 particularly at US companies \u8211\'20\'13 for workers to return to the office, reversing the boom in home working prompted by the pandemic lockdowns. Banks such as \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  have been forcing some staff to come in five days a week, while others such as \uc2 Google\uc2  are factoring office attendance into their regular staff performance reviews.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about security and confidential information could end up trumping studies that show working from home {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/feb/17/working-from-home-can-bring-big-health-benefits-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can deliver big health benefits}}}\uc2 , allowing people to eat more healthily, feel less stressed and have lower blood pressure.\par \par \uc2 Loudon did not deny the allegations outlined in the SEC complaint, which was filed at the US district court for southern Texas, and instead agreed to a partial judgment, subject to court approval. That partial judgment will ban him from taking company leadership roles, force him to repay the money he made from the trade \u8211\'20\'13 with interest \u8211\'20\'13 on top of an extra fine to be determined by the court.\par \par \uc2 He is facing criminal charges from the US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office for the southern district of Texas.\par \par \uc2 The SEC filing said Loudon, who is in his early 40s, is employed with an unnamed publicly listed company but is not in a sector supervised by the regulator.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240223ek2n001mk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
