\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Twenty-five US universities face calls to cancel \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  contracts\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 672 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 February 2024\par 12:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Student organizers, faculty and workers protest against coffee company\u8217\'20\'19s response to union organizing efforts\par \par \uc2 Student organizers, faculty and workers at 25 university campuses across the US are calling for their institutions to cancel their contracts with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in protest against the company\u8217\'20\'19s response to union organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  gets an F\u8221\'20\'1D actions will take place on Thursday at campuses including the \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2 , the \uc2 University of South Florida\uc2 , \uc2 UW-Madison\uc2 , \uc2 New York University\uc2 , Georgetown and Rutgers.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of college campuses have \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  locations on them, either through licensing agreements or through contracts with third-party vendors.\par \par \uc2 Student organizers are circulating petitions pushing their universities to cut contracts with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  on their campuses and raise public awareness about their efforts to hold the company accountable and support workers\u8217\'20\'19 unionizing efforts at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to make sure that our tuition dollars aren\u8217\'20\'19t continuing to enable this company and the injustices they commit,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Ramirez, a student organizer at UCLA where students submitted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailynews.com/2024/01/29/ucla-uc-riverside-students-petition-to-remove-starbucks-from-campuses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition}}}\uc2  in January to the university to cut its contract with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in response to the company\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive campaign against unionization efforts in its stores.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re seeing many universities across the country also taking a stand against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , and now many people are realizing that this company isn\u8217\'20\'19t as progressive as it claims, and that we have a real voice in how these companies treat their workers and it\u8217\'20\'19s our responsibility to take a stand,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedp.com/article/2024/01/penn-starbucks-union-39th-walnut"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nearly 400 Starbucks stores}}}\uc2  around the US have won union elections to join Starbucks Workers United since December 2021, when stores in Buffalo, New York, first unionized. On Tuesday, 21 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/starbucks-union-elections_n_65d24123e4b0ce1bdc39d7d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  for union recognition, the single largest single-day filing for the union campaign.\par \par \uc2 But a first union contract for any store has yet to be reached.\par \par \uc2 Students at Cornell successfully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cornellsun.com/2023/08/16/cornell-to-end-partnership-with-starbucks-by-june-2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed}}}\uc2  the university to not renew its contract with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , in response to local union campaigns where workers faced significant pushback, including the closure of a store. In the wake of that success, similar campaigns have emerged at several other college campuses around the US.\par \par \uc2 Haya Odeh {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cornellsun.com/2023/08/16/cornell-to-end-partnership-with-starbucks-by-june-2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worked}}}\uc2  as a barista at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in North Carolina and was a leader in union organizing efforts until her transfer request \u8211\'20\'13when she started college at the \uc2 University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 was denied. Now she is leading student organizing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailytarheel.com/article/2024/01/opinion-effective-starbucks-boycott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts}}}\uc2  on campus as part of a campaign against the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are college students. We are the next generation of workers and consumers. We\u8217\'20\'19re just not going to let \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  slide with the injustices they pass on to workers. Their union busting is just the very tip of the iceberg. Their labor practices and how they treat their workers, we want to push the message that we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to stand for this as students,\u8221\'20\'1D said Odeh.\par \par \uc2 Since the Starbucks Workers United campaign first started, workers have filed hundreds of unfair labor practice charges against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has not admitted wrongdoing over the union campaign.\par \par \uc2 In a recent post-hearing brief before an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  administrative judge, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  attorneys joined attorneys at Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s, Amazon and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  in arguing that the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  is unconstitutional in beginning proceedings over labor law violations by these companies. In January, \uc2 Starbucks{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://one.starbucks.com/get-the-facts/starbucks-petitions-scotus-for-level-playing-field/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised}}}\uc2  a decision by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to hear their appeals case over firing seven \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers at a unionized store in Memphis.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  spokesperson denied all allegations of union busting in response to the actions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe disagree with claims that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  engages in \u8216\'20\'18union-busting\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D they said in an email.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  believes that our direct relationship as partners is core to the culture and experiences created in our stores, we respect our partners\u8217\'20\'19 right to organize and collectively bargain \u8211\'20\'13 and remain committed to our stated aim of reaching ratified contracts for US union-represented stores in 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240221ek2l001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
