\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be historic\u8217\'20\'19: US flight attendants picket at major airports\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 744 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 February 2024\par 15:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Protests come as over two-thirds of flight attendants in the US are currently in new union contract negotiations\par \par \uc2 Flight attendants are holding picket protests at over 30 major airports across the US on Tuesday as part of the Worldwide Flight Attendant Day of Action.\par \par \uc2 Picket line events are planned in New York City, Orlando, Miami, San Francisco, Charlotte, Washington DC, Dallas, Atlanta, Chicago, Boston, Cleveland, Las Vegas, Los Angeles and several other major cities. Some 100,000 flight attendants across three different labor unions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CWAUnion/status/1756048247079006658"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected}}}\uc2  to participate.\par \par \uc2 The protests come as over two-thirds of flight attendants in the US, at \uc2 United Airlines\uc2 , \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2 , \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2 , \uc2 Air Wisconsin\uc2 , \uc2 American Airlines\uc2 , Omni and Frontier, are currently in new union contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLegacy sexism that traditionally devalued our jobs must be stamped out and replaced with the true value of our work,\u8221\'20\'1D the group said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/event_campaigns/213-day-of-action?fbclid=IwAR1kgvaD2RW3G0f0ZBxf-sLbc3ksVo-Mla_bzN7F55hM2A6dN3h3X27EYXw_aem_ARI7vmwjT6gj-sZyCVnjz6Inu6jXl-Nd_2rkBmZSNjKZsen-en2TgGa2iyUrOCBp0rY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  for the event. \u8220\'20\'1COur time on the job must be compensated. We need retirement security. We need flexibility and control of our lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over 26,000 flight attendants at \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  represented by the \uc2 Association of Professional Flight Attendants\uc2  (\uc2 APFA\uc2 ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unitedafa.org/news/2023/8/30/american-airlines-flight-attendants-vote-to-authorize-strike-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to authorize a strike in August 2023 with 99.47% in favor. At \uc2 Air Wisconsin\uc2 , an American Eagle Carrier, flight attendants voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afacwa.org/arw_vote_authorize_a_strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 99% }}}\uc2  in favor of a strike authorization and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/southwest-airlines-flight-attendants-vote-approve-strike-authorization-2024-01-23/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 98%}}}\uc2  of flight attendants at \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2  voted in favor of a strike authorization last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the wages that we have, it\u8217\'20\'19s just unsustainable. We can\u8217\'20\'19t live off of these wages,\u8221\'20\'1D said Doris Millard, a flight attendant at \uc2 Air Wisconsin\uc2  for 44 years who said her pay had changed little since she started at the airline in 1980. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like I\u8217\'20\'19m being forced to give up my career and find something else or continue to basically live in poverty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Flight attendants represented by the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants-CWA\uc2  (\uc2 AFA\uc2 ) at \uc2 United Airlines{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unitedafa.org/news/2023/12/14/united-flight-attendants-demonstrate-at-19-airports-nationwide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed }}}\uc2  for federal mediation in December 2023 and have held numerous picket protests amid long delays in their fight for a new union contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe federal mediator requested by the \uc2 AFA\uc2  has scheduled our first negotiations session for March 19. We\u8217\'20\'19re looking forward to working with \uc2 AFA\uc2  to narrow the issues so that we can continue to work toward an industry-leading agreement for our flight attendants,\u8221\'20\'1D said a \uc2 United Airlines\uc2  spokesperson in an email.\par \par \uc2 Flight attendants at \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2  will be announcing their strike authorization vote results on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Melissa Osborne has worked as a flight attendant for 23 years and has worked the past seven years at \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She said union contracts had experienced cuts to wages and benefits since the 9/11 tragedy and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=2ahUKEwjr3J6UzqaEAxW-4skDHT7WCLcQFnoECCUQAQ&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newyorker.com%2Fmagazine%2F2022%2F05%2F30%2Fflight-attendants-fighting-back&usg=AOvVaw0bXa6VOZ_Tthr5Eo9wiG0d&opi=89978449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downturn }}}\uc2  experienced by the airlines industry. But she added working conditions have exponentially worsened since the Covid-19 pandemic began in 2020, when workers had to deal with exposure to the virus, an uptick in unruly passengers and, more recently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/01/25/alaska-airlines-boeing-737-max-9-grounding-will-cost-150-million.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issues}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Boeing\uc2  planes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven today putting on my uniform and going to work, there are several layers of anxiety all of us experience,\u8221\'20\'1D said Osborne. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like that level of stress is not being recognized by the company, they\u8217\'20\'19re not recognizing our value and what we do everyday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She rejected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/alaska-airlines-flight-attendant-union-los-angeles-houston-texas-2023-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2  that the economic proposals from the union were not feasible. She said \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2  and others had come out of the Covid-19 pandemic with record profits and \uc2 Alaska Airlines{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/business/boeing-aerospace/as-major-airlines-hike-pilot-pay-alaska-airlines-boosts-wages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave}}}\uc2  pilots pay raises outside of contract negotiations and recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/advisor/credit-cards/travel-rewards/alaska-airlines-agrees-to-buy-hawaiian-airlines/#:~:text=Alaska%20Airlines%20announced%20that%20it,price%20of%20%2418%20per%20share."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reached}}}\uc2  a deal to acquire \uc2 Hawaiian Airlines\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Osborne said the picket protests were being conducted by flight attendants across different unions and airlines because they were all experiencing similar issues and fighting for similar industry improvements. The idea to organize picket protests across different airlines and unions, she said, came from Iceland where she attended a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/23/europe/iceland-women-strike-scli-intl/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationwide women\u8217\'20\'19s strike }}}\uc2  in October 2023 across different jobs and industries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook at all of us, all fighting for contracts, all having the same sort of obstacles to overcome with our negotiations, dealing with the same company responses,\u8221\'20\'1D said Osborne. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be historic. It\u8217\'20\'19s so impactful to tell companies we see what you\u8217\'20\'19re doing and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to stand together in solidarity. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been in the industry for 23 years and I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen anything like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240213ek2d001ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
