\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Biden hails robust jobs market as proof US economy is \u8216\'20\'18strongest in the world\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Dominic Rushe in New York \par \uc2 552 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 February 2024\par 17:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 42\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US adds 353,000 new jobs over month as growth in hiring gives boost to president, whose polling on economy has remained weak\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden declared the strong jobs figures released on Friday as proof that \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s economy is the strongest in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US jobs market defied fears of a downturn again, when figures were released on growth in January, with employers adding 353,000 new jobs over the month, the labor department announced.\par \par \uc2 The jobs market has remained strong despite an aggressive series of interest rate rises by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , aimed at cooling the economy and bringing down the rate of inflation. In January the unemployment rate was 3.7%, close to a 50-year low.\par \par \uc2 Economists had been predicting that the US would add less than 200,000 jobs over the month. The labor department also revised its job gains for December up from an initial estimate of 216,000 to 333,000.\par \par \uc2 The news was another boost to the US president, whose polling on the economy has remained weak despite the robust jobs market. Hiring was broad-based with gains in healthcare, government, professional and business services and retail.\par \par \uc2 Biden pointed out that the US has added almost 15m jobs since he was sworn in in January 2021.\par \par \uc2 In a statement from the White House, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we saw more proof, with another month of strong wage gains and employment gains of over 350,000 in January, continuing the strong growth from last year \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s great news for working families that wages, wealth and jobs are higher now than before the pandemic, and I won\u8217\'20\'19t stop fighting to lower costs and build an economy from the middle out and bottom up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He further said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to stand in the way of efforts by congressional Republicans to enact massive tax giveaways for the wealthy and big corporations; cut Medicare, Medicaid and social security; and raise costs for American families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But there have been signs recently that the strong labor market is weakening. On Wednesday, ADP, the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest payroll supplier, said private employers had added 107,000 new jobs in January, less than analysts expected and down from 158,000 in December.\par \par \uc2 Several large employers have also announced layoffs recently, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/jan/12/citi-bank-layoffs-earnings#:~:text=Citigroup%20to%20cut%2020%2C000%20jobs,quarterly%20loss%20%7C%20Banking%20%7C%20The%20Guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Citigroup, }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/feb/01/deutsche-bank-to-cut-3500-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deutsche Bank}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/jan/30/paypal-job-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PayPal}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/2024/01/30/ups-layoffs-2024/72405535007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UPS}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US added 2.7m jobs last year even as the Fed drove interest rates up to a 22-year high.\par \par \uc2 This week, Fed chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  said the US economy remained resilient and the rate of inflation \u8211\'20\'13 which has fallen from a high of just over 9% in June 2022 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/jan/11/us-inflation-rate-december-federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  3.4% in December}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 was moving in the right direction.\par \par \uc2 But the Fed is still targeting an annual rate of inflation of 2%. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/jan/31/fed-interest-rates-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Powell warned:}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CInflation is still too high, the ongoing progress in bringing it down is not assured, and the path forward is uncertain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The latest jobs report will add pressure for the Fed to maintain its current interest rates. \u8220\'20\'1CThe big picture for now is that markets are no longer convinced that the Fed will cut rates in May, let alone March,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240202ek22001vw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
