\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US government\uc2  employees plan to fast for Gaza in protest against Biden policy\b0\par\par\uc2 Jonathan Guyer \par \uc2 727 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 January 2024\par 16:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Feds United for Peace, group of workers from more than two dozen agencies, to stage one-day hunger strike on Thursday\par \par \uc2 US government\uc2  employees are planning a \u8220\'20\'1Cday of fasting for Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D this week to draw attention to the humanitarian crisis in the territory and to denounce Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policy toward Israel.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for Feds United for Peace, a group of several dozen government employees frustrated with the Gaza crisis who organized an office walkout earlier in the month, told the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  that on Thursday its members will stage a one-day hunger strike. Participating federal employees are expected to show up to their offices dressed in black or wearing keffiyeh scarves or other symbols of Palestinian solidarity.\par \par \uc2 A federal employee speaking on behalf of the group said the Day of Fasting is a response to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s use of \u8220\'20\'1Cstarvation as a weapon of war by intentionally withholding food from entering Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D, citing \uc2 UN\uc2  reporting that up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/19/us-food-medicine-aid-gaza-un-famine-warnings-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2 million people in the territory}}}\uc2  are at risk of famine.\par \par \uc2 The group says its members represent more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/C2IocLhp5vo/?img_index=3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two dozen agencies}}}\uc2 , among them the departments of defense, homeland security and state, and include career public servants and political appointees. They expect hundreds of government employees to participate.\par \par \uc2 A walkout staged by the group earlier this month drew strong reactions in Washington, with national security officials from both parties {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/opinion/white-house/4379866-white-house-staffers-protesting-biden-should-be-fired/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticizing}}}\uc2  their protests as insubordination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey deserve to be fired,\u8221\'20\'1D the House speaker, Mike Johnson, a Republican from Louisiana, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/01/14/mike-johnson-gop-federal-workers-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Feds United for Peace representatives say that their goal is to force a conversation in their offices, where many federal employees might support a ceasefire but fear retribution for speaking out, or are afraid to even casually discuss politics because doing so might hamper their own efforts to effectively work on policy.\par \par \uc2 Government employees have been organizing against the war under other umbrellas as well. Staffers for Ceasefire, for example, put on a vigil for Gaza outside the White House in December.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Staffers for Ceasefire published a scathing statement in opposition to the efforts of senior White House officials to boost morale that has flagged as a result of opposition to the US\u8217\'20\'19s support of Israel. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile White House chief of staff Jeff Zients throws a morale-booster party for staff tonight, a child in Gaza is killed every 8 minutes,\u8221\'20\'1D Staffers for Ceasefire said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are disgusted by this display of complete apathy towards the lives that have been taken in the region over the last three months.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Van Jackson, a political scientist who worked in the Pentagon during the Barack Obama administration, said the recent protests from US public servants were unprecedented. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in uncharted territory, and no presidential administration the past 40 years has been denounced by its own staff like this \u8211\'20\'13 not collectively, not so publicly, and not with this regularity,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson wrote in his newsletter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.un-diplomatic.com/p/biden-staffers-mobilizing-non-violent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Un-Diplomatic}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But it is not clear whether the demonstrations are having an effect. Insiders say Biden himself is the decision-maker on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s Israel policy, and he does not seem swayed by dissenters.\par \par \uc2 The state department has been holding \u8220\'20\'1Copen forum\u8221\'20\'1D sessions for its employees that have become \u8220\'20\'1Cvery frank\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cquite heated\u8221\'20\'1D, according to internal department emails seen by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s action follows a string of public acts of dissent from inside the government. In early January, a senior political appointee from the education department, Tariq Habash, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/06/biden-administration-staff-gaza-policy-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned in protest}}}\uc2 . State department employees have used the department\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdissent channel\u8221\'20\'1D to convey policy disagreements directly to the secretary of state. More than a thousand officials for the development agency \uc2 USAid\uc2  signed a letter in support of a ceasefire. At Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 re-election headquarters, campaigners have also anonymously signed petitions.\par \par \uc2 Government employees say that even though their substantive criticisms of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy do not seem to be changing policy, the barrage of dissenting actions have reached the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is aware, and his entire senior team is aware. I just think that they\u8217\'20\'19re in a bubble,\u8221\'20\'1D said a Biden official affiliated with Staffers for Ceasefire. Dissent against Israel policy is \u8220\'20\'1Csomething that goes incredibly high up, no matter how much folks try to disregard that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240130ek1u002jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
