\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  found to have subjected 13 women to \u8216\'20\'18sexually hostile work environment\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in Washington \par \uc2 591 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 January 2024\par 18:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US DoJ reaches agreement with New York state executive chamber over workplace conduct of former governor, 66, who quit in 2021\par \par \uc2 The former New York governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  subjected at least 13 female government employees \u8220\'20\'1Cto a sexually hostile work environment\u8221\'20\'1D and retaliated against four who complained, a formal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/crt/media/1335301/dl?inline=&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreement}}}\uc2  between the state executive chamber and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-edny/pr/justice-department-secures-settlement-agreement-state-new-york-executive-chamber"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US justice department}}}\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Cuomo repeatedly subjected these female employees to unwelcome, non-consensual sexual contact; ogling; unwelcome sexual comments; gender-based nicknames; comments on their physical appearances; and/or preferential treatment based on their physical appearances,\u8221\'20\'1D read the agreement, which was released on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Cuomo, a Democrat and son of the former New York governor \uc2 Mario Cuomo\uc2 , rose to national prominence during the Covid pandemic in 2020 and was widely believed to hold presidential ambitions.\par \par \uc2 He denied accusations of sexual misconduct, but Cuomo resigned in August 2021 after the New York attorney general, Letitia James, said she found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/03/andrew-cuomo-new-york-governor-sexual-harassment-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11 such claims credible}}}\uc2 . He was replaced by his lieutenant, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now 66, Cuomo is fighting civil {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cityandstateny.com/politics/2023/09/women-who-accused-cuomo-harassment-fight-subpoenas-his-legal-team/390709/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuits}}}\uc2  from two accusers and, in the words of the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cslowly manoeuvring toward re-entering political life\u8221\'20\'1D. But, the paper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/26/nyregion/andrew-cuomo-justice-department-harassment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  on Friday, such \u8220\'20\'1Cefforts may be sharply compromised by the justice department findings\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The investigation by the federal civil rights division and the US attorney for the eastern district of New York opened in August 2021.\par \par \uc2 The settlement released on Friday said Cuomo \u8220\'20\'1Csubjected at least 13 female employees of New York state, including executive chamber employees, to a sexually hostile work environment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The executive chamber was aware of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s conduct but did not \u8220\'20\'1Ceffectively remediate the harassment on a systemic level\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen employees attempted to raise concerns about Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s conduct to his senior staff,\u8221\'20\'1D the agreement said, \u8220\'20\'1CCuomo\u8217\'20\'19s staff failed to follow equal employment opportunity policies and procedures to promptly report those allegations to the appropriate investigative body.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIndeed, the executive chamber\u8217\'20\'19s response was designed only to protect Cuomo from further accusations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The investigation \u8220\'20\'1Calso found that Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s senior staff were aware of his conduct and retaliated against four of the women he harassed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The agreement listed reforms to be implemented and some undertaken under Governor Hochul, beginning with the removal of employees held to have \u8220\'20\'1Cfacilitated Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s misconduct and/or engaged in unlawful retaliation against women who raised concerns\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Rita Glavin, a Cuomo lawyer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/26/nyregion/andrew-cuomo-justice-department-harassment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Times}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis is nothing more than a political settlement with no investigation. Governor Cuomo did not sexually harass anyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Kristen Clarke\uc2 , assistant attorney general in the civil rights division, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-edny/pr/justice-department-secures-settlement-agreement-state-new-york-executive-chamber"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CExecutive chamber employees deserve to work without fear of sexual harassment and harsh reprisal when they oppose that harassment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe conduct in the executive chamber under the former governor, the state\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful elected official, was especially egregious because of the stark power differential involved and the victims\u8217\'20\'19 lack of avenues to report and redress harassment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hochul said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe moment I took office, I knew I needed to root out the culture of harassment that had previously plagued the executive chamber and implement strong policies to promote a safe workplace for all employees, and [I] took immediate action to do so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Breon Peace, US attorney for the eastern district of New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-edny/pr/justice-department-secures-settlement-agreement-state-new-york-executive-chamber"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe appreciate the governor\u8217\'20\'19s stated determination to make sure that sexual harassment does not recur at the highest level of New York state government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240126ek1q003e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
