\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Boost for Biden as \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  endorses his re-election\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2024\par 11:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Both Biden and Trump had courted influential union. Plus, poll finds 35% of Americans say Israel is committing genocideDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW){\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/24/united-auto-workers-endorse-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally endorsed Joe Biden}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign on Wednesday at the union\u8217\'20\'19s national community action program conference in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Both Biden and the former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the New Hampshire primary this week}}}\uc2 , have courted the union and supported its successful strike action against the big three automakers last year. Biden became the first sitting president to walk a picket line in support of the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  bet on the American worker while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  blamed the American worker,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf our endorsement must be earned, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has earned it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a scab. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a billionaire and that\u8217\'20\'19s who he represents,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about who will stand up with us and who will stand in our way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How influential is the \uc2 UAW\uc2 ? It has 40,000 members. It is based in Detroit, Michigan, a key swing state where, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://redfieldandwiltonstrategies.com/latest-us-swing-states-voting-intention-28-30-december-2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one poll}}}\uc2  conducted at the end of 2023, Trump is edging out Biden 39% to 37%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How did Trump try\par \par \uc2 to court the union? In September, Trump said Fain was \u8220\'20\'1Ca good man \u8230\'20\'26 he\u8217\'20\'19s got to endorse Trump\u8221\'20\'1D. He also attacked electric vehicles and claimed, in office, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe will drill baby drill\u8221\'20\'1D and support gas engines.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did Biden tell the \uc2 UAW\uc2  conference? On Wednesday, Biden talked up his pro-labor credentials, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe union movement in America is important because it produces the best skilled workers in the world\u8221\'20\'1D. He added: \u8220\'20\'1CDuring my presidency, we opened 20 auto factories and more than 250,000 auto jobs all across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Poll finds 35% of Americans believe Israel is committing genocide against Palestinians\par \par \uc2 A poll from the Economist/\uc2 YouGov\uc2  found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/24/americans-believe-israel-committing-genocide-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 35% of Americans say Israel is committing genocide}}}\uc2  against Palestinians, with 36% saying it is not and 29% undecided. The figures were even higher when accounting for age and politics, with 49% of people aged 18-29, and 49% of Democrats, seeing Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions as genocide.\par \par \uc2 The polling, taken from 21 to 23 January, comes as the international court of justice (ICJ) prepares to deliver on Friday an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/24/icj-to-deliver-interim-ruling-on-genocide-case-against-israel-on-friday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interim ruling}}}\uc2  on South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s genocide case against Israel, and a separate lawsuit against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration for \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/13/biden-lawsuit-alleged-failure-prevent-genocide-israel-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failing}}}\uc2  to prevent genocide\u8221\'20\'1D advances.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the US state department was forced on Wednesday to \u8220\'20\'1Cdeplore\u8221\'20\'1D the attack on the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Khan Younis training centre, after the \uc2 UNRWA\uc2  building sheltering about 800 people was hit by Israeli tank shelling, killing at least 12 and injuring 75.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is the latest in Gaza? The Israeli army says it has \u8220\'20\'1Cencircled\u8221\'20\'1D the southern city of Khan Younis after two days of heavy fighting. The city is crowded with 88,000 residents and about 425,000 displaced people, with many trapped sheltering in hospitals. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone in Gaza is hungry,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 UN\uc2  secretary general said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How many Palestinians have been killed? More than 25,700, health officials in \uc2 Hamas\uc2 -run Gaza say, since the 7 October attack that saw 1,200 in Israel killed. About 85% of the 2.3 million people in Gaza have been displaced and face hunger and disease.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\par \par \uc2 is happening off the coast of Yemen? Two ships owned by \uc2 Maersk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US subsidiary sought US navy support after hearing explosions. Houthi militants are continuing their attacks on commercial shipping \u8211\'20\'13 which they say is in solidarity with Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 Russia accuses Kyiv of shooting down plane carrying Ukrainian prisoners of war\par \par \uc2 Russia has accused Kyiv of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/24/russian-plane-carrying-ukrainian-pows-has-crashed-moscow-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting down a large military transport plane}}}\uc2  carrying Ukrainian prisoners of war to an exchange on Wednesday, after a crash in the Belgorod region that killed everyone onboard.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has neither confirmed nor denied that it hit the plane but said Moscow had created a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeliberate threat to the life and safety\u8221\'20\'1D of its PoWs by failing to warn Kyiv to deconflict the airspace before the swap.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , called for full clarity over the crash, accusing Moscow of \u8220\'20\'1Cplaying with the lives of Ukrainian prisoners of war\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, fighting continues with 58 combat clashes on the frontlines, Ukrinform {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ukrinform.net/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . A drone attack on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea port of Odesa injured one person and started a fire, the regional governor said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What are the details of the crash? Russia says the Ilyushin Il-76 aircraft, which was filmed crashing and exploding, was carrying 65 Ukrainian PoWs, six crew and three Russian servicemen. Russia says all were killed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How is funding for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s war effort going? The UK defence secretary and Germany\u8217\'20\'19s finance minister have called on other countries to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/25/russia-ukraine-war-live-latest-news-updates-plance-crash-volodymyr-zelenskiy?page=with:block-65b1e8848f088600a74d29e9#block-65b1e8848f088600a74d29e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase funding}}}\uc2  to support Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has been the impact on Russia since its invasion? According to Ukrainian figures, Russia has suffered almost 380,000 killed or injured as the war enters its 701st day.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Argentinian demonstrators staged their largest show of opposition to far-right president Javier Milei\u8217\'20\'19s radical attempt to reshape the South American country, with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/24/argentina-strike-protest-javier-milei"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationwide strike}}}\uc2  and tens of thousands of marchers hitting the streets on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio was accused of inflicting \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat pain\u8221\'20\'1D as it blocked trans youth from receiving gender-affirming care, with the state senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/24/ohio-senate-trans-youth-health-care-sports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning a gubernatorial veto}}}\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The French parliament is debating plans to enshrine abortion as a constitutional right, with several parties {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/24/france-debates-plan-to-enshrine-abortion-as-constitutional-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing to protect}}}\uc2  the voluntary ending of pregnancies after Roe v Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s embattled chief executive said the company\u8217\'20\'19s planes\par \par \uc2 fly only when \u8220\'20\'1C100% confident\u8221\'20\'1D of safety, after a wheel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/jan/24/delta-air-lines-plane-nose-wheel-falls-off"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falling off}}}\uc2  a 757 passenger jet while awaiting takeoff added to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/jan/24/boeing-ceo-plane-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing\u8217\'20\'19s troubles}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Saudi Arabia will allow its first alcohol sales in 72 years, available in the capital\u8217\'20\'19s Diplomatic Quarter in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/25/saudi-arabia-to-allow-first-alcohol-sales-in-72-years-dividing-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teetotal kingdom}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: 8% annual drop in fossil fuel CO2 emissions helps EU produce lowest since early-1960s\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  pushed fossil fuel CO2 emissions down to their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/jan/24/eu-fossil-fuel-co2-emissions-hit-60-year-low"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowest level in 60 years}}}\uc2 , after pumping out 8% less in 2023 than 2022. That is according to an analysis from the Centre for Research on Energy and Clean Air (Crea). More than half of the drop in emissions came from the use of cleaner electricity, such as dams and nuclear power \u8211\'20\'13 and with record levels of solar panels and wind turbines built in 2023. The CO2 fall \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be celebrated\u8221\'20\'1D but \u8220\'20\'1Cmore must be done to wean the EU off fossil fuels\u8221\'20\'1D, said a Crea analyst, Isaac Levi.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this:\par \par \uc2 five women share their miscarriage stories\par \par \uc2 Up to one in five known pregnancies end in miscarriage, but despite its ubiquity, the experience is rarely discussed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/jan/24/pregnancy-miscarriage-stories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Ava Macha}}}\uc2 . A recent Guardian callout asked readers about having a miscarriage in the US. Almost all indicated that understanding the statistical frequency of miscarriages \u8211\'20\'13 they occur in 10%-20% of known pregnancies \u8211\'20\'13 did not lessen the trauma they felt iafterwards. We selected five of those testimonies \u8211\'20\'13 from women in Montana, Illinois, Washington, New Jersey and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 devastating Amazon drought worsened by climate crisis\par \par \uc2 The climate crisis turned the drought that struck the Amazon rainforest in 2023 into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/jan/24/devastating-drought-in-amazon-result-of-climate-crisis-study-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a devastating event}}}\uc2 , a study by the World Weather Attribution team found. Decreasing rainfall and increased heat in the Amazon made the drought about 30 times more likely than pre-industrial times. The drought was the worst recorded in many places and hit the maximum \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptional\u8221\'20\'1D level on the scientific scale. Without planet-warming emissions from the burning of oil, gas and coal, it would have been far less extreme, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Cute!\par \par \uc2 100 adorable photos taken by readers\par \par \uc2 From Hello Kitty toys to silly emojis, contemporary culture has fallen hard for all things adorable. A London exhibition opening today explores how cuteness has become such a dominant force. To celebrate the opening of Cute at Somerset House, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  asked readers to send in photos of the cutest thing they have ever seen \u8211\'20\'13 and the overwhelming majority seem to be animals. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/jan/25/the-eyes-have-it-100-of-the-worlds-cutest-photos-as-chosen-by-readers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Start your day with these 100 cute photos}}}\uc2 , from a baby brown bear to a fur seal to a donkey named Pop Tart.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240125ek1p001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
