\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  endorses \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for president\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 462 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2024\par 20:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  formally backs president\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign after both Biden and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  courted the powerful group\par \par \uc2 The powerful \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  formally endorsed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign on Wednesday at the union\u8217\'20\'19s national community action program conference in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Both the US president and rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 courted the union}}}\uc2  and supported its successful strike action against the US\u8217\'20\'19s big three automakers last year. Biden became the first president to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walk a picket line}}}\uc2  in support of the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  bet on the American worker while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  blamed the American worker,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain told the conference. \u8220\'20\'1CIf our endorsement must be earned, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has earned it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a scab. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a billionaire and that\u8217\'20\'19s who he represents,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about who will stand up with us and who will stand in our way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-kicks-off-national-cap-conference-in-washington-d-c-sets-political-legislative-agenda/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conference}}}\uc2  is where the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s delegates and leaders develop and shape the 40,000-strong union\u8217\'20\'19s political and legislative priorities. It is the union\u8217\'20\'19s first conference with Fain at the helm since he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/executive-board/shawn-fain/#:~:text=The%20membership%20elected%20Shawn%20Fain,President%20on%20March%2026%2C%202023."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected}}}\uc2  president of the union on a reform slate in March 2023.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the conference, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CI honest to God have always believed the union movement in America is important because it produces the best skilled workers in the world. It\u8217\'20\'19s good for everybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur plan is delivering for the American people, building an economy from the middle out and the bottom up, not the top down,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was in office, six auto factories closed around the country. Tens of thousands of auto jobs were lost nationwide during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency. During my presidency, we opened 20 auto factories and more than 250,000 auto jobs all across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fain has been strongly critical of Trump. This week he said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty much contrary to everything we stand for\u8221\'20\'1D. But the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has many Trump-supporting members and the union had held off on endorsing Biden.\par \par \uc2 Biden has repeatedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/statements/icymi-president-biden-im-most-pro-union-president-american-history-and-i-make-no"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touted}}}\uc2  himself as the most pro-labor president in history and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2  the picket line of striking \uc2 UAW\uc2  members during the \u8220\'20\'1Cstandup\u8221\'20\'1D strikes at the big three automakers in September, becoming the first sitting president to join a picket line.\par \par \uc2 Last week \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2 , announced he had met privately with Trump in a move that progressive members called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/18/teamsters-union-chief-trump-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a slap in the face}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden has also received the endorsements from the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest federation of unions in the US, and the \uc2 National Education Association\uc2 , which represents about 3 million educators, the largest union in the US.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240124ek1o003ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
