\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We want everybody walking out\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 UAW\uc2  chief outlines mass strike for May 2028\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 392 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2024\par 04:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain, the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president, reaffirms general strike on 1 May 2028, saying \u8216\'20\'18members need to come together\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain, the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president, criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Monday but declined to back \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he reaffirmed plans to lead a general strike in the US in 2028.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to union members at the \uc2 UAW\uc2  national political conference in Washington DC, Fain said it was time for union members to come together.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to pay for our sins of the past. Back in 1980 when Reagan at the time fired patco workers, everybody in this country should have stood up and walked the hell out,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe missed the opportunity then, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to miss it in 2028. That\u8217\'20\'19s the plan. We want a general strike. We want everybody walking out just like they do in other countries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He reaffirmed ambitious plans to organize a general strike for 1 May 2028, coinciding with International Solidarity Day or May Day.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-10-30/uaw-urges-all-unions-in-us-to-prepare-for-may-day-2028-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescheduled}}}\uc2  the expiration of their union contracts with the US\u8217\'20\'19s big three automakers to align on this day in the contracts it reached late last year and has been encouraging other labor unions to schedule contracts to expire on this day to maximize the participation from workers across different industries.\par \par \uc2 A general strike is a mass strike across various industries around similar demands or bargaining positions. In the US, they have been virtually non-existent in recent decades given the passage of the Taft-Hartley Act in 1947 that restricted secondary strikes and the decline of labor unions in the US since the 1970s.\par \par \uc2 After successfully taking on the US auto companies, Fain has emerged as a potent political figure, courted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  and Biden.\par \par \uc2 Fain also used his speech to criticize Trump, telling reporters that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cis as a person... pretty much contrary to everything we stand for\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has yet to formally endorse Biden, who was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first president}}}\uc2  to walk on a picket line with striking workers in September 2023. Fain told reporters the union will be holding formal discussions on an endorsement amid rumors that Biden may address the union in person later this week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240122ek1m003s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
