\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18There won\u8217\'20\'19t be any beer come March\u8217\'20\'19: US Anheuser-Busch workers threaten strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 904 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 January 2024\par 14:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Represented by \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , 5,000 workers at 12 breweries prepare to strike after voting 99% in favor\par \par \uc2 Workers who make Bud Light and other top-selling beers are threatening to strike in demand of significant wage increases, job security and improvements to retirement and benefits in the first big union contract battle of 2024.\par \par \uc2 Five thousand workers, represented by the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  at 12 \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  breweries in the US, are threatening to strike after voting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2023/12/by-99-teamsters-authorize-strike-at-anheuser-busch/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 99%}}}\uc2  in favor of a strike authorization last month. Their current union contract is set to expire on 29 February.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout a contract by February 29, there won\u8217\'20\'19t be any beer come March,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Teamsters/status/1744410783935545649"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters warned}}}\uc2  on X.\par \par \uc2 The contract fight is the first at \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/24/teamsters-president-sean-obrien-ups-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien}}}\uc2 , at the helm of the union. Elected in 2022, O\u8217\'20\'19Brien led the union in securing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/ups-teamsters-strike-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record contract gain}}}\uc2  at UPS last year amid threats of a massive strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executives can\u8217\'20\'19t get their act together to negotiate an agreement that respects workers, we will see them out on the streets,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said in a statement on the strike vote. According to the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , the union hasn\u8217\'20\'19t met with \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  since 16 November, when the company refused to negotiate on job security.\par \par \uc2 Anntonette Norris, who has worked at the \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  brewery in Jacksonville, Florida, for 25 years, said workers were due for a substantial wage increase in the new contract as wages have lagged behind inflation and price increases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I started, \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  was what you would consider the top dog, it was the job to have. The pay was great, but with inflation, we are not the top-paying job,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Norris said her brother had started working at \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  in the last five years. \u8220\'20\'1CThings that would have been easily attainable to me when I started, are not that for him now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Norris. \u8220\'20\'1CWith the increases of prices for everything, people are working numerous amounts of overtime to try to make up for the pay we don\u8217\'20\'19t have at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers face intense heat during summer weather and intense cold during the winter, said Norris. They sacrifice time away from families to work night shifts and handle dangerous, hi-tech equipment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a great product to enjoy out in the market, but it\u8217\'20\'19s a big sacrifice to make that product,\u8221\'20\'1D Norris added. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  wants to be No 1 in the beer industry, then they should want the No 1 group of employees working for them, who are proud to work for them and who are being compensated like it. We just want a fair and great contract that we feel that we are long overdue for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  brews some of the best-selling beer products on the US market, including Budweiser products, Michelob Ultra, Busch and Stella Artois, with US breweries in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/baldwinsville-ny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Baldwinsville,}}}\uc2  New York; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/cartersville-ga"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cartersville,}}}\uc2  Georgia; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/columbus-oh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbus,}}}\uc2  Ohio; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/fairfield-ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fairfield,}}}\uc2  California; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/fort-collins-co"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fort Collins,}}}\uc2  Colorado; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/houston-tx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Houston,}}}\uc2  Texas; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/jacksonville-fl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jacksonville,}}}\uc2  Florida; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/los-angeles-ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles,}}}\uc2  California; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/merrimack-nh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Merrimack,}}}\uc2  New Hampshire; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/newark-nj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Newark,}}}\uc2  New Jersey; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/st-louis-mo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 St. Louis,}}}\uc2  Missouri, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.anheuser-busch.com/breweries/williamsburg-va"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Williamsburg,}}}\uc2  Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Parent company \uc2 AB InBev\uc2  makes around a quarter of all beer drunk globally and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.macrotrends.net/stocks/charts/BUD/anheuser-busch/gross-profit#:~:text=Anheuser%2DBusch%20gross%20profit%20for%20the%20twelve%20months%20ending%20September,a%2014.53%25%20increase%20from%202020."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  profits of over $32bn in fiscal year 2023, a 1.97% increase from 2022. The increase came despite a slump in US sales following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/19/dylan-mulvaney-bud-light-boycott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative-driven boycott }}}\uc2  over a social media promotion with Dylan Mulvaney, a transgender influencer. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/brewer-anheuser-busch-inbev-posts-065906803.html#:~:text=(Reuters)%20%2DAnheuser%2DBusch,also%20paying%20down%20hefty%20debts."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a $1bn stock buyback program in October 2023 over the next year and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sports.yahoo.com/ufc-inks-multi-year-sponsorship-deal-with-anheuser-busch-worth-over-100m-180023337.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  a sponsorship campaign with the UFC in the same month valued at over $100m.\par \par \uc2 Angel Arroyo, 53, has worked at \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s brewery in Fort Collins, Colorado, for 20 years. He said that wages at the brewery had fallen behind compared with other businesses in the area.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwenty years ago, \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  was one of the top-paying businesses here in Colorado. Unfortunately, with the concessions we made throughout the years, a two-tier in medical benefits and slight wage increases, we really let Anheuser InBev get a stronghold on the work we\u8217\'20\'19ve accomplished,\u8221\'20\'1D said Arroyo. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re looking for job security. We\u8217\'20\'19re looking for the American Dream,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to share in our profits and we need to bring up the working class better than it was before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arroyo said the 99% strike authorization vote sent a message that workers are sticking together to demand what\u8217\'20\'19s due to them. The last contract reached in 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2019/01/b-contract-proposal-raises-wages-provides-4000-bonus-protects-benefits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 included }}}\uc2  only $2.50 in wage increases over five years and included higher medical benefit costs for new employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven our younger employees who aren\u8217\'20\'19t so well versed in unions are getting on board. They see what the future holds. They\u8217\'20\'19ve seen their parents struggle and I think now they\u8217\'20\'19re realizing that\u8217\'20\'19s not the life they want,\u8221\'20\'1D added Arroyo.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  said in response to the strike authorization vote and contract negotiations with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  is aware of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 strike authorization vote, which is common during labor negotiations. We have a long-standing track record of reaching agreements with organized labor and look forward to resuming negotiations to reach a mutually acceptable agreement that continues to recognize and reward our employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240117ek1h001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
