\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New York solar firm accused of union busting after furloughing staff\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 921 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 January 2024\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 EmPower Solar suspended 40% of its workforce but says action is unrelated to recent successful election of workers to join \uc2 UAW\par \par \uc2 A New York-based solar panel business has been accused of being a \u8220\'20\'1Cposter child\u8221\'20\'1D of union busting after furloughing 40% of its workforce for more than a year, days after a victorious union election.\par \par \uc2 Installers and technicians at EmPower Solar, in Bethpage \u8211\'20\'13 concerned about poor working conditions and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.longislandpress.com/2023/12/18/oped-why-the-renewable-energy-industry-needs-unionizing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issues}}}\uc2  they faced on the job \u8211\'20\'13 reached out to the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  after the gains it won during the \u8220\'20\'1Cstand up\u8221\'20\'1D strikes at the big three automakers.\par \par \uc2 Just before Christmas, on 22 December, workers at Empower voted to join UAW Local 259. The union fight overcame opposition from the company and consultants at National Labor Relations Advocates. NRLA specializes in union avoidance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nlradvocates.com/cost-of-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claiming }}}\uc2  a 96% success rate.\par \par \uc2 Barely a week after the vote, on 30 December, EmPower furloughed 21 workers until 2025. \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 256 claimed this amounted to a \u8220\'20\'1Cunion busting\u8221\'20\'1D tactic, designed to target workers for unionizing.\par \par \uc2 EmPower said the decision had \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing to do with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  or results of the union vote\u8221\'20\'1D, insisting it was \u8220\'20\'1Csolely due to a slowdown in business\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The union is due to hold a rally outside the company\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters on Saturday to protest against its actions.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Lozano, who started working as a solar installer at EmPower in April 2023, is one of the furloughed employees. He enjoys the job, but does not believe that he and other workers are compensated enough for the work they do, which includes inherent dangers in working on different types of roofs, especially through hot summer heat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re afraid of heights, it\u8217\'20\'19s not the job for you,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lozano, who was being paid $18.65 an hour, plus bonuses dependent on the number of solar panel installations he completed monthly. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want more for what we put in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union-organizing drive stemmed from Lozano and other workers wanting their concerns and voices to actually be heard by management, he added, and to not have to work under constant pressure to finish jobs and worry about high turnover rates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to be treated with respect,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the jobs of the future. If we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be working a lot of jobs with climate change and everyone needing solar, we need a livable wage and we need to know we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to get fired because they have high or low selling periods.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While on vacation during the December holiday break after the union election win, Lozano was notified he was to be furloughed. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do they need to make this such a big deal and be so arrogant? They\u8217\'20\'19re going to furlough us without giving the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and us a notice, doing all of these shady things.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can make this easy, sit down at the bargaining table and get this done. EmPower can and has the power to stop all of this right now, to accept the union, to sit down with us \u8211\'20\'13 and we can have a fair contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Just before the union election, EmPower {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/29-CB-332414"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  an unfair labor practice charge with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  against the union, alleging coercion. The union also filed unfair labor charges with the board against EmPower over the layoffs, and allegations of coercion and intimidation.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of its decision to furlough workers, EmPower had several job postings on its website, including for solar installers.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the company said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe decision to furlough had nothing to do with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  or results of the union vote. Demand for solar has gone down due to multiple macroeconomic factors, such as high interest rates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSimilar to many construction and all types of businesses, we have had to reduce workforce many times due to economic conditions. Inflation and rapidly rising interest rates have had a negative impact on demand for EmPower\u8217\'20\'19s products and services.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s crazy,\u8221\'20\'1D Michael DiGiuseppe, vice-president of \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 259, said of the move. \u8220\'20\'1CHow is that not union busting, a week after the election? We keep hearing about this just transition. I have two millionaires at a solar panel company that won\u8217\'20\'19t even talk to the union they just voted in, instead choosing to lay off 21 guys.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe should all be working together right now to make EmPower the best solar company in the world and a partnership between them and labor, setting an example for the new economy going forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 UAW Local 259 is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot going to stop\u8221\'20\'1D, DiGiuseppe said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going to be bullied. They could have been the standard bearers of what\u8217\'20\'19s good and what we want to do going forward. Instead, they\u8217\'20\'19re the poster child of union busting. They decided this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The conflict comes as labor unions and environmental groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://climatejusticealliance.org/just-transition/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push}}}\uc2  for a just transition to green energy. Only 4% of US solar workers are union members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were told the green economy had to be a race to the bottom, and there was nothing anyone could do about it,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president, Shawn Fain, said during a \uc2 US Senate{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/a700be36-df10-7e25-faa8-b9a5b29ac93d/Shawn%20Fain%20HELP%20testimony%20and%20bio.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2  last November. \u8220\'20\'1CBut \uc2 UAW\uc2  members rejected that false choice, that it can only be either green auto jobs or good auto jobs. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  just proved that it can and must be both.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240106ek16001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
