\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 UAW\uc2  wants to unionize \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . It faces a tough and high-profile battle with Musk\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,670 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 December 2023\par 21:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pro-union workers are hopeful but realistic \u8211\'20\'13 and fear Musk\u8217\'20\'19s previous ruthlessness towards workers trying to unionize\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and a powerful US union may clash next year in what could be a defining moment for both the embattled tech titan and an American labor movement seeking to flex its muscles fresh off a dramatic victory over Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s car makers.\par \par \uc2 The fight is shaping up as 2023 draws to a close \u8211\'20\'13 a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/us-unions-successes-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 great year}}}\uc2  for US unions and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/nov/30/can-elon-musk-stop-x-going-to-the-wall-after-tirade-at-advertisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complicated}}}\uc2  one for Musk.\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man has lit so many dumpster fires at X (n\u233\'00\'E9e \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ) that it is hard to see his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2023/nov/18/elon-musk-spacex-loses-contact-with-starship-rocket-after-second-launch-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/nov/30/tesla-cybertrucks-delivery-begins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accomplishments}}}\uc2  for the smoke. Meanwhile, the US\u8217\'20\'19s biggest unions have pulled off a series of victories that have burnished their reputation in ways Musk can only envy.\par \par \uc2 As the only US car manufacturer whose workers are not represented by a union, Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s most valuable car company, has long been a target of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After years of scandal and setbacks, the union has a new leader who has scored a major \u8211\'20\'13 and highly popular \u8211\'20\'13 victory after taking industrial action against the Big Three car companies: Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is seeking to continue that momentum by taking on non-union auto corporations, with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  an important target given its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kbb.com/car-news/tesla-ev-market-share-falls-to-50/#:~:text=Tesla%20maintained%20its%20giant%20lead,purchased%20in%20America%20last%20quarter."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dominant market role}}}\uc2  in the transition to electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is the richest man in the world, with a net worth of $230bn,\u8221\'20\'1D notes the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/join/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new organizing website}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CUS production has more than doubled since 2020, and \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sales are booming. The question is, will \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers get their fair share? It\u8217\'20\'19s time for \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers to Stand Up and fight for more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It looks to be a tough, and high-profile, battle. Inside \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , pro-union workers are hopeful but realistic. They fear Musk\u8217\'20\'19s previous ruthlessness towards workers trying to unionize and the slow, ineffective processes for enforcing US labor laws could hinder efforts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s so much disinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D said a pro-union \uc2 Tesla\uc2  worker at the company\u8217\'20\'19s Fremont, California, plant who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. A previous attempt to unionize ended with \u8220\'20\'1CElon firing everybody, and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be years of litigation\u8221\'20\'1D, they said.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing, but that\u8217\'20\'19s Elon, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about any of the workers here\par \par \uc2 Pro-union \uc2 Tesla\uc2  worker\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about that, he got them out of there. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a long time until they get their jobs back. It\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing, but that\u8217\'20\'19s Elon, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about any of the workers here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has attempted to unionize {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/cars/2016/05/19/united-auto-worker-uaw-tesla-motors/84585682/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tesla facilities before}}}\uc2 , most notably in 2016 in Fremont, at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfactory of the future\u8221\'20\'1D, a venue where hard-pressed workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2017/may/18/tesla-workers-factory-conditions-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had reported}}}\uc2  problems including fainting spells, seizures, abnormal breathing and chest pains.\par \par \uc2 As organizing took off, Musk seized on those complaints, pledging to have \u8220\'20\'1Cevery injury be reported directly to me, without exception\u8221\'20\'1D and promising to make safety his top priority. The union drive failed.\par \par \uc2 Since then Musk has changed, becoming seemingly ever more combative and mercurial. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has changed too \u8211\'20\'13 it became the world\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2020/jul/01/tesla-becomes-worlds-most-valuable-carmaker-without-making-a-profit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most valuable automaker}}}\uc2  in 2020 and started {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jan/26/tesla-elon-musk-profit-electric-car-deliveries-soar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generating profits}}}\uc2  after years of losses.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has also undergone a transformation. After a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/05/business/uaw-indictment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  corruption scandal}}}\uc2  involving the union\u8217\'20\'19s leaders resulted in numerous criminal charges in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/who-is-shawn-fain-uaw-strike-union-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shawn Fain}}}\uc2  won election as president in March 2023 on a reform ticket and has emerged as a potent force in US labor, courted by both Joe Biden and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his first big test as leader of the union, he helped the \uc2 UAW\uc2  secure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic gains}}}\uc2  in their contracts with the Big Three and won the backing of both likely presidential candidates at a time when opinion polls show that support for US unions has reached levels unseen since the 1960s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe approach of the union leadership to organizing has changed, and the change is overdue. The emphasis is on public communication and mobilizing workers at multiple firms. In the past they would focus on one non-union plant at a time; now they say they\u8217\'20\'19re focusing on all of them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ian Greer, the director of the Ithaca industrial and labor relations (IRL) co-lab and a research professor at \uc2 Cornell University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He explained that the non-union assembly industry has been an issue for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  since the 1980s, but emphasized the \uc2 UAW\uc2  under new leadership has changed their approach in how they talk about non-union workers as \u8220\'20\'1Cfuture union brothers and sisters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe agreements at the Detroit Three will make unionization more attractive to the unorganized in terms of potential economic gains than it was before,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see \uc2 Tesla\uc2  as very different from the other non-union automakers in these respects, but \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s belligerent public statements may be useful for organizers given the newfound sophistication of the union\u8217\'20\'19s communications.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The primary reason we see young people unionizing is they want to have a voice in their workplace\par \par \uc2 Cathy Creighton\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s previous efforts to unionize \uc2 Tesla\uc2  came up short after allegations of retaliation and union-busting that may indicate a battle plan for how \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is likely to fight the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest drive.\par \par \uc2 Among the workers to lose their jobs last time was union organizer Richard Ortiz, a worker at the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  plant in Fremont. A federal appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/31/business/tesla-union-musk-twitter.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld}}}\uc2  a ruling by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) in March 2023 that Ortiz was unlawfully terminated by \uc2 Tesla\uc2  in retaliation for union organizing and ordered his reinstatement. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is still appealing that decision. The court also upheld a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/apr/01/elon-musk-broke-law-with-threat-to-tesla-workers-stock-options-court-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ruling that}}}\uc2  Musk violated labor law by tweeting that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers would lose stock options if they unionized, ordering Musk to delete the tweet.\par \par \uc2 Jose Moran, another worker at the Fremont plant, wrote a public blog post detailing the grievances facing workers at the plant in 2017. Musk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2017/feb/11/elon-musk-in-union-spat-after-wrongly-calling-tesla-worker-a-paid-agitator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  falsely accused}}}\uc2  Moran of being a paid agitator for the union. Moran {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.industryweek.com/talent/article/22026401/tesla-worker-says-musk-summoned-him-to-meeting-ripped-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  Musk offered to remedy workers\u8217\'20\'19 safety complaints if workers refrained from unionizing.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, Dezzimond Vaughn, a worker at the Fremont plant, and his supervisor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2018/jun/13/tesla-workers-pay-price-elon-musk-failed-promises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told the Guardian}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  had changed his performance reviews to justify firing him for union activity. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  denied that the firing was retaliatory and claimed that unfair labor practice filings are an organizing tactic.\par \par \uc2 Crystal Guardado also claimed in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2018/jun/13/tesla-workers-pay-price-elon-musk-failed-promises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with the Guardian in 2018 that she had been fired by \uc2 Tesla\uc2  for being involved with the union drive under the guise of her testing positive for marijuana, though she said she had provided human resources with her medical marijuana documentation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe \uc2 Tesla\uc2  definitely needs a union,\u8221\'20\'1D Guardado told the Guardian in response to the renewed organizing drive, citing she has still heard of the same issues from workers at the plant, including unequal pay, favoritism and rampant retaliation.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has also faced allegations of firing workers in retaliation for union organizing in Buffalo, New York, as part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/tesla-workers-illegally-fired-for-unionizing-in-buffao-nlrb-complaint-2019-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  2019 United Steelworkers}}}\uc2  union drive and more recently in March 2023, a day after Workers United publicly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/feb/17/tesla-fires-workers-union-buffalo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a union drive at Buffalo\u8217\'20\'19s Gigafactory 2. The union is currently appealing a ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://buffalonews.com/news/local/business/nlrb-director-dismisses-claims-by-union-that-tesla-illegally-fired-workers/article_b58c901c-8d61-11ee-a07a-8fda2a6bafbc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismisses}}}\uc2  that claim but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=2ahUKEwjn-eGXhPaCAxWTkyYFHb_mDXEQFnoECA0QAw&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.shrm.org%2Fresourcesandtools%2Flegal-and-compliance%2Femployment-law%2Fpages%2Ftesla-union-drive.aspx%23%3A~%3Atext%3DTesla%2520said%2520the%2520firings%2520were%2Cthwart%2520support%2520for%2520the%2520union.&usg=AOvVaw0CjmbLyeaYJa7yedgqtip4&opi=89978449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found merit}}}\uc2  on two separate claims against \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response to the union drive.\par \par \uc2 In April 2023, an administrative judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/2023/4/27/23700463/tesla-nlrb-labor-violation-ruling-orlando-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  violated labor law by suppressing workers at a service center in Orlando, Florida, from discussing pay and bringing up working condition grievances.\par \par \uc2 There are currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/search/case/tesla?s[0]=Open"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 open unfair labor practice charges}}}\uc2  pending with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  involving \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , which has denied all previous allegations of retaliation.\par \par \uc2 Musk is already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/23/elon-musk-decries-strikes-as-swedish-workers-take-on-tesla"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 battling}}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/nov/21/tesla-sweden-unions-us-strikes-blockade-carmaker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far stronger}}}\uc2  labor forces in Sweden and has taken to X to attack them, calling their actions \u8220\'20\'1Cinsane\u8221\'20\'1D. The coming dispute will no doubt be fought out on X (although the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Fain seems to prefer \uc2 Facebook\uc2 ) but Musk\u8217\'20\'19s overarching attitude to unions is clear. Like union-bashers before him, Musk characterizes unions as adversaries and not as a collective voice for workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI disagree with the idea of unions \u8230\'20\'26 [because] I just don\u8217\'20\'19t like anything which creates a lords and peasants sort of thing,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk said at the New York Time\u8217\'20\'19s Dealbook conference last month. \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Tesla\uc2  gets unionized, it will be because we deserved it, and because we failed in some way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is likely to use the US\u8217\'20\'19s broken labor protections to try to stop the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , said Cathy Creighton, the director of Cornell\u8217\'20\'19s Buffalo IRL co-lab and a former field attorney for the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of our very weak labor laws in the US, it\u8217\'20\'19s very hard for workers to form a union in their workplace as evidenced by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s anti-union tactics,\u8221\'20\'1D said Creighton, who added that Musk is facing a tougher fight this time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe primary reason we see young people unionizing is they want to have a voice in their workplace. They don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be subjected to just whatever happens to them without any say,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWith a power discrepancy between a big employer and one particular lone voice of one worker, there\u8217\'20\'19s no way that worker can achieve any real gains without a collective voice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that people are understanding that, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why we have these very high rates of public support for unions, astonishingly high rates of support for the auto workers strike from the public. So, if I was \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and I wanted the status quo, I\u8217\'20\'19d be nervous that the status quo might be changing in the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231211ejcb001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
