\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We can\u8217\'20\'19t trust them\u8217\'20\'19: workers decry alleged union busting at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  air hub\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 974 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 November 2023\par 16:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees at facility in Kentucky allege \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is retaliating against them as they push for union representation\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s largest air hub in the world allege \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is retaliating against them as they try to organize their first union.\par \par \uc2 The workers at the 882-acre KCVG air hub in Hebron, Kentucky, have been organizing \u8220\'20\'1CMarch on the Boss\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AmazonUnionKCVG/status/1723186070760591761"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 actions}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facility in which staff confront managers en masse to \u8220\'20\'1Cdemand an end to union busting\u8221\'20\'1D, which they claim includes write-ups and other disciplinary actions against workers.\par \par \uc2 Workers at the facility are calling for a starting pay of $30 an hour, free on-site childcare, double pay for flex (overtime), professional translation and union representation.\par \par \uc2 More than 4,000 workers are employed at the Amazon KCVG air hub. Workers involved in organizing the union drive claim they were targeted after collecting union authorization cards to file with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Marcio Rodriguez, an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  worker for more than three years, joined the union organizing drive at KCVG in response to an experience at a nearby \uc2 Amazon\uc2  site where he said he was terminated when his visa expired. Despite having an extension, Rodriguez said, he was notified that he had lost his job. He only found out when he tried to clock in for work and his pass didn\u8217\'20\'19t work.\par \par \uc2 Rodriguez said \uc2 Amazon\uc2  managers deter workers from unionizing with claims that unions are businesses only interested in union dues and portraying signing union authorization cards as ceding rather than exercising rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve told workers a union is not a business; we\u8217\'20\'19re here to fight for each other to get better benefits, better pay and better working conditions, and that\u8217\'20\'19s really hit home for a lot of workers \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ve had over 1,000 workers sign union authorization cards,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rodriguez.\par \par \uc2 Unionizing efforts by workers at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  have been stymied since the first \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in the US won a union election in Staten Island, New York, in April 2022. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  filed objections to the election, which an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  regional director dismissed, a decision currently being appealed. Objections over \uc2 Amazon\uc2  union elections in Albany, New York, and the rerun union election in Bessemer, Alabama, are still awaiting decisions by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/amazon-anti-union-spending-2022_n_6426fd1fe4b02a8d518e7010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $14.2m}}}\uc2  on union avoidance consultants in 2022.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , 222 open or settled unfair labor practice charges as of September 2023 have been filed against \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in 25 states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to treat us like retail workers out there. I\u8217\'20\'19ve had multiple managers tell me this is no different than a fulfillment center, which is a complete lie. There is so much liability we have out there, and it is so easy to get hurt,\u8221\'20\'1D added Rodriguez.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have co-workers who are homeless and sleeping in the parking lot because inflation has gotten so high. They could pay us the $75m \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  spent on a support yacht. Each plane we push out there has over $100,000 in freight in it. So there\u8217\'20\'19s no reason the money isn\u8217\'20\'19t there, they just want to be greedy and keep it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union recently alleged that 12 workers involved in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AmazonUnionKCVG/status/1724831496437936227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizing }}}\uc2  for the Amazon Labor Union in the parking lot outside of work hours have received final written warning notices for doing so, placing them at risk of job termination.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said the warnings were for policy violations and denied they were related to any cause or group the workers support, claiming \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has policies to prevent blocking access to site.\par \par \uc2 Several unfair labor practice charges have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/search/case/amazon?r%5B0%5D=09&page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  by workers with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  at the air hub against \uc2 Amazon\uc2  this year related to the union organizing drive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve talked to so many people who have two or three other jobs, just because they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to make ends meet working at KCVG,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jordan Quinn, who has worked at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  for more than a year and one of the workers who recently received a final warning from \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt should be that one job is enough. \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have two different jobs. \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to clock in for 54- to 60-hour weeks, Bezos can be on his yacht in the Mediterranean enjoying the sunshine. I wish I could ever afford to go to the Mediterranean \u8211\'20\'13 you know, I can barely afford my rent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Quinn argued peak season pay bumps at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  have declined compared to recent years and that annual wages have been undercut by increases in insurance costs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Amazon\uc2  says that safety is a top priority \u8211\'20\'13 in reality, profit always really comes first, pushing out more volume always comes first,\u8221\'20\'1D added Quinn. \u8220\'20\'1CDespite all of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s corporate speak and their policies, they don\u8217\'20\'19t actually care about workers. What they put first is their profits and how much volume they\u8217\'20\'19re pushing out. And I think it honestly shows that we can\u8217\'20\'19t trust them to make things better. That\u8217\'20\'19s why we have to get organized and fight. We\u8217\'20\'19re the only ones who have each other\u8217\'20\'19s backs in there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1COur employees have the choice of whether or not to join a union. They always have. We favor opportunities for each person to be respected and valued as an individual, and to have their unique voice heard by working directly with our team. The fact is, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  already offers what many unions are requesting: industry-leading pay, health benefits on day one, and opportunities for career growth. We look forward to working directly with our team to continue making \uc2 Amazon\uc2  a great place to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231129ejbt001mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
