\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Legoland trying to deter ride techs\u8217\'20\'19 bid to unionize, workers say\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 973 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 November 2023\par 18:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: ride technician engineers in California say union avoidance consultants brought in after filing for union election\par \par \uc2 Lego play sets have captivated children and adults alike for decades, but engineers at Legoland California are dealing with blocks of a different kind: opposition from management and hired union avoidance consultants trying to deter their bid to formally unionize.\par \par \uc2 Ride technician engineers at Legoland in Carlsbad, California, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/21-RC-325975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  for a union election to join \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2  (IAMAW), District Lodge 947 in September. They await a ruling by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  on accepting their bargaining unit, and permitting the election to be scheduled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe big focal point they have is a complete and utter lack of fairness,\u8221\'20\'1D said William Corona, business representative and organizer with IAMAW, District Lodge 947. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we first got into the impact of what that meant with the workers, it got into extreme amounts of favoritism and nepotism. Some of these ride technicians are getting zero raises and it\u8217\'20\'19s based on who you know and how well you are with the supervisors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The engineers \u8220\'20\'1Cstood up and said \u8216\'20\'18enough is enough\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Corona added. \u8220\'20\'1CSigning a union authorization card and reaching out is already commendable and empowering alone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This action amounts to a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric presence\u8221\'20\'1D at the resort, according to Corona. \u8220\'20\'1COur future members there want fairness. They want to be recognized not just as a number, but as a person and Legoland is not doing that, and they haven\u8217\'20\'19t been doing that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Legoland California \u8211\'20\'13 the first Legoland theme park in the US \u8211\'20\'13 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fox5sandiego.com/entertainment/legoland-among-best-amusement-and-water-parks-in-the-world-tripadvisor/#:~:text=%E2%80%94%20Legoland%20California%20is%20being%20recognized,U.S.%2C%20but%20around%20the%20globe."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 often rated}}}\uc2  as one of the most popular amusement parks in the world. Opened in 1999, the park was acquired by \uc2 Merlin Entertainments\uc2  in 2004. The family of Kirk Kristiansen, who controls Lego, later led a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2019/jun/28/lego-consortium-buys-merlin-entertainments-theme-parks-for-59bn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u163\'00\'A35.9bn takeover of Merlin}}}\uc2  in 2019.\par \par \uc2 One worker at Legoland described lagging and low pay of workers in the ride engineering department, arbitrary and unfair disciplinary enforcement by supervisors, and a culture of favoritism fostered by managers and supervisors. This prompted workers to start organizing a union at the park, said the worker, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a lot of micromanaging, and our management doesn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily trust us to do our jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the lowest-paid park engineers in California at the moment, I believe. Compared to Disneyland, SeaWorld, Six Flags, Magic Mountain, we\u8217\'20\'19re one of the lowest, if not the lowest, in starting pay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They described how ride engineers perform preventative maintenance on rides, regular safety inspections and routine scheduled maintenance. The favoritism and micromanaging that workers complain about is often reflected in annual performance reviews, with supervisors arbitrarily deducting points toward that review for certain workers, or enforcing certain policies to add disciplinary points to a workers\u8217\'20\'19 review. This impacts any bonuses they might receive and promotions or pay increases.\par \par \uc2 Since management became aware of the union campaign, the worker said there has been an uneasy tension between management and workers. Union avoidance consultants have been brought in, they said, and have used regular one-on-one and group meetings to isolate and separate workers who push back on anti-union arguments and claims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the very beginning, they definitely made it seem like they were your friend trying to be on your side, like, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, you know, we\u8217\'20\'19re here to help you guys,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said, claiming that this attitude quickly veered into fearmongering about the union. \u8220\'20\'1CThey would give us one of the sheets that they were going over at the very bottom of that, it was saying, \u8216\'20\'18Do you want the union to have complete control over you?\u8217\'20\'19 in black bold letters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey emphasize that there\u8217\'20\'19s a big possibility the workplace might not get better, that Legoland could take things away, that our benefits will go down, without directly saying that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The opposition to unionization at Legoland is \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to say the union has an agenda, and that they don\u8217\'20\'19t\u8221\'20\'1D, the worker added. \u8220\'20\'1CBut they do, and the union at the end of the day isn\u8217\'20\'19t a separate body, it\u8217\'20\'19s us. We\u8217\'20\'19re not going to do something we don\u8217\'20\'19t agree upon or don\u8217\'20\'19t want.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Legoland\u8217\'20\'19s management {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/21-RC-325975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retained}}}\uc2  the law firm \uc2 Littler Mendelson\uc2 , the same union avoidance law firm used by \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://laborlab.us/laborlab-files-complaint-against-kv-information-consultants-for-deficient-lm-20-filings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaint}}}\uc2  was filed recently by the non-profit LaborLab against one of the union avoidance consultant firms hired by Legoland \u8211\'20\'13 KV Information \u8211\'20\'13 for not providing adequate information in filings with the federal government about their compensation and consultant activities related to their work for Legoland in response to this union campaign.\par \par \uc2 These actions in opposition to the union appear to contradict the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lego.com/cdn/cs/sustainability/assets/blt123637cf697b8687/1023787_LEGO_Responsible_Business_Principles_130618_FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lego Group\u8217\'20\'19s Responsible Business Principles}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers have the right to form or join trade unions and take part in union activity, select their own representatives and to bargain collectively without interference, obstruction, influence or sanctions from employers,\u8221\'20\'1D it states.\par \par \uc2 Kirkbi, the private investment company of Kristiansen\u8217\'20\'19s family, owns 75% of \uc2 Lego Group\uc2  and 47.5% of Merlin, which owns and operates Legoland parks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLegoland is a great place to work. The people that I work with are all great people, and I just feel like we deserve to be treated a lot better,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe play a very important role in the operation of the park and that role is really undermined.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t feel job qualification is that important to how we\u8217\'20\'19re being treated. Everyone does their job very well, but I just believe our management really needs to reevaluate themselves, fix their issues and how they treat the workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Legoland did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231128ejbs002h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
