\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  workers launch Black Friday strike in Washington state\b0\par\par\uc2 Victoria Bekiempis \par \uc2 619 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 November 2023\par 19:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 About 400 workers walk out in dispute over allegedly unfair labor practices and retail giant\u8217\'20\'19s failure to agree to a new contract\par \par \uc2 About four hundred \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  workers in Washington state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/22/macys-workers-strike-black-friday-thanksgiving"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began striking}}}\uc2  on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 known as Black Friday among retailers and one of the year\u8217\'20\'19s busiest shopping days \u8211\'20\'13 citing allegedly unfair labor practices and the retail giant\u8217\'20\'19s purported refusal to agree to a new contract.\par \par \uc2 The union representing the employees, \uc2 UFCW\uc2  3000, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UFCW_3000/status/1728041086848028982"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  workers started arriving about 3am on Friday to form picket lines. Workers are striking outside the Alderwood, Southcenter and Bellis Fair Macy\u8217\'20\'19s stores and plan to continue for three days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are on an unfair labor practice strike because \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  intimidated and retaliated against me for calling security and 911 about a thief,\u8221\'20\'1D one employee, Liisa Luick, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UFCW_3000/status/1728073443789218004"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  during a rally outside Southcenter. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  has not bargained in good faith throughout this process, frustrating our ability to get to a fair contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another protester, Azia Domingo, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UFCW_3000/status/1728073446121226515"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe need increased security to better protect workers and customers in our stores. We also want \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  to share some of the $1 billion/year in profits by raising our wages so we can care for our families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  is among the biggest retailers in the US, boasting hundreds of department stores, with its flagship in New York City {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.manhattanhoteltimessquare.com/attractions/shopping/macys-herald-square/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  to be among the largest in the world.\par \par \uc2 In October, 96% of workers voted in favor of a strike. The union has criticized \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  for refusing to budge on wage increases despite its flourishing finances and the $11m yearly pay package of its CEO, \uc2 Jeff Gennette\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  profits exceeded $1bn in 2021 and 2022, and it spent $600m on stock buybacks while paying $173m in shareholder dividends last year.\par \par \uc2 The union\u8217\'20\'19s most recent contract with \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  saw starting pay hover near Washington state\u8217\'20\'19s hourly minimum wage, which will reach $16.28 in January.\par \par \uc2 Asked for comment, \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CAt \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , we respect the rights of our colleagues. As always, our top priority is to ensure the safety of our colleagues and customers in-store. Our stores remain open to serve our valued customers as we continue to work through contract negotiations with the union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before the strike, it commented: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  seeks to reach a deal that is mutually beneficial to the colleague, company and union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The action comes as workers from \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s warehouse in Coventry in the UK were joined on Friday by union members from the US and Europe, as part of a global effort demanding better working conditions at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/nov/24/what-do-we-want-15-hundreds-join-amazon-picket-line-for-black-friday-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internet retail titan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jessie Moreno, an Amazon Teamsters member from California\u8217\'20\'19s Local 396, said that company workers, \u8220\'20\'1Care taking action around the globe to fight for the good jobs we deserve\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the US, my Teamster siblings and I are on strike against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unfair labor practices,\u8221\'20\'1D Moreno {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uniglobalunion.org/news/makeamazonpay2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe have taken our picket line across the country and now we\u8217\'20\'19re joining our colleagues from around the world to demand respect, fair wages, and a workplace where our health and safety are a priority. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is no match for the power of its workers united.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has defended itself against claims of unfair labor practices, saying the \u8220\'20\'1Cvast majority of these allegations are false or misinformed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has created millions of good jobs, while helping create and support hundreds of thousands of small businesses around the world. We offer great pay and benefits for our employees,\u8221\'20\'1D an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson, Mary Kate Paradis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/technology/4325609-amazon-workers-strike-black-friday/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Hill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231124ejbo00336\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\