\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What do we want? \u163\'00\'A315!\u8217\'20\'19 Hundreds join \uc2 Amazon\uc2  picket line for Black Friday strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Heather Stewart \par \uc2 888 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2023\par 13:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 54\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trade unionists from US and Europe stand with staff at Coventry hub over local pay dispute amid global day of action\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of strikers outside \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Coventry warehouse were joined on Black Friday by trade unionists from Europe and the US as part of a global campaign calling for better working conditions at the internet retailer.\par \par \uc2 Wearing orange beanie hats branded with the \uc2 GMB union\uc2  logo, activists from Germany, Italy and California, on strike at their respective \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workplaces, expressed solidarity with the Coventry strikers, who have taken 28 days of industrial action since January.\par \par \uc2 Gathered on a grassy roundabout close to the vast warehouse in the chilly early morning air, scores of the activists from the Make \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Pay campaign joined in chants of: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat do we want? \u163\'00\'A315! When do we want it? Now!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jessie Moreno, who delivers \uc2 Amazon\uc2  parcels from Palmdale, in the California desert, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t just a US fight, this is a global fight, so we are happy to come here to support our brothers and sisters at the GMB.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to spread the word and bring awareness,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe issues are the same, no matter where you are, no matter what country you\u8217\'20\'19re in \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s all the same.\u8221\'20\'1D Moreno described the challenges he faces at work of operating in high temperatures, to stringent targets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the living conditions, it\u8217\'20\'19s respect, and of course it\u8217\'20\'19s money. We\u8217\'20\'19re living in poverty conditions while the CEO, \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , gets richer and richer off our hard work, and we\u8217\'20\'19re just struggling to put food on the table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Organisers at the GMB in Coventry, where workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/16/amazon-workers-vote-strike-coventry-depot-uk-first"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first took strike action in January}}}\uc2 , say they have now signed up 1,200 members.\par \par \uc2 They made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/apr/26/amazon-workers-in-coventry-to-request-union-recognition-after-membership-doubles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a formal bid for union recognition}}}\uc2  to the independent Central Arbitration Committee (CAC) this year, believing they represented more than half of the workers in Coventry. They subsequently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jun/08/gmb-halts-bid-for-official-amazon-union-claiming-firm-skewed-staff-numbers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew the application}}}\uc2 , accusing \uc2 Amazon\uc2  of hiring up to 1,000 extra workers to \u8220\'20\'1Cbust the union\u8221\'20\'1D after the CAC was understood to confirm \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claim that there were 2,700 staff on site. They are now considering a fresh application.\par \par \uc2 Standing with campaigners, Alke B\u246\'00\'F6ssiger, the deputy general secretary of the UNI global union, which is one of the co-convenors the Make \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Pay campaign, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really important that people here know that they\u8217\'20\'19re not lonely in this fight. It\u8217\'20\'19s a long game, it\u8217\'20\'19s not that we can achieve something overnight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said 150 actions against \uc2 Amazon\uc2  were taking place in more than 30 countries on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the actions are strikes and some of them are protests \u8211\'20\'13 on environmental issues, for example,\u8221\'20\'1D B\u246\'00\'F6ssiger added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s such a big company and it has such a big global footprint.\u8221\'20\'1D She raised other issues including taxation, and claims of monopoly power.\par \par \uc2 The US regulator the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  is engaged in a lawsuit against the company, accusing it of anti-competitive practices \u8211\'20\'13 something \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has denied.\par \par \uc2 In Coventry, the GMB has focused on winning higher pay, with action first kicking off last summer, after workers were offered a 50p-an-hour rise. Since then, the basic rate of pay has increased several times, and will rise to \u163\'00\'A312.30 an hour. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  denies the increases have any link with the industrial action, insisting it reviews pay regularly and always has.\par \par \uc2 Kate Bell, the deputy general secretary of the TUC, praised the long-running campaign at Coventry, telling the workers: \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are the future of trade unionism in the UK. You\u8217\'20\'19re bringing people together and you\u8217\'20\'19re only getting stronger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rainer Raising, from Germany\u8217\'20\'19s ver.di union, who is usually based near Bremen, also joined the Coventry workers. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here to show solidarity,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of action going on in Germany today, with nine or 10 places on strike. We\u8217\'20\'19re asking for a decent living, and better conditions in the workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gianpaulo Meloni, from Piacenza in Italy, where workers are on strike on Friday, is the president of the European Works Council, which brings together \uc2 Amazon\uc2  union reps from across the continent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt my site, we are fighting against \uc2 Amazon\uc2  since they came to increase the wage by just 1.1%. We were very upset. We started with a mobilisation, and we did some strikes this year \u8211\'20\'13 and today and tomorrow we are going to be striking,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Coventry workers shared stories from the early days of the strike, when the GMB only represented a few dozen workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people were scared that if they started joining, they would end up losing their job \u8211\'20\'13 but I said, we can do better,\u8221\'20\'1D said one striker, Destiny Oebi. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a long journey \u8211\'20\'13 when the fire started, it was small, but it will get bigger and bigger, and it will be difficult to quench it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe offer competitive pay, comprehensive benefits, opportunities for career growth, all while working in a safe, modern, work environment. At \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , these benefits and opportunities come with the job, as does the ability to communicate directly with the leadership of the company.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231124ejbo001me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
