\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Tesla\uc2  may have picked an unwinnable fight with Sweden\u8217\'20\'19s powerful unions\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Gelin \par \uc2 1,028 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 November 2023\par 10:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The first ever strikes and a solidarity blockade against the US carmaker could force it to rethink its entire anti-union model\par \par \uc2 For the first time anywhere in the world, workers for the US carmaker \uc2 Tesla\uc2  have gone on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/07/world/europe/sweden-tesla-strike.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike.}}}\uc2  It\u8217\'20\'19s not a coincidence that this strike is happening in Sweden, which has one of the strongest labour movements in Europe. More than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lo.se/start/nyheter/svenska_kollektivavtal_ska_galla_i_sverige_aven_pa_tesla#:~:text=I%20Sverige%20har%20%C3%B6ver%2090,ocks%C3%A5%20Tesla%20anpassa%20sig%20till"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 90% of workers}}}\uc2  are protected by collective bargaining agreements, and the system has strong backing among employees and employers alike. With good reason: the Swedish labour relations model has sustained relative industrial peace between wage-earners and corporations for decades.\par \par \uc2 By refusing to play ball, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s car giant may have picked an unwinnable fight. What started as a minor local disagreement has grown to the point that it could have global implications, with potential ripple effects for labour movements and auto workers across Europe and the US.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t manufacture cars in Sweden, but it does operate workshops to service its cars. The dispute began when a group of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/tesla-faces-pressure-sweden-workers-supplier-strike-2023-11-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 130 disgruntled mechanics}}}\uc2  had their request for a collective bargaining agreement rejected. As is customary in Sweden, unions in other sectors came out in solidarity. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wired.co.uk/article/sweden-tesla-strike-cleaners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dockworkers}}}\uc2 , mail and delivery workers, cleaners and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/sweden-tesla-union-strike-eae1d9b10c7bca2d9bd416f7d19db412"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 car painters}}}\uc2  have so far all agreed to refuse to work with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  products. Stockholm\u8217\'20\'19s largest taxi company has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newrepublic.com/article/176757/elon-musk-vs-swedens-working-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopped buying new Tesla cars}}}\uc2  for its fleet. Their fight against \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s anti-union business model could now spread to Germany, where \uc2 Tesla\uc2  runs factories and has a significantly larger workforce. The powerful German union \uc2 IG Metall\uc2  has said that it is ready to launch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/5d9jvn/tesla-strike-europe-elon-musk-uaw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collective bargaining negotiations}}}\uc2  if the workers demand it.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and other US corporations have certainly misjudged the situation if they expect special treatment in Sweden. Much about Swedish society has changed in the past few decades, but strong support for collective bargaining agreements is still considered the backbone of the country\u8217\'20\'19s economic model.\par \par \uc2 Minimum wage rates and benefits are generally not regulated by law, but in negotiations between unions and employers in each sector. It has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.socialeurope.eu/us-electric-car-maker-faces-swedish-union-shock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mostly worked }}}\uc2  well: Sweden has fewer strikes than its Nordic neighbours. This is because the unions are so strong they only need to call for industrial action as a last resort. Despite the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/14/swedish-parties-agree-coalition-with-backing-of-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rightwing government}}}\uc2  currently in power in Sweden, calls to change the employment model are rare.\par \par \uc2 Foreign and domestic tech giants have tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arbetsvarlden.se/tech-companies-disrupt-the-swedish-model/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenge the system}}}\uc2 , but these attempts are now more likely to backfire. The financial tech company \uc2 Klarna\uc2  recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://techcrunch.com/2023/11/03/fintech-klarna-reaches-agreement-with-workers-planned-strike-called-off/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had to give way}}}\uc2  after several years of attempting to resist collective bargaining agreements, and settled with employees in a victory for white-collar unions. There is increasing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sverigesradio.se/artikel/trade-unions-vow-to-keep-talking-with-spotify-on-collective-bargaining-agreement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressure on Spotify}}}\uc2  to do the same.\par \par \uc2 Instead of importing the US\u8217\'20\'19s lax labour standards to Sweden, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  may end up jeopardising its own business model. In the US, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has been involved in a number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/31/business/tesla-union-musk-twitter.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scandals }}}\uc2  over the past decade, with allegations relating to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasobserver.org/tesla-elon-texas-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  workplace safety,}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jul/01/tesla-hit-by-new-lawsuit-alleging-racial-abuse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  racial discrimination}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/alanohnsman/2021/12/14/tesla-hit-by-6-more-sexual-harassment-claims/?sh=228fbc965def"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexual harassment, }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/tesla-broke-us-labor-law-by-silencing-workers-official-rules-2023-04-26/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labour violations }}}\uc2  and unlawful practices to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/board-rules-workplace-policies-limiting-wearing-union-insignia-including"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 curb unionisation efforts.}}}\par \par \uc2 Corporations used to get away with such behaviours, but increasingly successful strikes and labour organising this year suggest that the power balance is shifting. 2023 has been a year of high-profile strikes and labour union victories in the US. Despite decades of supreme court rulings that make it harder to form unions, and conservative state governments enacting so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/issues/right-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right-to-work laws}}}\uc2  (an Orwellian euphemism for suppressing labour organising), there now seems to be real momentum, with support for unions at record highs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/pdf/union2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fewer than 10%}}}\uc2  of US private sector workers are unionised, but 67% now support unions, up from only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/510281/unions-strengthening.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 48% in 2009}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Hollywood actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike organised by the Sag-Aftra union lasted 118 days, making it the longest strike in the guild\u8217\'20\'19s history. It ended with significant victories including big increases in salaries, benefits and pensions, as well as a framework for AI guardrails for actors. More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/healthcare-pharmaceuticals/kaiser-healthcare-workers-ratify-new-contract-2023-11-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than 75,000 workers }}}\uc2  for the healthcare giant \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  also participated in a US-wide strike, resulting in pay rises of more than 21% for workers.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  organised strikes at the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig three\u8221\'20\'1D car companies \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 in Michigan this summer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/americans-side-with-striking-uaw/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three-quarters of Americans}}}\uc2  said they supported it. Joe Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed up}}}\uc2 , having {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2023/09/04/remarks-by-president-biden-celebrating-labor-day-and-honoring-americas-workers-and-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called himself}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most pro-union president in American history\u8221\'20\'1D. Characteristic hyperbole perhaps, but Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration has accomplished quite a lot for labour unions in the past three years, especially compared to the dismal record of other recent presidents. (\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also showed up in Michigan, but gave a speech at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 non-unionised car parts maker,}}}\uc2  which was equally characteristic of his signature working-class cosplay without policy substance.)\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike resulted in big concessions from the carmakers, who agreed to 20-30% pay increases for workers. For Musk, there are reasons to worry that his business model could be challenged, as the fight in Sweden reverberates with the strengthening power of labour organisers across American unions. The average worker for the big three US carmakers now makes significantly more money, and has better benefits, than a \uc2 Tesla\uc2  worker, which could make it easier for \uc2 UAW\uc2  to organise workers at \uc2 Tesla\uc2  factories across the US as well.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.di.se/nyheter/tesla-anstallda-i-tyskland-flockas-till-facket/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  interview,}}}\uc2  Susanna Gideonsson, who heads the Swedish trade union federation fighting \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , sounded remarkably confident. \u8220\'20\'1CThis will end with the employees winning a collective bargaining agreement, one way or another,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. And if they don\u8217\'20\'19t? \u8220\'20\'1CThen \uc2 Tesla\uc2  can leave the country.\u8221\'20\'1D If she is right, this could be a tremendous symbolic victory, which would strengthen the tailwinds for union movements on both sides of the Atlantic.\par \par \uc2 In facing off with its Swedish mechanics, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  seems to have underestimated the sheer force of the union movement behind them. In classic David v Goliath fashion, the mechanics took on the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, but the momentum is now with them.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Martin Gelin writes for the Swedish newspaper Dagens Nyheter\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231121ejbl000xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
