\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Mars to buy \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 ; \u8216\'20\'18too early\u8217\'20\'19 to consider UK interest rate cuts; US jobless claims rise \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Graeme Wearden \par \uc2 5,600 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2023\par 15:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mars to swallow \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 , and \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Megan Greene says fall in inflation is \u8216\'20\'18good news\u8217\'20\'19, but it\u8217\'20\'19s too early to think about cutting borrowing costs\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 Time to wrap up\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Upmarket chocolates maker \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  has agreed to a \u163\'00\'A3534m takeover by the US food company Mars at a near 170% premium to the UK firm\u8217\'20\'19s market value.\par \par \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s founders will share a \u163\'00\'A3280m payday once the deal is completed.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/hotel-chocolat-founders-mars-takeover-angus-thirlwell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hotel Chocolat founders to land \u163\'00\'A3280m after it agrees \u163\'00\'A3534m Mars takeover}}}\par \par \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  policymaker Megan Greene has insisted it is too early to think about cutting interest rates, despite UK inflation falling to 4.6% yesterday.\par \par \uc2 But the City is now expecting rate cuts by next May, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65562bbf8f08d1d922ef80fe#block-65562bbf8f08d1d922ef80fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Goldman Sachs suggesting the first cut could come as soon as February 2024}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6556073e8f08d1d922ef7ec1#block-6556073e8f08d1d922ef7ec1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The pound hit a six-month low against the euro today}}}\uc2 , as traders calculated that UK interest rates have probably peaked.\par \par \uc2 The maker of Mr Kipling cakes, Angel Delight and Bisto gravy granules has announced price cuts on some of its ranges on the back of a fall in the rate of inflation on associated production costs.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/mr-kipling-super-noodles-cuts-prices-cost-inflation-premier-foods"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr Kipling and Super Noodles maker cuts prices as cost inflation falls}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 train drivers\u8217\'20\'19 union, Aslef\uc2 , will stage a series of one-day strikes and call an overtime ban across England\u8217\'20\'19s operating companies at the start of December, causing more disruption,\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/rail-strikes-aslef-december-rmt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rail strikes: Aslef announces industrial action in December}}}\par \par \uc2 One in three people in the UK had problems with the most recent delivery of a parcel to them, Citizens Advice research has shown, with Evri and Yodel named as the worst courier companies.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/uk-parcel-delivery-problems-citizens-advice-evri-yodel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One in three people in UK had problem with last parcel delivery, research shows}}}\par \par \uc2 Large parts of the Port Talbot steelworks will be closed or mothballed for years, and would leave the plant and its few remaining workers reliant on imported steel, according to proposals under consideration by the owner, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/tata"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tata}}}\uc2  Steel.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/port-talbot-steelworks-tata-steel-cuts-llanwern"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Large parts of Port Talbot steelworks could be shut under Tata Steel cuts plan}}}\par \par \uc2 Energy bills in Great Britain are expected to rise by 5% from January, with analysts predicting that the government\u8217\'20\'19s price cap could increase to about \u163\'00\'A31,930 a year for a typical gas and electricity bill.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2023/nov/16/energy-bills-great-britain-rise-january-cap-gas-prices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Energy bills in Great Britain \u8216\'20\'18to rise by 5% from January as cap hits \u163\'00\'A31,930\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 The government will offer significantly higher subsidies for new offshore windfarms after crisis talks with developers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/15/sse-to-increase-clean-energy-investment-after-profits-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that are battling cost inflation across global energy supply chains}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/nov/16/uk-to-offer-higher-subsidies-for-offshore-windfarms-after-crisis-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK to offer higher subsidies for offshore windfarms after crisis talks}}}\par \par \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  has launched a bonus scheme worth up to \u163\'00\'A3500 a worker in an attempt to meet delivery targets over Christmas, as its owner\u8217\'20\'19s losses more than doubled in the first half of the financial year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/royal-mail-christmas-bonus-losses-universal-service-obligation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Royal Mail launches Christmas punctuality bonus as losses soar}}}\par \par \uc2 South East Water\uc2  is to be investigated by the industry watchdog over possible failures in maintaining the supply to households.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/south-east-water-investigation-supply-failures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South East Water under investigation over supply failures}}}\par \par \uc2 In the US, the number of people filing new jobless claims {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65561a3f8f08945e7e4d0449#block-65561a3f8f08945e7e4d0449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has risen}}}\uc2 , while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-655627398f08d1d922ef80c5#block-655627398f08d1d922ef80c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 industrial production dropped last month}}}\uc2  amid strikes at major carmakers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 HMV to reopen Oxford Street store next week\par \par \uc2 HMV will be returning to its original home on Oxford Street next week.\par \par \uc2 The retailer originally opened on 363 Oxford Street in 1921 and will be reopening its doors on Friday, November 24, after a four-year absence.\par \par \uc2 Back in 1921, the Guardian reported on the same HMV store, owned by the Gramophone Company, being officially opened by Edward Elgar.\par \par \uc2 Our story said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe [Elgar] recommended the modern gramophone with its superior technical accomplishment to the \u8220\'20\'1Cwild and virulent piano playing\u8221\'20\'1D so painfully popular in the suburbs.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Before its closure four years ago, the hmv website says the Oxford Street store was seen as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunity hub for music fans with performances and signings from global artists such as The Weeknd, Kylie Minogue, The Spice Girls, Blur and more, with the latter performing an iconic rooftop gig at the shop in 1995.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  could start cutting UK interest rates as early as February, says \uc2 Goldman Sachs\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  has suggested that the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  could start cutting interest rates as soon as February, if the UK economy weakens.\par \par \uc2 In a note to clients, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  suggested that if the UK economy suffered a worse-than-expected slowdown in the coming months then the Bank\u8217\'20\'19s Monetary Policy Committee would start cutting interest rates at either the February or March 2024 meeting.\par \par \uc2 Goldman says the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://publishing.gs.com/content/research/en/reports/2023/11/02/6c17a15c-7b8c-4999-8d4b-76f01cf24f31.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MPC}}}\uc2  is very likely to hold Bank Rate again at the December meeting.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street bank also predicts the MPC is most likely to stay on hold until making its first cut in the third quarter of next year.\par \par \uc2 But it added:\par \par \uc2 That said, earlier cuts are possible if the economy turns out weaker than expected, putting our probability-weighted path for Bank Rate slightly below market pricing for the end of 2024.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US industrial production drops amid auto strike disruption\par \par \uc2 US industrial production declined 0.6% in October, new data shows, as strikes at major carmakers hit the sector.\par \par \uc2 Output of motor vehicles and parts fell by 10% last month, according to the latest survey from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That shows the impact of the walkout by workers at the Detroit Three automakers, in a strike organised by the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/uaw-reaches-deal-with-gm-ends-coordinated-strikes-against-detroit-automakers-2023-10-30/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The UAW reached deals with GM}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/ford-uaw-negotiators-reach-labor-deal-cnbc-2023-10-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with Ford}}}\uc2  and also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/business-67254006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with Stellantis}}}\uc2 , at the end of October,\par \par \uc2 Economists had expected a smaller, 0.4%, drop in industrial production last month.\par \par \uc2 enltrIndustrial Production turns negative YoY\par \par \uc2 In Oct manufacturing output, which accounts for 78% of total production, dropped 0.7% vs 0.3% drop est. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LfpGig277m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LfpGig277m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ophir Gottlieb (@OphirGottlieb) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OphirGottlieb/status/1725158088913596715?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  department store in Doral, Florida. Photograph: Wilfredo Lee/AP\par \par \uc2 Unlike \uc2 Walmart\uc2  ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-655614388f08945e7e4d03ee#block-655614388f08945e7e4d03ee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see earlier post}}}\uc2  ), shares in department store chain \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  are sharply higher after it beats Wall Street expectations today.\par \par \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  has upgraded its forecast for earnings this year to between $2.88 and $3.13 per share, up from previous guidance of $2.70-$3.20/shares.\par \par \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  also reported a 7% drop in sales for the third quarter of 2023, compared with a year earlier, a smaller drop than expected.\par \par \uc2 Profit margins for merchandise rose, due to lower permanent markdowns within the \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  brand.\par \par \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  stock is up 12% in premarket trading.\par \par \uc2 CEO \uc2 Jeff Gennette\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 We delivered better-than-expected top and bottom line third quarter results and are entering the holiday period in a healthy inventory position.\par \par \uc2 Our portfolio of nameplates are leading gift-giving destinations across the value spectrum offering exclusive products. We have refined our gift assortment, simplified our promotions and improved our shopping experience.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US jobless claims rise\par \par \uc2 Just in: More Americans filed new claims for unemployment support last week, which may indicate a weakening jobs market.\par \par \uc2 There were 231,000 \u8216\'20\'18initial claims\u8217\'20\'19 for jobless support filed in the week to November 11, an increase of 13,000 from the previous seven days.\par \par \uc2 Initial jobless claims have been extremely low in recent years, so this may be a sign that the labor market is normalising.\par \par \uc2 enltrUnited States Initial Jobless Claims {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7p2FYAmZ3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7p2FYAmZ3d}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WEerQCjLN6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WEerQCjLN6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TRADING ECONOMICS (@tEconomics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tEconomics/status/1725146774296240364?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The number of \u8216\'20\'18continuing claims\u8217\'20\'19 (people claiming unemployment support for at least two weeks) has also risen, up 32,000 to 1,865,000 in the week to November 4th.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the highest since November 2021.\par \par \uc2 enltr2 year high on continuing jobless claims\par \par \uc2 Thats the sound of the mandate slowly switching {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wwmUKTQDEN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wwmUKTQDEN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TheHappyHawaiian (@ThHappyHawaiian) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThHappyHawaiian/status/1725146564081893866?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Back in the UK, housebuilder \uc2 Crest Nicholson\uc2  has signalled it could start cutting jobs soon as a slowdown in the construction sector hit its business.\par \par \uc2 The company said that it would \u8220\'20\'1Calign headcount\u8221\'20\'1D in its divisions to their \u8220\'20\'1Cexpected level of output\u8221\'20\'1D in the next financial year.\par \par \uc2 The announcement follows a trading update in August which warned that Crest would have to start reducing its overhead costs.\par \par \uc2 Chief executive \uc2 Peter Truscott\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the challenging trading backdrop we have experienced this year, the group has acted decisively in streamlining its operations to align our cost base with the operating environment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are difficult decisions to take but will ensure the group is well positioned to recover strongly as more supportive market conditions return.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would like to thank all \uc2 Crest Nicholson\uc2  colleagues for their efforts this year and their professionalism in dealing with the changes we have made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rivals such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/10/housebuilder-persimmon-cuts-jobs-drop-demand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Persimmon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/mar/02/taylor-wimpey-plans-job-cuts-amid-downturn-in-uk-housing-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Wimpey}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/09/bellway-cuts-jobs-in-anticipation-of-uk-property-market-slowdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bellway}}}\uc2  have all cut jobs this year too.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  warns consumer health is weakening\par \par \uc2 Over in the US, shopping giant \uc2 Walmart\uc2  has warned that consumer spending has weakened this autumn.\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Walmart\uc2  have dropped over 5% in pre-market trading, after it struck a cautious tone with its outlook after reporting financial results today.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNBC, chief financial officer \uc2 John David Rainey\uc2  said consumers are \u8220\'20\'1Cleaning heavily\u8221\'20\'1D into major promotions as they watch their spending and search for deals.\par \par \uc2 Customers are holding out for lower prices, meaning \uc2 Walmart\uc2  has seen a drop in purchases before and after a sales event.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur events have been strong,\u8221\'20\'1D Rainey said, adding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been pleased with those. Halloween was good overall. But in the in the last couple of weeks of October, there were certainly some trends in the business that made us pause and kind of rethink the health of the consumer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWALMART CFO: "Halloween was good overall. But in the last couple of weeks of October, there were certainly some trends in the business that made us pause and kind of rethink the health of the consumer." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNBC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24WMT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $WMT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/melissa_repko?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @melissa_repko}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wJysHsg7bj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/wJysHsg7bj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carl Quintanilla (@carlquintanilla) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/carlquintanilla/status/1725129756666998964?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Data yesterday showed a small drop in US retail spending in October.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Young\u8217\'20\'19s to buy rival City Pub Group for \u163\'00\'A3162m\par \par \uc2 In another takeover deal today, Young\u8217\'20\'19s has agreed a \u163\'00\'A3162m deal to buy London-based rival City Pub Group.\par \par \uc2 The move will bring a further 50 pubs into the Young\u8217\'20\'19s business, taking its total estate to 279 pubs and bolstering its position as one of the biggest operators in London and the South East.\par \par \uc2 It comes against a challenging backdrop for pubs and the wider hospitality sector, amid pressure from higher borrowing costs and tighter customer budgets.\par \par \uc2 Young\u8217\'20\'19s has said it will seek to benefit from \u8220\'20\'1Csynergies\u8221\'20\'1D as part of the deal, particularly linked to overlapping jobs across the two firms.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pound hits six-month low against euro\par \par \uc2 In the currency markets, the pound has hit its lowest level against the euro since May, as traders anticipate cuts in UK interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Despite Megan Greene\u8217\'20\'19s insistance that it\u8217\'20\'19s too early to consider cuts, sterling is down 0.3% against the euro today at \u8364\'20\'AC1.142.\par \par \uc2 The pound earlier fell as low as \u8364\'20\'AC1.1396, its weakest level since May 4th.\par \par \uc2 That highlights that yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s drop in UK inflation, to 4.6% from 6.7%, has helped cement expectations that rates have peaked.\par \par \uc2 Jim Reid, strategist at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 , says the inflation report \u8220\'20\'1Csaw investors grow in confidence that the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  was finished hiking rates, with only a 11% likelihood of a further hike now priced in\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The fact {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?page=with:block-6555c9e38f08d1d922ef7b91#block-6555c9e38f08d1d922ef7b91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mars is willing to pay a 170% premium for Hotel Chocolat\u8217\'20\'19s shares}}}\uc2  is remarkable on two accounts, says \uc2 AJ Bell\uc2  investment director \uc2 Russ Mould\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 First, bid premiums are typically in the 25% to 50% range so Mars paying so much more would suggest it has taken a long-term view of what the business is worth.\par \par \uc2 Second, it suggests that Mars has spotted an opportunity and there is no way it wants to waste time with a low-ball bid. This looks like going in with its best offer with the hope of wrapping up the transaction as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMars doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to worry about sales of its eponymous chocolate bar, but it does have to think about the evolution of the business and tapping into parts of the market who are looking for a higher quality product.\par \par \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  ticks the right boxes and while its international expansion strategy hasn\u8217\'20\'19t gone to plan, perhaps Mars thinks it has the necessary skills to make a good job of turning the UK chocolatier into a global name. It is hard to imagine shareholders turning down such a generous offer.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mr Kipling maker plans price cuts as cost inflation eases\par \par \uc2 Mr Kipling and Ambrosia maker \uc2 Premier Foods\uc2  has said it will start reducing prices across some of its products after seeing a drop in cost pressures.\par \par \uc2 Premier Foods\uc2  told the City this morning that its imput cost inflation has slowed, meaning it can pass this onto consumers.\par \par \uc2 Alex Whitehouse\uc2 , chief executive officer at \uc2 Premier Foods\uc2 , says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know how challenging the past year has been for many consumers and so it\u8217\'20\'19s good to see the rate of input cost inflation falling.\par \par \uc2 This has now given us the opportunity to lower promotional prices across a number of our major branded products such as Batchelors Super Noodles and Mr Kipling Slices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This means a cup of Super Noodles \u8211\'20\'13 a popular student snack \u8211\'20\'13 will cost less than a pound again, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.standard.co.uk/business/super-noodle-ps1-price-premier-foods-mr-kipling-students-bisto-gravy-oxo-stock-cubes-ambrosia-b1120774.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Evening Standard says}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Food ingredients, and energy costs, surged after the invasion of Ukraine in March 2022. But global food prices have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dw.com/en/global-food-prices-fall-to-2-year-low-says-fao/a-66758166"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since fallen back to a two-year low}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Premier Foods\uc2  has also reported a 17.7% increase in revenues in the first half of the financial year, to 30 September, with pre-tax profits up 38%.\par \par \uc2 Trading profits rose 19%, with profit margins in line with prior year, the company added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?page=with:block-6555c9e38f08d1d922ef7b91#block-6555c9e38f08d1d922ef7b91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mars\u8217\'20\'19s takeover of Hotel Chocolat}}}\uc2  is likely to add to concerns about an exodus from the London stock market, says Susannah Streeter, head of money and markets at \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Streeter says:\par \par \uc2 The Mars owner clearly sees \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  as an appetising addition to its shelf of confectionery brands, providing an upmarket option to sit alongside Snickers, Twix, M&Ms and the ubiquitous Mars bar.\par \par \uc2 The price being paid is at a hefty premium to the share price at the close of trading yesterday but given the weakness of the pound would have helped fuel hunger for the acquisition. \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  has a loyal customer base of cocoa lovers, helped by its tasting club and its strategic locations across the travel network.\par \par \uc2 Although the company posted two profit warnings earlier this year, the recent update has been more encouraging, showing a turnaround bearing fruit, with stronger sales particularly at its new shops. International expansion however has proved super tricky for \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 , with its Japanese joint venture forced through insolvency.\par \par \uc2 The clout of the Mars operation, should help ensure \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s future ventures are far slicker, and the company clearly sees great opportunity for the brand\u8217\'20\'19s expansion into other markets, particularly in the airport retail sector.\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Although \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares are still up 160%, near to Mars\u8217\'20\'19s offer, the wider stock market is more subdued.\par \par \uc2 Britain\u8217\'20\'19s blue-chip FTSE 100 index is down 40 points, or 0.55%, at 7446 points, after three days of gains, while the FTSE 250 index of medium-sized companies is down 08.%.\par \par \uc2 Kyle Rodda, senior market analyst at Capital.com, says markets have been hit by US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  calling Chinese president Xi Jinping a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator\u8221\'20\'1D at a press conference today.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/16/joe-biden-xi-jinping-meeting-california-apec-seven-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden meets Xi Jinping in California: seven key takeaways}}}\par \par \uc2 Rodda explains:\par \par \uc2 Risk assets were already on the back foot in Asian trade. However, the comments gave the market an extra nudge in the bearish direction, as the tone of what had otherwise been a constructive visit to the US by the Chinese President soured. The White House hasn\u8217\'20\'19t publicly retracted the comments or clarified yet. Whatever the outcome, it\u8217\'20\'19s a stark reminder that geopolitical risks are never too far away from being a volatility driver in this market.\par \par \uc2 Futures are implying a soft open for the markets tonight, as Wall Street looks poised to take a breather following a ripping run through November. US jobless claims are released and expected to show a slight uptick in the number of Americans seeking unemployment benefits. At the same time, industrial production and the Philly Fed Manufacturing Index is tipped to decline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mortgage lenders slashed more fixed rates to sub-5% this week\par \par \uc2 A string of UK lenders have cut their mortgage rates this week, as the financial markets have concluded that \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  interest rates are now at their peak.\par \par \uc2 Data provider Moneyfacts reports that Halifax, \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , \uc2 Yorkshire Building Society\uc2 , Virgin Money, Bank of Ireland UK and Bank of Ireland UK for Intermediaries have all revealed new sub-5% two-year fixed mortgages this week.\par \par \uc2 There are now 27 lenders offering a sub 5% fixed mortgage, Moneyfacts reports, up from 13 at the start of October.\par \par \uc2 At the start of November only \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  was offering two-year fixed mortgages priced below 5%, with no lenders offering this at the start of October.\par \par \uc2 Rachel Springall, finance expert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://moneyfactscompare.co.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moneyfactscompare.co.uk}}}\uc2 , says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s encouraging to see cheaper mortgages on the market for borrowers, particularly the return of two-year fixed mortgages priced below 5%. This is great news for those who do not want to commit to a longer-term fixed deal. Several large lenders have slashed fixed mortgage rates and there is much anticipation for more cuts in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 As we head ever closer to the year-end, lenders will be weighing up both the current competition and their own lending targets, so it\u8217\'20\'19s a promising market for consumers looking for a new deal.\par \par \uc2 enltrExpect light trims before Christmas followed by a tentative cut next year, but restyling rates won\u8217\'20\'19t kick in till there is inner confidence in taming inflation. Expectation; post election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kEfpkRIs51"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kEfpkRIs51}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emma Fildes (@emmafildes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/emmafildes/status/1725061659088048563?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/nov/16/mars-hotel-chocolat-burberry-luxury-spending-slowdown-business-live?page=with:block-6555c9e38f08d1d922ef7b91#block-6555c9e38f08d1d922ef7b91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\u8217\'20\'19s swoon into the hands of chocolate giant Mars}}}\uc2  comes seven years after it floated on the London stock market.\par \par \uc2 That float, at 148p per share, valued the company at \u163\'00\'A3167m, with founders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2015/apr/02/hotel-chocolat-boss-easter-angus-thirlwell-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angus Thirlwell}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Peter Harris\uc2  recieving \u163\'00\'A320m each in 2016.\par \par \uc2 At the time, Thirlwell insisted that \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone who knows me knows that I am not really motivated by money\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He and Harris each still own 27% of the company, so will pick up another \u163\'00\'A3144m each through the sale to Mars.\par \par \uc2 Although Mars is paying a chunky premium of 170% to last night\u8217\'20\'19s share price, today\u8217\'20\'19s takeover offer is still below the peak of \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s value in 2021 (when shares hit 540p, valuing the firm at \u163\'00\'A3740m).\par \par \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s share price Photograph: Refinitiv\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 EY\uc2  picks Janet Truncale as the first woman to lead a Big Four firm\par \par \uc2 In the accountancy world, \uc2 EY\uc2  has become the first Big Four firm to appoint a woman as chief executive.\par \par \uc2 Janet Truncale, currently the head of \uc2 EY\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s financial services business in the Americas, will replace Carmine Di Sibio, who is retiring in June.\par \par \uc2 Partners were informed of the move yesterday in an email, in which Di Sibio said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTruncale is an exceptional leader, with a strong foundation in serving clients across all \uc2 EY\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s businesses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Truncale\u8217\'20\'19s appointment comes just months after \uc2 EY\uc2  scrapped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/may/27/ey-plans-to-spin-off-audit-business-in-shake-up-for-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  its planned breakup}}}\uc2 , which included a plan for the company to spin off its consulting business and much of its tax practice into a stand-alone public company.\par \par \uc2 The FT says Truncale beat early favourites including the British partner \uc2 Andy Baldwin\uc2 , who helped craft the spin-off plan, and Jad Shimaly, who runs \uc2 EY\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business in Canada.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Megan Greene then warned that global investors have not fully grasped the message that central bank interest rates may have to stay at restrictive levels for some time.\par \par \uc2 BoE\uc2  policymaker Greene told Bloomberg TV that there had been structural changes in major economies over recent years that pointed to a need for higher interest rates.\par \par \uc2 She says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think markets globally haven\u8217\'20\'19t really clocked onto this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Investors are expecting several cuts to UK interest rates next year, bringing them down to 4.5% by the end of 2024, down from 5.25% today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s another clip from Megan Greene\u8217\'20\'19s interview this morning:\par \par \uc2 enltrRecent UK economic data on inflation and the labor market is "good news," says new \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  rate-setter Megan Greene\par \par \uc2 But she identifies some "reasons to worry" about the persistence of UK inflation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kJ5epHpsrN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kJ5epHpsrN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SUvoriirYE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SUvoriirYE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bloomberg TV (@BloombergTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BloombergTV/status/1725086998149333014?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 BoE\uc2 's Greene: Too early to think about interest rate cuts\par \par \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  policymaker Megan Greene has hailed yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s fall in inflation to 4.8% as \u8216\'20\'18good news\u8217\'20\'19, but warned that it\u8217\'20\'19s too early to consider cutting interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on Bloomberg TV, Greene \u8211\'20\'13 a member of the Monetary Policy Committee \u8211\'20\'13 said that UK wage growth was still \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly high\u8221\'20\'1D, and that there are reasons to worry about the persistence of inflation in the UK.\par \par \uc2 She says:\par \par \uc2 The recent data is good news.\par \par \uc2 Inflation came down pretty significantly, in both headline and core, but the biggest contributor was energy.\par \par \uc2 Greene is one of three MPC members who wanted to raise UK interest rates to 5.5% last month, but were outvoted by the other three committee members.\par \par \uc2 She says the Bank\u8217\'20\'19s current monetary stance is restrictive, but the question is whether it is restrictive enough to bring inflation down to the 2% target.\par \par \uc2 She says she is not thinking about cutting interest rates at the moment, adding \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think that\u8217\'20\'19s where we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The money market, through, are anticipating a rate cut, down to 5%, by next May.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Fran, I'm not thinking about cuts at the moment"\par \par \uc2 New Bank of England official Megan Greene responds to market speculation about rate cuts in 2024, telling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/flacqua?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @flacqua}}}\uc2  : "I don't think that's where we are right now" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DWgBoW3oyo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DWgBoW3oyo}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WqhRZKMYao"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WqhRZKMYao}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bloomberg UK (@BloombergUK) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BloombergUK/status/1725089459715063822?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s inflation rate fell from 6.7% to 4.6%, down more than half from its peak last autumn. Wages are rising faster, with total pay up 7.9%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/15/uk-inflation-drops-gas-electricity-prices-interest-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK inflation drops sharply to 4.6% as energy prices fall}}}\par \par \uc2 Greene argues that bringing inflation down from 10% to 5% is easier than the journey from 5% to 2%.\par \par \uc2 October\u8217\'20\'19s inflation data included the drop in energy prices last month, after \uc2 Ofgem\uc2  lowered the price cap. That means energy disinflation has now largely come through in the data, so the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  will be relying on goods and services inflation slowing, she explains.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ofgem\uc2  launches review of standing charges\par \par \uc2 In the energy sector, regulator \uc2 Ofgem\uc2  has launched a review into the \u8216\'20\'18standing charges\u8217\'20\'19 levied on customers by suppliers.\par \par \uc2 Standing charges cover cost such as maintaining the energy supply network and taking meter readings, and also support help schemes for people that cannot afford energy, and environmental schemes.\par \par \uc2 But they are controversial, as customers pay them regardless of how much, or little, energy they use.\par \par \uc2 Peter Smith of fuel poverty charity \uc2 National Energy Action\uc2  (NEA), says the system needs overhauling.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18For years, there has been growing alarm about increases to standing charges. Many people rightly feel they are now too high and the current approach is unfair.\par \par \uc2 How can it be right that someone who can\u8217\'20\'19t afford any energy for their home, still pays a daily charge that is the same or more than someone in a mansion? An overhaul of the system is long overdue.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Rail strikes: \uc2 Aslef\uc2  announces industrial action in December\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 train drivers\u8217\'20\'19 union, Aslef\uc2 , will stage a series of one-day strikes and call an overtime ban across England\u8217\'20\'19s operating companies at the start of December, ratcheting up the national rail dispute again.\par \par \uc2 Drivers at each company will strike for 24 hours on dates between Saturday 2 and Friday 8 December, and will refuse to work overtime between Friday 1 and Saturday 9 December, causing more disruption for operators that rely on rest day working.\par \par \uc2 The move comes days after the \uc2 RMT union\uc2  and employers signalled a possible breakthrough, with an agreement on pay to be ratified in a members\u8217\'20\'19 vote.\par \par \uc2 The fresh strikes appear to have been partly provoked by remarks made by the transport secretary, Mark Harper, at a select committee hearing on Wednesday, which the union described as \u8220\'20\'1Cdisingenuous\u8221\'20\'1D. Harper said \uc2 Aslef\uc2  should put an offer rejected as \u8220\'20\'1Crisible\u8221\'20\'1D by the union in April to drivers. The union said the offer was no longer on the table and had in effect been rejected in further votes for strikes.\par \par \uc2 More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/rail-strikes-aslef-december-rmt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/nov/16/rail-strikes-aslef-december-rmt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rail strikes: Aslef announces industrial action in December}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Analyst: the shine is dimming on the luxury sector\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s warning that it could miss its revenue target shows that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe shine is dimming on the luxury sector as even higher end consumers tighten their belts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 So explains \uc2 Sophie Lund-Yates\uc2 , lead equity analyst at \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown\uc2 , who adds:\par \par \uc2 Heralded as a more resilient corner of the economy, suggestions of missing targets and lower-end profits aren\u8217\'20\'19t what investors have come to expect and that has consequences for valuations. Specifically for \uc2 Burberry\uc2 , it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a basket of other brands or products to help diversify risk in this scenario.\par \par \uc2 The work the group\u8217\'20\'19s done to become a more premium luxury house is to be commended and will improve strength in the long-term, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no getting away from the fact that particularly aspirational, younger shoppers are thinking twice before swiping their cards. There could be further pressure to come before things improve, especially if a broader pull back in spending comes through in 2024 after the glut of festive trading.\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s decision to halt VAT refunds is denting demand in the important UK market, Lund-Yates adds:\par \par \uc2 The scheme was an important pull to encourage tourist spending and this revenue-cow now has no more to give. The wider European region is seeing an increase in tourist spending overall which is the shift \uc2 Burberry\uc2  wanted to see \u8211\'20\'13 American and Asian tourists splashing the cash while taking in Europe\u8217\'20\'19s sights is a cornerstone of the business model.\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2  has done pretty much all it can to place itself in a better position, both operationally and creatively. The issue is that while it\u8217\'20\'19s a slicker and bolder beast, \uc2 Burberry\uc2  is currently residing in a hostile environment outside of its control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/apr/24/brexit-drag-on-growth-burberry-chair-vat-gerry-murphy-rishi-sunak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brexit is a drag on growth, says Burberry chair, as he attacks \u8216\'20\'18own goal\u8217\'20\'19 on VAT}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 The huge, 170%, premium which Mars is prepared to pay for \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  suggests the stock market had rather undervalued the business.\par \par \uc2 Retail analyst Nick Bubb says Mars\u8217\'20\'19s move is a \u8216\'20\'18shock takeover\u8217\'20\'19, explaining:\par \par \uc2 Well, \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  has had its problems recently, not least with its Overseas expansion, but even so the disconnect between financial market valuations and takeover valuations shows through in the huge premium that Mars has been willing to pay for the business\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  shares surge 164% towards takeover offer\par \par \uc2 Boom! \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares have surged by 164% this morning.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve jumped from 139p to 369p in early trading, to just below Mars\u8217\'20\'19s offer of 375p in cash.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 Ouch. Shares in \uc2 Burberry\uc2  have tumbled almost 10% in early trading, to the bottom of the FTSE 100 leaderboard.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2  hit by slowdown in luxury spending A Burberry store in Beijing, China. Photograph: Tingshu Wang/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Another UK brand, \uc2 Burberry\uc2 , has been hit by a slowdown in luxury spending.\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2  told shareholders this morning that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe slowdown in luxury demand globally\u8221\'20\'1D is having an impact on current trading.\par \par \uc2 If the weaker demand continues, \uc2 Burberry\uc2  says it is unlikely to achieve its revenue guidance for the 2024 financial year, and operating profits would only come in towards the lower end of the current consensus range (\u163\'00\'A3552m-\u163\'00\'A3668m).\par \par \uc2 Jonathan Akeroyd\uc2 , \uc2 Burberry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief executive officer, says:\par \par \uc2 We made good progress against our strategic goals, executing our priorities at pace. We continued to build momentum around our new creative vision with the launch of our Winter 23 collection in September, the first designed by \uc2 Daniel Lee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While the macroeconomic environment has become more challenging recently, we are confident in our strategy to realise our potential as the modern British luxury brand, and we remain committed to achieving our medium and long-term targets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2  has reported a 4% rise in revenues in the six months to the end of September (the first half of its financial year) but a 15% drop in operating profits.\par \par \uc2 It says sales in mainland China increased 15% in the half, but fell 8% in the second quarter (July-September) \u8220\'20\'1Cas spending shifted offshore\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sales in the Americas fell by 9% in the half \u8211\'20\'13 a sign that US consumers may be cutting back.\par \par \uc2 Burberry\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 While the American customer has remained weak overall, we are pleased with the progress made with our customer acquisition programme with an increased share of higher income female clients.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Introduction: Mars to buy \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  in \u163\'00\'A3534m deal\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 UK chocolatier \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  has agreed to be taken over by food giant Mars in a \u163\'00\'A3534m deal.\par \par \uc2 The takeover, announced to the stock market this morning, will help \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  expand internationally, the companies say.\par \par \uc2 And Mars is paying a steep premium to get its prize. It will pay 375p per \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  share, a hefty 170% premium to last night\u8217\'20\'19s closing price of 139p.\par \par \uc2 Mars, which employs around 10,000 people in the UK, says the deal will bring a \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch-loved brand into its portfolio\u8221\'20\'1D and deepen its relationships with consumers.\par \par \uc2 It adds:\par \par \uc2 The UK has been an important market for Mars, and it expects this to be complemented by the acquisition of \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 , with its distinctive capabilities in product development, luxury gifting and immersive brand experiences.\par \par \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s directors say the offer is fair and reasonable, and are recommending shareholders back it (the directors hold about 54% of the stock).\par \par \uc2 A chocolate mixing machine at the \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  factory in Huntingdon, Cambridgeshire. Photograph: Antonio Zazueta Olmos/Antonio Olmos\par \par \uc2 Angus Thirlwell\uc2 , chief executive officer of \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2 , argues that teaming up with Mars makes sense for his company.\par \par \uc2 Thirlwell says:\par \par \uc2 We know our brand resonates with consumers overseas, but operational supply chain challenges have held us back. By partnering with Mars, we can grow our international presence much more quickly using their skills, expertise and capabilities.\par \par \uc2 The pillars on which we have built the \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  brand - originality, authenticity and ethical trading, is precisely what brought \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  and Mars together and our intention is to strengthen and invest behind these. I\u8217\'20\'19m excited about the future of the business and in Mars we have found an excellent long-term steward of the \uc2 Hotel Chocolat\uc2  brand and everything we stand for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The agenda\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9.30am BST: Latest realtime economic data on UK economy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm BST: US weekly jobless figures\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2.15pm BST: US industrial production stats for October\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3.45pm BST: \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  deputy governor \uc2 Dave Ramsden\uc2  speaks at the 7th Annual Conference of the \uc2 European Systemic Risk Board\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18Financial stability challenges ahead: emerging risks and regulation\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231116ejbg00133\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
