\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Bernie Sanders: US should back union movement \u8216\'20\'18to save the middle class\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,189 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 November 2023\par 15:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 24\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats and Republicans must back the movement together, senator says ahead of Senate hearing with labor leaders\par \par \uc2 If the US is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to save the middle class\u8221\'20\'1D then Democrats and Republicans must come together to back the newly resurgent labor movement, Bernie Sanders told the Guardian this week ahead of a Senate hearing on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/sep/15/bernie-sanders-uaw-auto-workers-strike-detroit-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 benefits of unions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sanders is holding a Senate health, education, labor and pensions committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/hearings/standing-up-against-corporate-greed-how-unions-are-improving-the-lives-of-working-families"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2  on Tuesday with US labor leaders on the state of the US labor movement and efforts to rein in corporate greed in America.\par \par \uc2 The hearing comes after a wave of successful strike actions by workers and as Congress once again considers legislation that would empower union organizing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have got to expand union organizing in this country if we\u8217\'20\'19re going to save the middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders. \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people are sick and tired of corporate greed, of record-breaking profits, outrageous compensation packages for CEOs while workers in many cases are earning starvation wages. That dynamic has got to change. I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen real, real progress in the last year,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 Two labor leaders who recently spearheaded successful strike actions \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, and the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president, \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 will be in attendance along with \uc2 Sara Nelson\uc2 , president of the Association of Flight Attendants-Communication Workers of America (\uc2 AFA\uc2 -\uc2 CWA\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 At the hearing, entitled, \u8220\'20\'1CStanding Up Against Corporate Greed: How Unions are Improving the Lives of Working Families\u8221\'20\'1D, the union leaders will discuss the role of labor unions in fighting corporate greed, recent historic union contract gains and the challenges and obstacles that continue to stymie workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to organize unions and engage in collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 Sanders, chair of the Senate help committee, sees this as a hopeful time for workers, citing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cios-shuler-state-unions-strong-record-public-support-unprecedented-activism-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record public support}}}\uc2  for unions. This revitalization should be seen in the context of growing wealth inequality, said Sanders, and a middle and working class that has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/social-trends/2015/12/09/1-the-hollowing-of-the-american-middle-class/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hollowed out}}}\uc2  over the past few decades in America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the weekly wage for the average American worker, despite the huge increase in technology and worker productivity, is actually lower than it was 50 years ago, back in 1973. Unbelievable. So what we have seen for 50 years is workers and the middle class falling deeper and deeper into economic despair. People are working incredible hours, in many cases, they\u8217\'20\'19re going nowhere in a hurry,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 We have got to expand union organizing in this country if we\u8217\'20\'19re going to save the middle class\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders\par \par \uc2 Sanders pointed to data on the widening economic divide in the US: 60% of American workers live paycheck to paycheck, millions of Americans, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/millions-of-americans-nearing-retirement-age-no-savings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about half}}}\uc2  of all Americans between the ages of 55 to 66 years old, have no retirement savings. Meanwhile, workers continue to struggle with unaffordable healthcare and childcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring all this time, the very richest people in America are becoming richer, we have more income and wealth inequality than we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever had in the history of this country. You\u8217\'20\'19re seeing CEOs now making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/ceo-pay-in-2021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost 400 times}}}\uc2  more than workers,\u8221\'20\'1D added Sanders.\par \par \uc2 Unions can use collective bargaining to negotiate decent wages and benefits, and collective action such as strikes to pressure powerful corporations to start to counter these harrowing economic trends through contract gains, said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 The hearing comes in the wake of successful strikes by the \uc2 UAW\uc2  led to auto workers reaching agreements with the big three US automakers, Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2 . Workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  25% wage gains over the life of the new contracts and reclaimed concessions made in previous contracts such as cost of living adjustments and the ending of lower-tier wage scales. The contract wins at GM were more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/GM2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 twice}}}\uc2  the value of what the company had offered before the strikes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/Ford2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50% }}}\uc2  more than what Ford offered before the strikes, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/stellantis2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 103%}}}\uc2  more than what \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  had offered before the strikes.\par \par \uc2 Following the contract agreements, Hyundai, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/business/story/2023-11-12/honda-will-give-autoworkers-11-raise-after-uaws-big-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Honda}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/toyota-hiking-wage-us-factory-workers-after-uaw-labor-deals-2023-11-01/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Toyota}}}\uc2 , announced wage increases for non-union auto workers in the US. Fain, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, plans to ramp up union organizing efforts at non-union automakers in the US. The wage increases have been hailed as a testament to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unions-and-well-being/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ripple effects}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 where wins for unionized workers spread to other workers and their communities.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2023/07/weve-changed-the-game-teamsters-win-historic-ups-contract/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celebrated}}}\uc2  a historic contract won at UPS this past summer after ramping up threats for what would have been one of the largest strikes in US modern history. Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s writers and actors also used their unions to strike and force media companies to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/10/contract-for-hollywood-actors-includes-40m-yearly-in-streaming-bonuses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 renegotiate better terms}}}\uc2  as the industry faces huge technological changes.\par \par \uc2 But despite these big wins and upticks in organizing, the US labor movement is still facing significant obstacles from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/26/amazon-trader-joes-starbucks-anti-union-measures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggressive opposition}}}\uc2  from corporations like Amazon and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  to union organizing and outdated and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nelp.org/publication/broken-laws-unprotected-workers-violations-of-employment-and-labor-laws-in-americas-cities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  broken labor law}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden has called himself the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-union president you\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen\u8221\'20\'1D and has backed legislation that Sanders and others hope will further boost the labor movement. But that legislation has stalled in a divided Congress.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/11/us-workers-unionization-nlrb-level-playing-field"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro Act}}}\uc2  (Protect the Right to Organize Act) first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jwj.org/legislative-history-of-the-pro-act#:~:text=The%20PRO%20Act%20benefits%20workers%20by%3A&text=Prohibiting%20employers%20from%20holding%20mandatory,who%20engage%20in%20union%20activities."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  in 2021 is a comprehensive labor law reform bill that Sanders said he would like to see passed into law to help workers whose organizing efforts are currently behind, stymied by employers under current labor laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we have got to do in Congress is pass legislation like the Pro Act which allows workers to exercise their constitutional right to form a union,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said, noting the Senate health, education, labor and pension committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/teamsters-commend-us-senate-help-committee-for-passing-pro-act-301861086.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  the bill earlier this year in an 11-10 vote along partisan lines.\par \par \uc2 Since then, some Republicans, including the likely presidential nominee, Donald Trump, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vance.senate.gov/press-releases/senator-vance-visits-uaw-picket-line-in-toledo-ohio/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 , have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thrown their weight}}}\uc2  behind striking workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to see that bill on the floor and I want to see it pass, but I want Republicans who are going to vote against it to explain to American workers why they don\u8217\'20\'19t have a right to organize and form a union without having to take on illegal and outrageous corporate opposition,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 Sanders said his office has been lending support to strikes and organizing efforts around the US, such as the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  hearing at which \uc2 Howard Schultz\uc2  testified earlier this year and most recently citing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/chair/newsroom/press/media-advisory-as-nurses-strike-for-safer-working-conditions-at-hospitals-sanders-to-hold-senate-help-committee-field-hearing-in-new-jersey-on-americas-nursing-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nurses strike }}}\uc2  at Robert Wood Johnson University hospital in New Brunswick, New Jersey. Nurses on strike participated in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/chair/newsroom/press/media-advisory-as-nurses-strike-for-safer-working-conditions-at-hospitals-sanders-to-hold-senate-help-committee-field-hearing-in-new-jersey-on-americas-nursing-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2  last month led by Sanders on the staffing crisis plaguing hospitals around the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will use all the tools that we have to work with organized labor, to a) increase the number of workers who are in unions, and b) support workers who are on strike, or negotiating for decent wages,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Sanders. \u8220\'20\'1CI would hope that we will continue to see widespread support for union organizing, that we will see more workers organize, that we will see workers fight for decent wages and benefits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231115ejbf002ee\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
