\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t beat us\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers to strike in \u8216\'20\'18Red Cup Rebellion\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 983 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 November 2023\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Thousands expected to participate, including actions at non-unionized stores, in latest attempt to pressure company to bargain\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers will strike at stores across the US on 16 November, the company\u8217\'20\'19s promotional Red Cup Day, in their latest attempt to pressure the company to bargain a first union contract with unionized stores and address issues such as understaffing.\par \par \uc2 On Red Cup Day, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  customers get a free limited edition reusable red cup as a promotional event to kick off the holiday season. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 2022 Red Cup Day was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/business/articles/2023-02-02/starbucks-misses-sales-revenue-estimates-as-china-falters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  its highest single sales day ever despite strikes affecting over 100 stores organized by the Starbucks Workers United union.\par \par \uc2 This year, thousands of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers are expected to participate in walkouts at hundreds of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores as part of an escalated effort to expand the strikes, including actions at non-unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores. The union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SBWorkersUnited/status/1717299124306145595"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dubbed}}}\uc2  the day of action the \u8220\'20\'1CRed Cup Rebellion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Workers are calling on the company to turn off mobile ordering on high-volume promotion days, improve staffing and scheduling issues, and bargain with the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like customers don\u8217\'20\'19t know to the full extent how hard the promotional days can be. It\u8217\'20\'19s super exciting and fun for our customers to have these new cups, new drinks and all these exclusive things, but our management does not staff us correctly,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bruce Halstead, a barista at a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  roastery in Seattle, Washington.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPartners will run themselves ragged having to do the job of three people sometimes because the demand of customers is a lot more. Partners will leave their shifts in tears, they will injure themselves just trying to keep up with the demand of the cups and the drinks. We just want to bring awareness to this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Halstead got involved with the union organizing committee at his store shortly after starting his employment at the company in February 2023 and has been impressed with its ability to change management policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so empowering to be able to take matters and actions into our own hands. At the roastery, we\u8217\'20\'19ve had many successful walkouts and strikes to the point where our managers have to listen and they will start doing what we are demanding of them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Halstead. \u8220\'20\'1CNobody should have to go into their shift dreading if they are going to be cussed out by a customer today because the wait times are too long because we\u8217\'20\'19re too understaffed to keep up with the volume.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than 360 Starbucks stores representing nearly 10,000 workers in the US have won union elections with Starbucks Workers United since December 2021, but the union campaign has faced significant opposition from the company through union elections and in efforts to bargain a first union contract.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) has been inundated with hundreds of unfair labor practice charges filed on behalf of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers alleging retaliation, intimidation, harassment and delay tactics from \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , regional offices have docketed or settled 672 unfair labor practice cases against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in 39 states and Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Among the complaints include a consolidated complaint that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has failed or refused to bargain with 242 bargaining units, with an administrative law judge hearing on that case currently in progress, and a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/29/business/starbucks-union-wages/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  by a federal judge that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  violated labor law by withholding benefits and pay increases from unionized workers.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kdrv.com/news/national/starbucks-is-handing-out-pay-hikes-and-new-benefits-but-some-are-only-for-non/article_77971154-9438-5c49-8860-fb48c28901eb.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered pay increases and benefits}}}\uc2  to only non-union stores shortly after the ruling following its annual earnings call in which the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/starbucks-earnings-coffee-ffda43505dd24c2c07c9f37aeb762c7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  record revenues in the past year.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/04/starbucks-labor-union-retaliation-firings#:~:text=%E2%80%9CStarbucks%20has%20become%20the%20worst,a%20price%20for%20their%20actions.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterized}}}\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst offender of federal labor law in modern US history\u8221\'20\'1D and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SBWorkersUnited/status/1710397039379616043"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extended organizing solidarity efforts}}}\uc2  to college campuses.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and Starbucks Workers United recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&ved=2ahUKEwiH57bY4LeCAxXTJ0QIHYh1A0g4FBAWegQIDRAB&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nydailynews.com%2F2023%2F10%2F18%2Fstarbucks-palestine-israel-sues-workers-united-union%2F&usg=AOvVaw3RdxXAyH4bIfHaAQkxc_LH&opi=89978449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed lawsuits}}}\uc2  against one another over the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  logo use over statements in support of Palestine made by the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had firings, really heavy rule enforcement, a lot of bullying, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve also been on our seventh manager since we filed,\u8221\'20\'1D said G Gamache, a barista at a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store in St Louis, Missouri.\par \par \uc2 Gamache argued that staffing dropped at his store and other locations around the time stores began unionizing. When his store manager resigned in early 2022 and was replaced with a manager from another store who had a poor reputation, Gamache and his co-workers quickly organized enough interest to file for a union election, which they won in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re still here, we\u8217\'20\'19re still doing this, we\u8217\'20\'19re still picking up steam, still picking up new stores. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has tried to do everything in the playbook to beat us down and get rid of us. This is going to be my store\u8217\'20\'19s 10th strike in a year and half and we\u8217\'20\'19re still organizing new people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gamache. \u8220\'20\'1CEven when they try to whittle this down to nothing. That\u8217\'20\'19s always the message I\u8217\'20\'19m trying to send, that it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work. You can\u8217\'20\'19t beat us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  disputed claims of delaying bargaining a contract, accusing the union of delaying negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe remain committed to working with all partners, side-by-side, to elevate the everyday, and it is clear that Workers United\u8217\'20\'19s priorities don\u8217\'20\'19t include the shared success of our partners. Despite escalating rhetoric and recurring rallies, Workers United hasn\u8217\'20\'19t agreed to meet for contract bargaining in more than four months and has yet to deliver on any campaign promise made,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAs we join together to celebrate the joy of the holiday season, we call on Workers United to come to the bargaining table and do the work of negotiating a first contract on behalf of the partners they represent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231115ejbf001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
