\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Hollywood stars hail actors\u8217\'20\'19 union\u8217\'20\'19s tentative deal with studios to end strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano and Lois Beckett in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,246 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 13:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra union celebrates agreement of \u8216\'20\'18extraordinary scope\u8217\'20\'19 with Hollywood producers to settle historic work stoppage\par \par \uc2 After a work stoppage that effectively ground the Hollywood film and TV industry to a halt for months, the Sag-Aftra union announced on Wednesday that it had reached a tentative agreement to end the strike, sparking jubilation among prominent Hollywood actors including Alec Baldwin and Jamie Lee Curtis.\par \par \uc2 Roughly a month after writers ended a similar strike, Sag-Aftra and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ) \u8211\'20\'13 which represents \uc2 Walt Disney\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2  and other media companies \u8211\'20\'13 reached a tentative agreement on Wednesday. The deal, which ended the longest-ever strike for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/actors-strike-100-days-explained-hollywood-40e0e325f7c92b6853bdc01c4c54b08c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 film and television actors}}}\uc2 , came after parties had resumed talks last week following stalled negotiations in early October.\par \par \uc2 The actor and Sag-Aftra president, Fran Drescher, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CzaC3W3RG47/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe did it!!!!\u8221\'20\'1D, and thanked her fellow union members \u8220\'20\'1Cfor hanging in and holding out for this historic deal!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the premiere for his wrestling film The Iron Claw, the actor Zac Efron described the deal as \u8220\'20\'1Cincredible\u8221\'20\'1D while his co-star Jeremy Allen White \u8211\'20\'13 who also stars in the TV drama The Bear \u8211\'20\'13 exclaimed \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s amazing!\u8221\'20\'1D after hearing the strike was over while being interviewed on the red carpet with Entertainment Tonight.\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Instagram\uc2  the Oscar winner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CzZ_y_6RSx7/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Octavia Spencer}}}\uc2  posted: \u8220\'20\'1CWho else is dancing right now???\u8221\'20\'1D while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CzZ9uHIx-CM/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jamie Lee Curtis}}}\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cperseverance pays off\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CzZ-6lpuC1M/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alec Baldwin offered}}}\uc2  his \u8220\'20\'1Ccongratulations to everyone who did this great work on behalf of the members\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The union said the new contract achieved what actors on the picket lines had said they needed: pay increases and protections that made it possible for \u8220\'20\'1CSag-Aftra members from every category to build sustainable careers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a public statement, it added: \u8220\'20\'1CIn a contract valued at over $1bn, we have achieved a deal of extraordinary scope.\u8221\'20\'1D Among its wins, the union said, were larger-than-expected increases in minimum compensation, a first-time \u8220\'20\'1Cstreaming participation bonus\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented provisions for consent and compensation that will protect members from the threat of AI\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood producers also touted the tentative deal as establishing \u8220\'20\'1Ca new paradigm\u8221\'20\'1D for the industry. The contract \u8220\'20\'1Cgives Sag-Aftra the biggest contract-on-contract gains in the history of the union, including the largest increase in minimum wages in the last forty years; a brand new residual for streaming programs; extensive consent and compensation protections in the use of artificial intelligence; and sizable contract increases on items across the board\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  said in a statement on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 The union said the 118-day strike would be \u8220\'20\'1Cofficially suspended\u8221\'20\'1D at 12.01am on Thursday, and that all picket locations would close.\par \par \uc2 The breakthrough means Hollywood can ramp up to full production for the first time since May, once union members vote to ratify the deal in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 The union had fought for increased base pay for residuals, and guardrails around the use of artificial intelligence in film and television, concerns shared by writers who fought for similar protections in their contract.\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  began its strike in July with top stars heading to picket lines from Los Angeles to New York, and offering their support. George Clooney called it \u8220\'20\'1Can inflection point in our industry\u8221\'20\'1D, and said change was necessary for the \u8220\'20\'1Cindustry to survive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The resolution of the writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike in September left union leaders feeling optimistic, and talks with the studios resumed in early October for the first time since their work stoppage. The studios walked away from negotiations amid a dispute over the use of AI and streaming residuals, arguing the actors\u8217\'20\'19 demands were unreasonable, but came back to the negotiating table.\par \par \uc2 In a contract valued at over one billion dollars, we have achieved a deal of extraordinary scope that includes "above-pattern" minimum compensation increases, unprecedented provisions for consent and compensation that will protect members from the threat of AI,... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lQe6snkQsY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lQe6snkQsY}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  (@sagaftra) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sagaftra/status/1722441057571684724?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 While the full details of the agreement were not immediately released, local news outlets reported that the actors had scored important wins, including on new compensation for shows that appear on streaming services, gains in health insurance, and new rules for the use of AI technology to replicate actors\u8217\'20\'19 images and likenesses.\par \par \uc2 In its statement, the union said the deal also included \u8220\'20\'1Ccompensation increases for background performers, and critical contract provisions protecting diverse communities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  said the details of the deal would be made public after a meeting on Friday, where board members will review the contract.\par \par \uc2 In late-stage negotiations over the weekend, the \uc2 Netflix\uc2  CEO, \uc2 Ted Sarandos\uc2 , told union leadership, \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t just come toward you, we came all the way to you,\u8221\'20\'1D Deadline reported.\par \par \uc2 The deals won by the actors\u8217\'20\'19 and writers\u8217\'20\'19 unions this fall \u8220\'20\'1Crepresent a capitulation by Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s biggest companies\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/08/business/media/actors-strike-deal.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , and a stark reversal for the studio bosses who thought the unions would be \u8220\'20\'1Crelatively compliant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  said in its statement it was \u8220\'20\'1Cpleased to have reached a tentative agreement and looks forward to the industry resuming the work of telling great stories\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With the strike causing film and TV productions to grind to a halt, affecting the awards season and taking a financial and mental toll on working actors, the parties had faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/oct/24/actors-strike-when-will-it-end-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing pressure}}}\uc2  to come to a resolution.\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Los Angeles, Karen Bass, said in a statement she was \u8220\'20\'1Cgrateful\u8221\'20\'1D that the parties had reached a deal, since the strike had \u8220\'20\'1Cimpacted millions in Los Angeles and throughout the country\u8221\'20\'1D. While those on the picket lines \u8220\'20\'1Chave been the hardest hit\u8221\'20\'1D, Bass said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere have been ripple effects throughout our entire city\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although the writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike had immediate, visible effects for viewers, including the months-long suspension of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/actors-strike-late-night-shows-return-negotiations-1ddcaa8c4684375f8e56d2cd2abd62ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 late-night talkshows}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/saturday-night-live-returns-a3c0feb411b8f673797fb1d4fdc2546b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saturday Night Live}}}\uc2 , the impact of the actors\u8217\'20\'19 absence was not as immediately apparent. But viewers may continue to feel its effects \u8211\'20\'13 delayed release dates and waits for new show seasons \u8211\'20\'13 for months or even years.\par \par \uc2 Now that a deal has been reached, actors could quickly return to movie sets where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/actors-strike-delayed-shows-movies-writers-42b99032bb638930df097f675b363898"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 productions were paused}}}\uc2 , including Deadpool 3, Gladiator 2 and Wicked. Other movies and shows will restart shooting once returning writers finish scripts.\par \par \uc2 The end of the strike would also fully free actors to return to red carpets, talkshows and podcasts, as Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s awards season approaches. The only major awards show directly effected by the strike was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/emmy-awards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emmys}}}\uc2 , which was moved from September to January. Now, the usual fall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/oscars"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oscar}}}\uc2  campaigns will mobilize.\par \par \uc2 The end of the strike announcement came hours after \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO, \uc2 Robert Iger\uc2 , and \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO, \uc2 David Zaslav\uc2 , reported their latest earning statements. Both executives said they hoped the strike would be resolved soon.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares rose based on its report, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/disney-earnings-iger-fox-hulu-bdb8b52dbeca1358270d0ee60e97cbfd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said its net income jumped}}}\uc2  63% to $264m in the quarter that ended on 30 September, up from $162m a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2  reported losses and saw its shares fall 19% on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 On an earnings call ahead of the deal announcement, Zaslav said the studio\u8217\'20\'19s last offer to \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmet virtually all of the union\u8217\'20\'19s goals and includes the highest wage increase in 40 years\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press and Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231109ejb90005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
