\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US nursing home workers face \u8216\'20\'18catastrophic crisis\u8217\'20\'19 of understaffing\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 981 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2023\par 19:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Persistent problem has grave impacts on patient care, on residents\u8217\'20\'19 wellbeing, and is causing spiraling burnout for staff\par \par \uc2 For Linda Long, who has worked in nursing homes since 1997, at the same facility outside of Tacoma, Washington, since 2003, understaffing has always been a problem.\par \par \uc2 It only got worse during the Covid-19 pandemic, when she said co-workers were leaving due to the short staffing, constant Covid outbreaks and the immense workloads that staff were left with to fill in the void.\par \par \uc2 But, workers and labor experts say, short-staffing in the crucial US industry has persisted after the pandemic, with grave impacts on patient care and residents\u8217\'20\'19 wellbeing, and spiraling burnout that has become pervasive in the care industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost of the time, I want to cry when I see things and I can\u8217\'20\'19t do any more than I can do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Long. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are times when we have extra people and we\u8217\'20\'19re jumping for joy because I know the residents will have somebody to talk to, but in general we are still short-staffed, which means you look at the residents every day thinking. \u8216\'20\'18Oh my God, how am I going to do this for them today?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Long said that the care many residents need has to be done by multiple people at a time, such as operating lifts to raise patients in and out of bed to bathe, to eat and to be active, and oftentimes nursing aides aren\u8217\'20\'19t available to help complete these tasks. The short-staffing often results in workers skipping their breaks and lunches, and cutting corners wherever they can to save time so they can attend to every resident.\par \par \uc2 You have to decide what to do, what you cannot do, but there\u8217\'20\'19s not one task that can really be left out\par \par \uc2 Linda Long\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to decide what to do, what you cannot do, but there\u8217\'20\'19s not one task that can really be left out,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt really affects the wellbeing of the residents and yours, because you go home knowing you couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do the things you need to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She described the heartbreaking daily experiences she and other workers face when residents are weary about asking staff to help them with something because they see how short-staffed and overworked they are at the facility. And if tasks are skipped or missed, residents\u8217\'20\'19 conditions can quickly deteriorate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShowers aren\u8217\'20\'19t being done all the time because we can\u8217\'20\'19t always get to it,\u8221\'20\'1D added Long. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople will lose the ability to walk, the ability to sit up, to do a range of motions, and that has a lot to do with being shorthanded because they don\u8217\'20\'19t get any of the basic care they need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration and labor groups are hoping for change. The US Department of Health and Human Services\u8217\'20\'19 Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/hhs-proposes-minimum-staffing-standards-enhance-safety-and-quality-nursing-homes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  a rule to implement minimum staffing standards in long-term care facilities, with the public comment period ending on 6 November. If implemented, it would be the first ever minimum federal staffing standard for nursing homes that care for 1.2 million people.\par \par \uc2 Under the proposed rule, the CMS estimates 75% of facilities would have to improve staffing in their facilities. The rule would require nursing homes to provide residents with a minimum of 0.55 hours of care from a registered nurse per resident per day and 2.45 hours of care from a nurse aide per resident every day.\par \par \uc2 More than 50 unions, worker groups and organizations signed on to a letter in support of federal minimum staffing levels in nursing homes, including the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 SEIU\uc2 ), the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  and MomsRising.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur country\u8217\'20\'19s long-term care system is in the midst of a catastrophic crisis, and nursing home workers and residents have suffered unspeakable consequences. In the absence of a federal staffing standard, nursing home workers have endured complete physical, mental and emotional exhaustion due to understaffed shifts and unsafe working conditions, and nursing home residents have been robbed of the quality care and quality of life they deserve,\u8221\'20\'1D said the \uc2 SEIU\uc2  president, \uc2 Mary Kay Henry\uc2 , in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiu.org/2023/09/seius-henry-cms-proposed-rule-is-a-historic-first-step-of-whats-needed-to-address-nursing-home-staffing-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  supporting the standard.\par \par \uc2 But several nursing home CEOs have written {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.regulations.gov/document/CMS-2023-0144-0001/comment?filter=CEO&pageNumber=2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public comments}}}\uc2  to oppose the rule, claiming it\u8217\'20\'19s not feasible due to costs and labor shortages, with many workers and family members of residents writing in support of the rule or calling to strengthen it.\par \par \uc2 The nursing home industry is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ibisworld.com/united-states/market-research-reports/nursing-care-facilities-industry/#IndustryStatisticsAndTrends"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multibillion-dollar industry}}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketplace.org/2021/02/11/the-economics-of-nursing-homes-and-paying-for-one/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 70% }}}\uc2  of nursing homes operating as for-profit facilities. In recent years, private equity firms have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kffhealthnews.org/news/article/private-equity-ownership-of-nursing-homes-triggers-federal-probe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  their ownership or stake in nursing homes, with research demonstrating that private equity ownership results in worse health outcomes.\par \par \uc2 Tina Siegel has worked as a licensed practical nurse in a nursing home in Erie, Pennsylvania, for 38 years, where she says staffing shortages have always been an issue in the industry but have worsened during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Pennsylvania {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://observer-reporter.com/news/localnews/new-staffing-ratios-for-pa-nursing-homes-takes-effect/article_4f78d5b4-1756-11ee-a4c6-035408a78965.html#:~:text=During%20the%20day%2C%20nursing%20home,250%20residents%20at%20all%20times."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enacted}}}\uc2  statewide staff-to-patient ratios for nursing homes amid pushes from workers like Siegel, which she says have helped to improve staffing issues. She said the ratios are needed nationwide to improve working conditions for staff and the care and dignity that nursing home residents deserve.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe feel really connected to our residents. We take care of them, some of them we\u8217\'20\'19re the only family they have. We\u8217\'20\'19re there when they\u8217\'20\'19re passing away, and you want to spend time with them because you\u8217\'20\'19re the only person there, but a lot of times you don\u8217\'20\'19t have time to do that either. So \u8230\'20\'26 you feel bad because in their last moments of their life, they\u8217\'20\'19re by themselves and that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t happen to people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Siegel.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231107ejb7001pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
