\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US labor movement faces big obstacles despite surge in strikes and union wins\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,582 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2023\par 14:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Recent union contract gains against a backdrop of decades of union decline, worsening wealth inequality and broken labor laws\par \par \uc2 The US labor movement is having a moment amid some recent big union contract wins, surges in strikes, historic union election wins at aggressively anti-union corporations, and a presidential administration that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/statements/icymi-president-biden-im-most-pro-union-president-american-history-and-i-make-no"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touts }}}\uc2  itself as the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-union in history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  reached a historic tentative agreement with Ford that includes 25% wage gains, then shortly after reached an agreement with \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2 . The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1718800736174080378"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on other unions to time their contract expirations with 1 May to collectively pressure employers simultaneously, with the next \uc2 UAW\uc2  contracts at the Big 3 set to expire on 1 May 2028.\par \par \uc2 Other unions have also won {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2023/08/teamsters-ratify-historic-ups-contract/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic}}}\uc2  contract gains this year at large employers such as UPS and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/oct/07/screenwriters-won-a-historic-victory-against-ai-the-rest-of-us-should-follow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Hollywood studios for TV and film writers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But labor in the US is still facing significant obstacles and challenges in transforming the popular culture shift into gains against a backdrop of decades of union decline, worsening wealth inequality, and broken labor laws where employers violate labor laws with impunity and try to delay and bust union organizing campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Unionized workers have been framing recent surges in strikes for new contracts around corporate greed, exorbitant profits and soaring executive pay, leveraging a tight labor market and a growing public shift in support of the US labor movement.\par \par \uc2 So far 2023 has seen a significant influx in work stoppages, with employers experiencing the largest loss of labor hours to work stoppages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poweratwork.us/why-so-many-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in at least 23 years}}}\uc2 , around 11m labor hours from January to September 2023, according to the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Cornell University Labor Action Tracker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ILRLaborAction/status/1716443493294350503/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  recorded}}}\uc2  69 strikes in September 2023, involving 214,300 workers. Some 11,000 Hollywood television and film writers recently reached a historic deal after five months on strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the business has boomed, and studios have collected almost $30bn in annual profits, writer pay has gone down,\u8221\'20\'1D Laura Blum-Smith, the director of research and public policy at \uc2 WGA West\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/writers-strike-hollywood-wga-vote-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  in April.\par \par \uc2 The Screen Actors Guild, which represents over 150,000 actors, has been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/oct/24/actors-strike-when-will-it-end-negotiations#:~:text=The%20Screen%20Actors%20Guild%2DAmerican,(Disney%2C%20Paramount%2C%20Sony%2C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  strike}}}\uc2  since July 2023.\par \par \uc2 The Good Fight star Christine Baranski said during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/bryan-cranston-bob-iger-sag-strike-speech-1235544919/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike rally}}}\uc2  in July: \u8220\'20\'1CIf this industry can generate millions, hundreds of millions, in compensation for those at the top, it can afford to share the wealth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over 75,000 healthcare workers walked out on a three-day strike from 4 October to 7 October, the largest healthcare strike in US history and shortly won a new contract following the strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe executives that are making millions of dollars aren\u8217\'20\'19t thinking about anyone else but their own profit and their own increasing wages and not thinking about the rest of us,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeffrey Melara, a \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  worker in California, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/kaiser-permanente-healthcare-strike-hospital-union-california-washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in the days ahead of the strike.\par \par \uc2 But it is the strike that hit the US car industry that has created the most headlines and impact.\par \par \uc2 The Big 3 automakers, Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , made $250bn in profits from 2013 to 2022, an increase in 92% while average auto worker wages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/uaw-automakers-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  dropped}}}\uc2  19.3% during the same period. Their three CEOS have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-10-13/detroit-carmakers-paid-1-billion-to-ceos-as-auto-wages-slumped"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  received}}}\uc2  about $1bn in compensation since 2010.\par \par \uc2 Andy Davis, an assembler at \uc2 Allison Transmission\uc2  in Indianapolis, Indiana, and \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 933 second vice-president, said the recent strikes and broad fight by autoworkers is a push to restore the upward mobility and security that has dissipated as a worker in a highly profitable industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica sees our \uc2 UAW\uc2  jobs as icons of success and stability for the average and ordinary,\u8221\'20\'1D said Davis. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to get back to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , union petitions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unions-and-well-being/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  increased}}}\uc2  3% in fiscal year 2023 compared to 2022, with 2022 seeing a 53% increase in union election petitions from the previous year. During the same period, the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s field offices saw a 10% increase in unfair labor practice charges, from a 19% increase in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/unfair-labor-practices-charge-filings-up-10-union-petitions-up-3-in-fiscal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  noted}}}\uc2  the agency remains severely understaffed and underfunded amid rises in caseloads, with field office staff being cut by 50% in the past two decades.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, labor law reform efforts to improve worker protections to organize unions such as the Pro Act have stalled in Congress, with little to no support from the Republican party despite public support for unions bridging across partisan lines.\par \par \uc2 US union membership declined to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/union2.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  10.1%}}}\uc2  in 2022 from 10.3% in 2021, the lowest on record according to the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . Although the number of workers belonging to unions increased by 273,000 workers to 14.3 million in 2022, the total number of workers in the US workforce grew by 5.3 million, resulting in the drop in union density.\par \par \uc2 While national headlines suggest there is a wave of union wins across the US, wide variations persist in unionization rates based on workforces and geography.\par \par \uc2 Some 33% of public sector workers are union members, compared with 6% of private sector workers. Hawaii has the highest union density in the US, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/union2.t05.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  21.9%}}}\uc2  of the workforce affiliated as members of unions, compared with the lowest union density in South Carolina at 1.7%.\par \par \uc2 These wide variations in union density by state have significant economic impacts. A December 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unions-and-well-being/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2  found on average the 17 states with the highest union densities have higher state minimum wages, higher median annual incomes, higher unemployment insurance recipiency rates, lower uninsured populations, and are more likely to have state laws such as paid sick leave and paid family and medical leave.\par \par \uc2 Union membership in the US soared in the 1930s amid industrial unrest and the Great Depression, spurring union density rates of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unions-help-reduce-disparities-and-strengthen-our-democracy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  over 30%}}}\uc2  in the wake of second world war, but gradually began decreasing in the 1960s only to sharply decline in the 1980s and the following decades.\par \par \uc2 The labor movement\u8217\'20\'19s rise in the US incited well-funded anti-union efforts, propped up by a multimillion-dollar anti-union consultant industry and corporations that are currently fighting union campaigns despite numerous violations and rulings against them at the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 . They include Amazon, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , REI, Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s, \uc2 Apple\uc2  and Chipotle \u8211\'20\'13 big employers who have vigorously fought off union drives and efforts for workers to secure a first union contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CManagement and employers have captured the labor law terrain and this has been true for quite a while, so that they are extremely effective at blocking unionization efforts and diminishing the power of already organized workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ruth Milkman, chair of the labor studies department at CUNY School of Labor and Urban Studies. \u8220\'20\'1CUntil there\u8217\'20\'19s some kind of overhauling of US labor law, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to see how that long-term decline is going to get turned around. Because what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing in the new organizing is blockages at every turn.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Milkman explained that previous upswings in unionization in the US have historically come in large waves, but that the increases in strikes, union organizing among young workers especially and increases in public support for the labor movement have yet to occur on a big enough scale to reverse the long trend of union density decline in the US.\par \par \uc2 But the desire among workers for unionization is there as numerous polls have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cios-shuler-state-unions-strong-record-public-support-unprecedented-activism-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2  record favorability, especially among young people, for labor unions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/working-people-want-a-voice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polling}}}\uc2  has shown that an increasing number of workers would join a union if they could \u8211\'20\'13 far higher rates of favorability than the low proportions of workers in the US who are currently unionized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe new organizing is happening, the attitudes, pro-union views, led by a new generation that was often dismissed as apolitical,\u8221\'20\'1D added Milkman. \u8220\'20\'1CThis whole political generation that has only come to being in the last decade or so, they\u8217\'20\'19re very eager to do this and they are running up against a brick wall in a lot of cases, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t think they\u8217\'20\'19re going to stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ken Jacobs, chair of the University of California Berkeley Center for Labor Research, cited some of the positive rulings to come out of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  under the Biden administration aimed at improving workers\u8217\'20\'19 protections to organize under the National Labor Relations Act amid not only at increases in union election petitions, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/bloomberg-law-analysis/analysis-unions-on-a-roll-are-reeling-in-the-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  win rates}}}\uc2  for unions as well.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe win rate has to be turned into gaining collective bargaining agreements\u8221\'20\'1D said Jacobs. \u8220\'20\'1CThere won\u8217\'20\'19t be a change in labor law unless large numbers of workers are in motion demanding unions, and that won\u8217\'20\'19t happen without a large investment in organizing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 From the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/apr/28/resistance-now-arizona-colorado-teachers-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Red for Ed}}}\uc2  teachers\u8217\'20\'19 strike wave in 2018 and 2019 to the uptick in worker organizing both in and out of unionization efforts through the Covid-19 pandemic, Jacobs noted workers being able to raise public awareness and see a ground swelling of support have helped inspire this cultural shift to viewing unions favorably.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we have seen a big cultural shift around unions,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Jacobs. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think we have in any time in history seen examples that have an important effect on the balance of power between workers and capital happen without very significant pressure from below with massive engagement of workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231031ejav0018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
