\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ford and \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 union negotiators reach potential new deal\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and agencies \par \uc2 598 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2023\par 13:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Agreement is pending union leadership approval and is the first settlement in the strike against big three automakers\par \par \uc2 Ford Motor Company\uc2  and the negotiators of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2  reached a labor deal on Wednesday, pending union leadership approval.\par \par \uc2 A deal would be the first settlement of strikes against Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 More than 45,000 union members working at the \u8220\'20\'1CDetroit Three\u8221\'20\'1D automakers have joined walkouts that began on 15 September.\par \par \uc2 The deal is expected to provide a 25% wage hike through the life of the contract, including 11% to start, one of the sources said. Including compounding and cost of living, workers will get more than 30% under the tentative deal. The agreement will also reportedly reduce the time it takes new workers to reach the maximum wage \u8211\'20\'13from eight to three years.\par \par \uc2 If agreed upon, the union deal will be one of several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/us-unions-successes-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major wins for US unions  }}}\uc2  over the last few months following agreements for double-digit pay rises for workers at parcel giant UPS, Hollywood writers and health workers at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 In a video posted on X, Shawn Fain, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe reached an historic agreement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Record profits mean record contracts. We have a tentative agreement at Ford. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandUpUAW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandUpUAW  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z00T5CfQJN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Z00T5CfQJN  }}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UAW\uc2  (@UAW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1717337144572662025?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023  }}}\uc2  (@UAW)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor months, we said that record profits mean record contracts. And \uc2 UAW\uc2  family, our stand-up strike has delivered.\u8221\'20\'1D He said union leaders would seek to get the deal finalized over the weekend before seeking approval from members.\par \par \uc2 Getting the deal ratified will be up to Fain and \uc2 UAW\uc2  leaders, and it is not assured. \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers at Mack Truck earlier this month rejected a proposed contract agreed to by Fain. \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers at the company now called \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  rejected a proposal endorsed by \uc2 UAW\uc2  leaders in 2015.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s most recent move was to strike against each company\u8217\'20\'19s most profitable plants \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 GM\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Arlington, Texas, assembly plant; Ford\u8217\'20\'19s heavy-duty pickup factory in Kentucky; and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 Ram pickup plant in Sterling Heights, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Total economic losses from the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike have reached $9.3bn, the Anderson Economic Group said this week.\par \par \uc2 If the contract is ratified by Ford-\uc2 UAW\uc2  workers, it would set the standard for bargaining at \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  , and expire in 2028.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis lays the groundwork for the next two contracts and they should fall in line fairly quickly because all three were within a narrow gap of each other,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Sam Fiorani\uc2  , the vice-president of global vehicle forecasting at AutoForecast Solutions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe strike so far has been painful for everybody and knowing what it takes to get a signed contract should bring them to the table much quicker,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The three companies had no immediate comment.\par \par \uc2 The union has waged an unusual campaign of simultaneous strikes against the Detroit Three automakers, demanding a 40% wage hike, including a 20% immediate increase and improvements in benefits, as well as covering EV battery plant workers under union agreements.\par \par \uc2 The automakers have argued that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s demands will significantly raise costs and hobble their electric vehicle ambitions, putting them at a disadvantage when compared with Tesla and foreign brands such as \uc2 Toyota\uc2  , which are non-unionized.\par \par \uc2 Rather than the hammer blow of a mass walkout it has wielded historically, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has played the companies against each other, using reprieves from expansion of work stoppages as encouragement.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed to this article\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231030ejau0033w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
