\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They have reached a historic agreement\u8217\'20\'19: Biden hails \uc2 UAW\uc2  settlement with big three carmakers \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 5,813 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2023\par 20:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  reached a tentative agreement with \uc2 GM\uc2  earlier today, the last of the three companies targeted in the strike\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 A judge in Denver has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fcf548f08b48bad7c4dfa#block-653fcf548f08b48bad7c4dfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started hearing arguments}}}\uc2  in a case brought by liberal group Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington aiming at removing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from the ballot for inciting the January 6 insurrection. A lawyer for the former president argued the plaintiffs do not understand the meaning of the word \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection,\u8221\'20\'1D while the case could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653f9fc88f0880c2481927fa#block-653f9fc88f0880c2481927fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately end up}}}\uc2  decided by the conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 . Hearings in the Colorado case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fb3b68f08b48bad7c4ca9#block-653fb3b68f08b48bad7c4ca9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are expected}}}\uc2  to continue throughout the week, while a judge in Minnesota will begin considering a similar lawsuit on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hailed agreements reached between the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  and the Detroit automakers as \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653ffc578f0837aa4c22e055#block-653ffc578f0837aa4c22e055"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a speech}}}\uc2  at the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Artificial intelligence developers face new rules under an executive order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6540065c8f0837aa4c22e0b9#block-6540065c8f0837aa4c22e0b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden signed today}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fab1a8f08b48bad7c4c3c#block-653fab1a8f08b48bad7c4c3c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains}}}\uc2  at the top of the polls in Iowa, which isn\u8217\'20\'19t really news. The most interesting tidbits of the survey may be \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarkable favorability despite his overall floundering campaign, and Nikki Haley \u8217\'20\'19s measurable jump in support.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Never Trumper Asa Hutchinson \u8217\'20\'19s campaign may be falling apart after his manager and confidante resigned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fd82a8f0837aa4c22dec2#block-653fd82a8f0837aa4c22dec2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reports}}}\uc2 . Hutchinson is polling at 1% support in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York House Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fed228f0880c248192c22#block-653fed228f0880c248192c22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are optimistic}}}\uc2  they have votes to boot congressman George Santos, who has admitted to fabricating his resume and faces federal charges, out of office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the top Republican in the Senate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fe5448f08b48bad7c4f47#block-653fe5448f08b48bad7c4f47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged Congress}}}\uc2  to approve aid to both Ukraine and Israel. House Republicans seem on board with the latter, but are growing increasingly wary of the former.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments on the apparent conclusion of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 strike came at the start of an event where he signed an executive order that imposes rules on artificial intelligence development.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-ai-artificial-intelligence-executive-order-cb86162000d894f238f28ac029005059"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Associated Press}}}\uc2  on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s new policy:\par \par \uc2 Before signing the order, Biden said AI is driving change at \u8220\'20\'1Cwarp speed\u8221\'20\'1D and carries tremendous potential as well as perils.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAI is all around us,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CTo realize the promise of AI and avoid the risk, we need to govern this technology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The order is an initial step that is meant to ensure that AI is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-ai-artificial-intelligence-518ec2a9190cfb10db9dbcc1eaab3c4c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trustworthy and helpful}}}\uc2 , rather than deceitful and destructive. The order \u8211\'20\'13 which will likely need to be augmented by congressional action \u8211\'20\'13 seeks to steer how AI is developed so that companies can profit without putting public safety in jeopardy.\par \par \uc2 Using the Defense Production Act, the order requires leading AI developers to share safety test results and other information with the government. The \uc2 National Institute of Standards and Technology\uc2  is to create standards to ensure AI tools are safe and secure before public release.\par \par \uc2 The commerce department is to issue guidance to label and watermark AI-generated content to help differentiate between authentic interactions and those generated by software. The extensive order touches on matters of privacy, civil rights, consumer protections, scientific research and worker rights.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip of a Biden laugh line from his event this afternoon announcing the order:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden ahead of signing an executive order imposing safety and security measures on AI:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith AI, fraudsters can take a three-second... recording of your voice. I\u8217\'20\'19ve watched one of me \u8230\'20\'26 I said, \u8216\'20\'18When the hell did I say that?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GKACIVPjHa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GKACIVPjHa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719074044706763118?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cheering the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new agreements with the Big Three automakers:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden praises the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and Big Three automakers for coming to tentative labor agreements on raises to end the strikes:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese record agreements reward auto workers who gave up much to keep the industry working and going during the financial crisis more than a decade ago.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZaSkMs95Nx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZaSkMs95Nx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719071624454889822?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden had gotten closer to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strike than any president who came before him, by traveling to Michigan to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 address a picket line of striking workers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden calls \uc2 UAW\uc2  agreements 'historic', says autoworkers can return to factories\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hailed the deals reached between the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  and the three major Detroit automakers that are set to end a six-week strike at their factories.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have reached a historic agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said of automakers Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  as well as the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , who president Shawn Fain he spoke to earlier today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese record agreements reward auto workers who gave up much to keep the industry working and going during the financial crisis more than a decade ago. These agreements ensure the iconic Big Three can still lead the world in quality and innovation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached a tentative agreement with GM earlier today}}}\uc2 , the last of the three companies targeted in the strike.\par \par \uc2 The agreements need to be ratified by union members, but Biden said the automakers and the \uc2 UAW\uc2  have agreed that workers can return to assembly lines before that happens.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI applaud the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and the leaders of the automobile companies for agreeing that all the workers on strike and all those who were walking the picket lines on behalf of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  brothers and sisters can go back to work immediately, even before the vote is taken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what we learned from the presidential poll of Iowa Republicans released this morning, which appeared to be very good for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  maintained his huge lead in the crucial early voting state of Iowa in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/first-read/trump-maintains-commanding-lead-iowa-poll-rcna122410"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major new poll}}}\uc2  by NBC News and the Des Moines Register but Nikki Haley is now emerging as his closest challenger.\par \par \uc2 The former US president has a 27-point lead in Iowa three months before the first vote of the Republican primary as he attracted 43% support. But Haley, the former South Carolina governor and United Nations ambassador, climbed 10 points to 16%, sharing second place with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , the Florida governor whose campaign has long been seen to be stalling.\par \par \uc2 No other candidate scored significantly, even after second choices of supporters of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former vice-president who suspended his campaign, were reapportioned.\par \par \uc2 J Ann Selzer\uc2 , the Iowa pollster who conducted the survey, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a good poll for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . For all the things that happened between the last poll and now, he\u8217\'20\'19s still the dominant player in the field and his standing has, in fact, improved from August.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/iowa-poll-republicans-trump-nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump maintains huge Iowa polling lead as Nikki Haley gains ground}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  with more on the start of the legal effort today to keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  off presidential ballots for his involvement in the January 6 insurrection:\par \par \uc2 A multi-pronged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/20/trump-disqualified-constitution-section-3-14th-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effort to keep Donald Trump off the 2024 presidential ballot}}}\uc2  as an insurrectionist resumes in earnest, beginning with a court case in Colorado on Monday, the first of two states that will hear legal arguments this week.\par \par \uc2 Those seeking to have the former president ruled ineligible are relying on a civil war-era {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitution.congress.gov/browse/amendment-14/section-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provision of the 14th amendment}}}\uc2  to the US constitution that states no person can hold public office if they \u8220\'20\'1Chave engaged in insurrection or rebellion against the same, or given aid or comfort to the enemies thereof\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They argue that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s incitement of the deadly 6 January {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack on the US Capitol}}}\uc2 , in which his supporters attempted to block {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congress certifying}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election victory, perfectly encapsulates the clause that has yet to be seriously tested in a courtroom.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/trump-14th-amendment-colorado-trial-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Efforts to keep \u8216\'20\'18insurrectionist\u8217\'20\'19 Trump off 2024 ballot to be heard in court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York House Republicans believe they are close to securing the two-thirds majority required to expel their fellow Republican George Santos who has pled not guilty to over a dozen fraud-related counts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re getting two-thirds. There seems to be a good sentiment out there that enough is enough,\u8221\'20\'1D CNN reports Nick LaLota, who represents New York\u8217\'20\'19s first district, saying.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople have seen over the last ten months what a fraud he is,\u8221\'20\'1D Anthony D\u8217\'20\'19Espositio, who represents New York\u8217\'20\'19s fourth district, said, echoing similar sentiments.\par \par \uc2 Marcus Molinaro, the state\u8217\'20\'19s representative of its 13th district, said, \u8220\'20\'1CI think at this time, it is absolutely inapropriate for him to serve\u8230\'20\'26 I think there\u8217\'20\'19s significant support, certainly on both ends of the aisle. I understand hesitance but this is a clear case of an individual who used every lie and misdeed in order to obtain the very office he holds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNew York Rs believe they are close to 2/3 needed to make George Santos just the 6th House member ever expelled.\par \par \uc2 "I understand the hesitance, but this is a clear case of an individual who used every lie and misdeed in order to attain the very office that he holds," Molinaro said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IJTbg29i6r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IJTbg29i6r}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1719019637768155265?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is more from the lawyer in Colorado arguing against the lawsuits attempting to prevent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from appearing on the 2024 presidential ballot:\par \par \uc2 Refering to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions on January 6, 2021, he said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s substantial historical evidence that \u8216\'20\'18engage\u8217\'20\'19 does not mean mere incitement through words. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that. And frankly, president Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t engage.\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t carry a pitchfork to Capitol grounds. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t lead a charge. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t get into a fistfight with legislators. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t goad president Biden into going out back and having a fight.\par \par \uc2 He gave a speech in which he asked people to peacefully and patriotically go to the Capitol to protest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrLawyer argues Trump's actions on 1/6 don't constitute engaging in an insurrection:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe didn\u8217\'20\'19t carry a pitchfork to Capitol grounds. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t lead a charge. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t get into a fistfight with legislators. He didn't goad President Biden into going out back and having a fight.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FJmDcTl0Fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FJmDcTl0Fc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719014640963715313?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is urging the Senate to pass a supplemental foreign aid package to Ukraine and Israel.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on Monday, McConnell said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, our efforts are making a difference, both in Ukraine and here at home. But the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s hesitation along the way has really in my view prolonged the bloodshed.\par \par \uc2 This is a moment for swift and decisive action to prevent further loss of life, and to impose real consequences on the tyrants who have terrorized the people of Ukraine and of Israel.\par \par \uc2 And right now, the Senate has a chance to produce supplemental assistance that will help us do exactly that.\par \par \uc2 enltrMinority Leader McConnell (R-KY) urges the Senate to pass a supplemental foreign aid package:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a moment for swift and decisive action to prevent further loss of life, and to impose real consequences on the tyrants who have terrorized the people of Ukraine and of Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XLONK4RNIi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XLONK4RNIi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719035841555705985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A judge in Denver has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fcf548f08b48bad7c4dfa#block-653fcf548f08b48bad7c4dfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started hearing arguments}}}\uc2  in a case brought by liberal group Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington aiming at removing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from the ballot for inciting the January 6 insurrection. A lawyer for the former president argued the plaintiffs do not understand the meaning of the word \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection,\u8221\'20\'1D while the case could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653f9fc88f0880c2481927fa#block-653f9fc88f0880c2481927fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately end up}}}\uc2  decided by the conservative-dominated supreme court. Hearings in the Colorado case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fb3b68f08b48bad7c4ca9#block-653fb3b68f08b48bad7c4ca9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are expected}}}\uc2  to continue through the week, while a judge in Minnesota will begin considering a similar lawsuit on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fc5a28f0837aa4c22ddbd#block-653fc5a28f0837aa4c22ddbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  an agreement to end the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strike against \uc2 General Motors\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and the six-week walkout against the Detroit automakers \u8211\'20\'13 was \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fab1a8f08b48bad7c4c3c#block-653fab1a8f08b48bad7c4c3c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains}}}\uc2  at the top of the polls in Iowa, which isn\u8217\'20\'19t really news. The most interesting tidbits of the survey may be \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarkable favorability despite his overall floundering campaign, and Nikki Haley \u8217\'20\'19s measurable jump in support.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Never Trumper Asa Hutchinson \u8217\'20\'19s campaign may be falling apart after his manager and confidante resigned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fd82a8f0837aa4c22dec2#block-653fd82a8f0837aa4c22dec2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reports}}}\uc2 . Hutchinson is polling at 1% support in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 All the way back in July, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  took a look at the prospects of the few Never Trumpers competing for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, and concluded they were not good. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the forces that derailed \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign and are hurting Asa Hutchinson\u8217\'20\'19s:\par \par \uc2 For Asa Hutchinson, former governor of Arkansas, there were boos and chants of \u8220\'20\'1CTrump! Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D. For \uc2 Francis Suarez\uc2 , mayor of Miami, there were jeers and cries of \u8220\'20\'1CTraitor!\u8221\'20\'1D And perhaps most tellingly, there was no Florida governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2  at all.\par \par \uc2 The recent Turning Point USA conference brought thousands of young conservatives to Florida and there was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-desantis-gop-primary-turning-point-usa-cb94fa925ba2e4774ecbb9736fbcbe15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no doubting the main attraction}}}\uc2  : former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who made a glitzy entrance accompanied by giant stage sparklers. In a less than rigorous poll, 86% of attendees gave Trump as their first choice for president; DeSantis, who polled 19% last year, was down to 4%.\par \par \uc2 Events and numbers like this are cause for sleepless nights among those Republican leaders and donors desperate to believe it would be different this time. The Never Trump forces bet heavily on DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/12/donald-trump-us-midterms-republicans-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as the coming man}}}\uc2  and the premise that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign would collapse under the weight of myriad legal problems.\par \par \uc2 But six months away from the first-in-the-nation Iowa caucuses, none of it seems to be working. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/02/ron-desantis-campaign-2024-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign is flailing}}}\uc2  and leaving some with buyers\u8217\'20\'19 remorse. Hutchinson and \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , outspoken Trump critics, are polling in single digits, sowing doubts about voters\u8217\'20\'19 appetite for change. Never Trumpers have reason to fear that his march to the Republican nomination may already be unstoppable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re experiencing a brutal wake-up call that the party is not interested in hearing critiques of Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thebulwark.com/author/tim-miller/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Miller}}}\uc2 , who was communications director for Jeb Bush\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump challengers\u8217\'20\'19 candidacies have been astonishingly poor and learned nothing from 2016. When the leading candidate gets indicted and all of his opponents besides \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and Asa Hutchinson just echo his fake persecution complex talking points, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be hard to beat him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/24/never-trump-republican-presidential-candidates-polling-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Never Trumpers get \u8216\'20\'18brutal wake-up call\u8217\'20\'19 as Republican candidates flounder}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  is among the few Republican presidential candidates who have openly attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and his campaign now appears to be collapsing.\par \par \uc2 CBS News reports Hutchinson\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager and longtime confidante has resigned:\par \par \uc2 enltrNews: Asa Hutchinson campaign manager Rob Burgess is leaving campaign... tendered resignation last week, per person familiar... Burgess has been at former governor's side the whole race, a key confidant and political strategist... didn't see a viable path forward for Hutchinson\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1719021056801857789?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans who have gone against the former president have gotten nowhere in this presidential election cycle. Hutchinson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/30/trump-jan-6-ballots-court-biden-ai-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-653fab1a8f08b48bad7c4c3c#block-653fab1a8f08b48bad7c4c3c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polled at 1%}}}\uc2  in the NBC News survey released this morning, and over the weekend, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president and fell out with him over his attempts to overturn the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/28/mike-pence-suspends-campaign-for-republican-presidential-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended his presidential campaign}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, a federal judge reinstated a limited gag order on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , intended to prevent him from making statements maligning those involved in his prosecution for trying to overturn the 2020 election, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was once again bound by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/16/donald-trump-trial-court-gag-order-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the gag order in the federal criminal case}}}\uc2  charging him with conspiring to overturn the 2020 election results, after a judge on Sunday reinstated restrictions prohibiting him from attacking prosecutors, court staff and potential trial witnesses.\par \par \uc2 The US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  also denied {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former US president\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  request to suspend the gag order indefinitely while his lawyers appealed.\par \par \uc2 Trump had been granted a reprieve when the judge temporarily lifted the gag order while she considered that request. Prosecutors argued last week that the order should be reimposed after Trump took advantage and posted a slew of inflammatory statements.\par \par \uc2 The statements included Trump\u8217\'20\'19s repeated attacks on the special counsel Jack Smith, whom he called \u8220\'20\'1Cderanged\u8221\'20\'1D, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments about the testimony that his former White House chief of staff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mark-meadows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Meadows}}}\uc2  had provided to the grand jury during the criminal investigation.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors argued that each of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statements were exactly the sort of comments that the order was designed to prevent, including intimidating or influencing witnesses who could wind up testifying against him at trial, and weighing on the substance of their testimony.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendant has capitalized on the court\u8217\'20\'19s administrative stay to, among other prejudicial conduct, send an unmistakable and threatening message to a foreseeable witness in this case,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors said in their brief. \u8220\'20\'1CUnless the court lifts the administrative stay, the defendant will not stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/donald-trump-election-interference-case-gag-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge reinstates gag order in Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s federal election interference case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Colorado, a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  argued that efforts to remove him from the ballot rely on a faulty interpretation of the word \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 See his reasoning here:\par \par \uc2 enltrA lawyer argues before a Colorado judge that plaintiffs suing to block \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from appearing on the presidential ballot are using a shoddy definition of an insurrection:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey're making up the standard so that it fits the facts of January 6th.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u6e0o1u9iI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/u6e0o1u9iI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719013806020448727?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike is part of a larger wave of union activism in recent months that has seen laborers win significant concessions from employers. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/steven-greenhouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steven Greenhouse}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Call it the Great Reset. Across the US, labor unions are winning surprisingly large contract settlements as workers have reset their expectations to demand considerably more than they did just a few years ago, and that has in turn pressured many corporations to reset \u8211\'20\'13 and increase \u8211\'20\'13 the pay packages they are giving in union contracts.\par \par \uc2 The result has been a wave of impressive \u8211\'20\'13 sometimes eye-popping \u8211\'20\'13 union contracts over the past year, far more generous than in recent decades. In August, 15,000 \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  pilots won pay increases of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/21/business/american-airlines-pilots-union.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 46% over four years}}}\uc2 . In a huge labor confrontation last summer, 340,000 Teamster members at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/ups-teamsters-strike-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UPS won raises}}}\uc2  of $7.50 an hour over five years, with drivers\u8217\'20\'19 pay climbing to $49 an hour and part-time workers receiving a pay increase of 48% on average.\par \par \uc2 After a three-day strike earlier this month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/13/kaiser-permanente-unions-deal-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 85,000 Kaiser Permanente workers}}}\uc2  won raises of 21%, as well as a $25 minimum wage for Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s workers in California. In March, 30,000 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/education/los-angeles-schools-union-leaders-reach-deal-on-worker-pay-and-benefits-after-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles school district workers}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 bus drivers, cafeteria workers and teachers\u8217\'20\'19 aides \u8211\'20\'13 won a 30% wage hike over four years. In Oregon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nwlaborpress.org/2023/08/providence-settles-with-nurses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1,400 nurses at Providence Portland}}}\uc2  hospital secured raises between 17% and 27% over two years.\par \par \uc2 Union leaders and rank-and-file workers hailed these contracts as great and historic, but Thomas Kochan, a longtime professor of industrial relations at MIT, put it another way: \u8220\'20\'1CAll this reflects a a reset in expectations and wage norms for workers and for employers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese successes,\u8221\'20\'1D Kochan continued, \u8220\'20\'1Care a reflection of the workforce\u8217\'20\'19s strong expectations and the workforce\u8217\'20\'19s demands to make up for lost ground due to inflation \u8211\'20\'13 and to signal that times have changed. The modest wage increases of the past will no longer be adequate to deal with our situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/us-unions-successes-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US unions winning big gains amid \u8216\'20\'18Great Reset\u8217\'20\'19 in worker power}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden call \uc2 GM\uc2 , \uc2 UAW\uc2  deal 'great' as end of six-week autoworkers strike appears near\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and the United Autoworkers have reached an agreement on a new contract that would end the six-week strike against the Big Three Detroit carmakers.\par \par \uc2 In a brief comment to reporters, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called the development \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat\u8221\'20\'1D. He has made supporting unions a priority of his administration, and last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traveled to Michigan}}}\uc2  to stand with \uc2 UAW\uc2  picketers.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/michael-sainato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Sainato}}}\uc2  on the agreement:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 six-week strike against the US\u8217\'20\'19s three largest automakers appeared to be coming to an end on Monday as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/30/business/economy/gm-uaw-contract-deal.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union brokered a deal }}}\uc2  with \uc2 General Motors\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The agreement follows on the heels of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/ford-united-auto-workers-union-deal-strike-general-motors-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deals with Ford and Stellantis}}}\uc2 , brokered in the past few days, effectively ending the first simultaneous strike against the three Detroit automakers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/uaw-strike-expands-gm-texas-walkout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the largest}}}\uc2  by car workers in decades, and has proved an unusual political flashpoint, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/uaw-strike-biden-visit-update-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  supporting workers over the car companies.\par \par \uc2 Biden lauded the reported agreement reached with \uc2 GM\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s great,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, who has touted himself as pro-union.\par \par \uc2 After the union reached a tentative agreement with Ford last week, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  reached an agreement with similar contract terms on Saturday, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/generalmotors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 General Motors}}}\uc2  followed suit on Monday. The agreements include 25% wage increases for workers over the life of the contract and cost-of-living adjustments.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GM deal sets stage for end to UAW strike against three largest US carmakers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The first of what are expected to be five days of hearings in Colorado to determine if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can appear on the ballot there is kicking off, and Politico has some details of what we can expect today:\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: Litigants seeking to keep Trump off the ballot in Colorado are laying out what they describe as Trump's "drumbeat" of disinformation and signals to conspiracy theorists and violent rhetoric, while sowing false doubts about election results.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1718999985407021112?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAmong those they say will testify that what occurred was an "insurrection" and that Trump is disqualified from the ballot:\par \par \uc2 -MPD Officer Danny Hodges\par \par \uc2 -Rep. \uc2 Eric Swalwell\par \par \uc2 -Extremism and 14th amendment experts\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1718999987063832906?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Last year, Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington succeeded in removing a New Mexico county commissioner from office for his role in the January 6 insurrection \u8211\'20\'13 a success the liberal group is trying to repeat with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Colorado. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the 2022 case, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A New Mexico official was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizensforethics.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/D101CV202200473-griffin.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removed from elected office}}}\uc2  on Tuesday for his role in the January 6 siege on the US Capitol, marking the first time a politician has lost their job for their involvement in the attack.\par \par \uc2 Couy Griffin, one of three commissioners in Otero county in southern New Mexico, was immediately removed from his position and cannot hold elected office again, Francis Mathew, a district judge in Santa Fe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizensforethics.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/D101CV202200473-griffin.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in his ruling}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 14th amendment to the US constitution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitution.congress.gov/browse/amendment-14/section-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bars anyone}}}\uc2  who has participated in an insurrection from holding elected office. In June, Griffin was sentenced to 14 days in jail and a $3,000 (\u163\'00\'A32,604) fine for misdemeanor trespassing during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr Griffin\u8217\'20\'19s crossing of barricades to approach the Capitol were overt acts in support of the insurrection, as Griffin\u8217\'20\'19s presence closer to the Capitol building increased the insurrectionists\u8217\'20\'19 intimidation by number,\u8221\'20\'1D Mathew wrote in his ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CMr Griffin aided the insurrection even though he did not personally engage in violence. By joining the mob and trespassing on restricted Capitol grounds, Mr Griffin contributed to delaying Congress\u8217\'20\'19s election certification proceedings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Griffin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/06/politics/couy-griffin-new-mexico-january-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  he was \u8220\'20\'1Cshocked\u8221\'20\'1D at the ruling and accused Mathew of being \u8220\'20\'1Ctyrannical\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m shocked. Just shocked,\u8221\'20\'1D Griffin said. \u8220\'20\'1CI really did not feel like the state was going to move on me in such a way. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know where I go from here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/06/jan-6-new-mexico-couy-griffin-first-politician-removed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Mexico official first politician removed over January 6 attack}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Could \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  actually be booted off ballots in Colorado, Minnesota, and perhaps other states? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  took a look at the cases in August, and here\u8217\'20\'19s what he found:\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  fights a mountain of criminal charges, a separate battle over his eligibility to run for president in 2024 is fast emerging.\par \par \uc2 The US constitution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitution.congress.gov/browse/essay/artII-S1-C5-1/ALDE_00013692/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sets out just a handful}}}\uc2  of explicit requirements someone must meet to be the president. They must be at least 35 years old, a \u8220\'20\'1Cnatural-born\u8221\'20\'1D citizen, and a United States resident for at least 14 years. The constitution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitution.congress.gov/constitution/amendment-22/#:~:text=No%20person%20shall%20be%20elected,the%20President%20more%20than%20once."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  also bars }}}\uc2  someone who has served as president for two full terms from running again.\par \par \uc2 None of those requirements disqualify Trump, or anyone else charged with a crime, from running for federal office.\par \par \uc2 But one provision in the constitution, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitution.congress.gov/browse/amendment-14/section-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 section 3 of the 14th amendment}}}\uc2 , makes things more complicated. It says that no person who has taken an oath \u8220\'20\'1Cas an officer of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D can hold office if they \u8220\'20\'1Chave engaged in insurrection or rebellion against the same, or given aid or comfort to the enemies thereof\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That language disqualifies Trump from running for office because of his efforts to overturn the 2020 election, two prominent conservative scholars, William Baude of the \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2  and \uc2 Michael Stokes Paulsen\uc2  of the \uc2 University of St Thomas\uc2 , concluded in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://electionlawblog.org/?p=138062"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 much}}}\uc2  - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4532751"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussed article}}}\uc2  to be published the University of Pennsylvania Law Review.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/20/trump-disqualified-constitution-section-3-14th-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Could Trump be barred under the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18engaged in insurrection\u8217\'20\'19 clause?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sarah B Wallace, a district court judge in Denver, will spend the next five days weighing arguments over whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may stay on Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s presidential ballots, or be removed over his involvement in the January 6 insurrection, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.denverpost.com/2023/10/30/donald-trump-colorado-ballot-challenge-insurrection-trial/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Denver Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The case is a novel one, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling if Trump\u8217\'20\'19s enemies, represented by Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington, will succeed, or if the supreme court will ultimately end up deciding the case.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what we can expect this week, from the Denver Post:\par \par \uc2 A provision in the Civil War-era federal constitutional amendment bars people who engaged in insurrection or rebellion from holding office.\par \par \uc2 But there are key unresolved questions: Which actions meet that threshold? Who can enforce it? And what is the burden of proof necessary to bar someone from the ballot under that provision?\par \par \uc2 Those considerations will be heard by Denver District Court Judge Sarah B. Wallace.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t a frivolous lawsuit,\u8221\'20\'1D said Doug Spencer, a \uc2 University of Colorado\uc2  law professor. He sees a \u8220\'20\'1Ccredible argument\u8221\'20\'1D that the events of Jan. 6, 2021, in fact amounted to an insurrection, but he added that nothing is certain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe challenges, of course, are (that) when you\u8217\'20\'19re litigating, every little word and technicality really matters,\u8221\'20\'1D Spencer said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think there are some real challenges with the plaintiffs prevailing in court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The civil suit was brought by several former and current Colorado Republicans, including some who are now unaffiliated voters. It\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.denverpost.com/2023/09/06/colorado-voters-lawsuit-donald-trump-ballot-challenge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spearheaded by Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington}}}\uc2 , or CREW, a liberal watchdog group.\par \par \uc2 Among the 14th Amendment ballot challenges being pursued against Trump in other states are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/10/27/trump-14th-amendment-colorado-minnesota/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cases in Minnesota and Michigan}}}\uc2  assisted by another group, called Free Speech for People. The Minnesota Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/elections/2023/10/will-first-amendment-or-the-14th-prevail-in-case-over-donald-trumps-name-on-minnesotas-presidential-primary-ballot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is set to hear arguments}}}\uc2  in that state\u8217\'20\'19s case Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Colorado suit, at its core, targets Trump on the basis that he allegedly urged on the Capitol siege and tried to overturn the election he lost in 2020. But it does so by also suing Colorado Secretary of State \uc2 Jena Griswold\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 a Democrat who\u8217\'20\'19s forthright in her assessment that Trump did incite an insurrection \u8212\'20\'14 because her office supervises elections and certifies the statewide ballot, making her the official who\u8217\'20\'19d carry out any disqualification order.\par \par \uc2 Griswold first ran for her office in 2017 and has voiced concerns about threats to democracy during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency as a chief worry. But this case has put her in a position of taking a step back, at least as far as the nominal defendant can.\par \par \uc2 Her office isn\u8217\'20\'19t putting on the case or providing evidence, beyond what\u8217\'20\'19s asked of her and other officials. She sees the case as a way to ask the court for guidance when it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear if a candidate is qualified for the ballot, a legal action available to voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is a foundational case to one of the central tenets about the attack on democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Griswold said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CDid \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  disqualify himself by engaging in insurrection? That is what this case is about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If you missed it when it happened, here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joannawalters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanna Walters}}}\uc2  with the news that \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president, had decided to end his ailing presidential campaign, further winnowing the Republican field:\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former vice-president under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has suspended his campaign to become the Republican nominee for president in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 Pence announced at an event held by the Republican Jewish Coalition in Las Vegas on Saturday that he was dropping out of the race, in which he has been lagging, along with others, far behind frontrunner Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI came here to say it\u8217\'20\'19s become clear to me this is not my time, so after much prayer and deliberation I have decided to suspend my campaign for president, effective today,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-pence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pence}}}\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Pence, 64 and the former governor of his home state of Indiana, after representing it as one of its congressman, had been leading a struggling campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/12/mike-pence-tours-iowa-state-fair-in-search-of-votes-but-who-is-his-candidacy-aimed-at"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for a while}}}\uc2 . He had not yet qualified for the third {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/second-republican-debate-takeaways-ron-desantis-chris-christie-mike-pence-nikki-haley-vivek-ramaswamy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GOP debate}}}\uc2  on 8 November, falling short on required donations.\par \par \uc2 But his announcement on Saturday during an event attended by other prominent candidates for the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination next year, including Trump and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the governor of Florida, came as a surprise to most.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/28/mike-pence-suspends-campaign-for-republican-presidential-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence suspends campaign for Republican presidential nomination}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump maintains overwhelming lead for GOP nomination in new Iowa poll\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has led almost every poll of the Republican presidential field for months, and a new survey released today of Iowa, the first state to vote in the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination process, shows that has not changed:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew NBC/Des Moines Register/Mediacom IA GOP caucus poll (conducted 10/22-26):\par \par \uc2 Trump 43% (+1% from August poll)\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 16% (-3%)\par \par \uc2 Haley 16% (+10%)\par \par \uc2 Scott 7% (-2%\par \par \uc2 Christie 4% (-1%)\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy 4% (\u8212\'20\'14)\par \par \uc2 Burgum 3% (+1%)\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson 1% (+1)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Kornacki (@SteveKornacki) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SteveKornacki/status/1718930837582856218?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The poll was taken before \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president turned foe, dropped out this weekend, and shows the depth of the devotion to the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s cause:\par \par \uc2 enltr63% of Trump supporters say their minds are already made up and they'll definitely back him, suggesting a depth of support we just haven't seen before. The last GOP candidate w/ a lead this size at this point -G.W. Bush in late '99- had "definite" numbers 20-30 points below this.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Kornacki (@SteveKornacki) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SteveKornacki/status/1718954821472878758?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 At the start of the year, it seemed as though Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  would mount a strong challenge to Trump for the nomination, but his campaign has struggled to gain traction in recent months, and NBC\u8217\'20\'19s survey shows his weak popularity ebbing further. That said, he has somehow managed to be the most well-liked candidate, even if most respondents plan to vote for Trump:\par \par \uc2 enltrDespite his failure to move up overall, DeSantis remains *very* popular w/ IA GOP voters - the most-liked, in fact. Favorable/unfavorable scores:\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 69/26%\par \par \uc2 Trump 66/32%\par \par \uc2 Scott 61/22%\par \par \uc2 Haley 59/29%\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy 43/37%\par \par \uc2 Burgum 42/37%\par \par \uc2 Pence 32/65%\par \par \uc2 Christie 20/69%\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson 17/45%\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Kornacki (@SteveKornacki) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SteveKornacki/status/1718957937559789976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Courts to consider liberal groups' attempt to keep Trump from ballots over insurrection\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is steaming ahead with his presidential run despite all the obstacles in front of him, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particularly the four criminal indictments he is facing}}}\uc2 . But if liberal groups have their way, the former president will soon have another legal headache to deal with. This week, judges in two states will consider lawsuits to bar him from ballots for violating the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s insurrection clause by trying to overturn the 2020 election and sparking the January 6 attack on the US Capitol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-insurrection-ballot-14th-amendment-colorado-f5d6c6174476ec414208323785df6e15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 . Proceedings begin today in Colorado, and a judge will start hearing arguments Thursday in Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 It seems likely these suits will in some form make their way up to the supreme court, which is dominated by six conservative justices, half of whom were appointed by Trump. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what will happen then, and we are unlikely to find out anytime soon, but it is possible these cases could become yet another source of legal peril for the former president.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we are watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will at 2.30pm eastern time hold an event dedicated \u8220\'20\'1Cto advancing the safe, secure, and trustworthy development and use of Artificial Intelligence\u8221\'20\'1D. After that, he will be hosting trick-or-treaters at the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office is heavily promoting her interview with CBS News\u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes on Sunday evening, saying it demonstrates her \u8220\'20\'1Cinvaluable\u8221\'20\'1D leadership. You can watch it for yourself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/kamala-harris-interview-60-minutes-transcript/?ftag=CNM-00-10aab7d&linkId=244809495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 War continues in the Gaza Strip, and you can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/30/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-aid-trucks-enter-gaza-strikes-casualties-israel-targets-hit-syria-lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow our live blog}}}\uc2  for the latest developments.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231030ejau001xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
