\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden hails reported \uc2 UAW\uc2  deal with \uc2 General Motors\uc2  to end strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2023\par 20:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Six-week strike against three largest US carmakers appears to be coming to an end after union brokers agreement\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 six-week strike against the US\u8217\'20\'19s three largest automakers appeared to be coming to an end on Monday as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/30/business/economy/gm-uaw-contract-deal.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union brokered a deal }}}\uc2  with \uc2 General Motors\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The agreement follows on the heels of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/ford-united-auto-workers-union-deal-strike-general-motors-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deals with Ford and Stellantis}}}\uc2 , brokered in the past few days, effectively ending the first simultaneous strike against the three Detroit automakers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/uaw-strike-expands-gm-texas-walkout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the largest}}}\uc2  by car workers in decades, and has proved an unusual political flashpoint, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/uaw-strike-biden-visit-update-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  supporting workers over the car companies.\par \par \uc2 Biden lauded the reported agreement reached with GM. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s great,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, who has touted himself as pro-union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s historic agreement is yet another piece of good economic news, showing something I\u8217\'20\'19ve always believed: worker power is critical to building an economy from the middle out and the bottom up, and so is economic growth,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said during an event at the White House.\par \par \uc2 After the union reached a tentative agreement with Ford last week, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  reached an agreement with similar contract terms on Saturday, and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  followed suit on Monday. The agreements include 25% wage increases for workers over the life of the contract and cost-of-living adjustments.\par \par \uc2 The union also won shortened wage progression scales, ended lower-paying wage tiers, and secured the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wifr.com/2023/10/28/belvidere-stellantis-plant-reopen-with-new-model-following-uaw-agreement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reopening }}}\uc2  of \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plant in Belvidere, Illinois, which closed down earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, surprised the automakers in September when, rather than all workers represented by the union being called on to strike simultaneously, the union strategically announced \u8220\'20\'1Cstand-up\u8221\'20\'1D strikes at specific work sites to pressure the automakers to continue making progress in contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 At the peak of the strikes, 46,000 auto workers were on strike at all three car firms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe stand-up strike will go down in history as an inflection point for our union, and for our movement,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/uaw.union/posts/pfbid07waNzgytGwhjruKjbYCUhrXcpN84fLqHH7c2AJdjqHG78x76tKKtkbGYgmqwcmt2l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 livestream update}}}\uc2  on 29 October.\par \par \uc2 In the update on the tentative agreements reached with Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , Fain said the next contract expiration was set for 1 May 2028. He called on other unions to align their contract expirations with their own to build collective pressure on employers in the next round of union contracts.\par \par \uc2 Fain had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1713993846407733514"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously}}}\uc2  referred to workers at other auto companies including \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , \uc2 Toyota\uc2  and \uc2 Honda\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 UAW\uc2  members of the future\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/autos/detroit-is-paying-up-to-end-the-uaw-strike-now-carmakers-will-live-with-the-costs-df1d88d7?st=asn6221fxxfewkh&mod=googlenewsfeed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  on Sunday that the union\u8217\'20\'19s next efforts will aim at unionizing auto workers at US plants currently not represented by unions at companies such as \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , \uc2 Toyota\uc2  and \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important that we not only strike, but that we strike together,\u8221\'20\'1D added Fain.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231030ejau002bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
