\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 UAW\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  close to tentative agreement in Illinois\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 503 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 October 2023\par 01:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Negotiators will outline terms to local union officials on Saturday, including reopening automaker\u8217\'20\'19s Belvidere plant, sources say\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 reached a tentative labor deal with Chrysler owner \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  on Saturday, two sources said, moving closer to securing record wage hikes and a new life for a \uc2 Jeep\uc2  factory shut down earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The tentative deal is a big step towards ending the first simultaneous strike against the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CDetroit Three\u8221\'20\'1D automakers, and will follow a template {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/ford-united-auto-workers-union-deal-strike-general-motors-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set just days ago}}}\uc2  by \uc2 UAW\uc2  and Ford, including a 25% wage hike over the 4.5-year-long contract.\par \par \uc2 General Motors (GM) \uc2 and \uc2 UAW\uc2  negotiators reconvened on Saturday after working into the early hours of the morning, two people familiar with the situation said. \uc2 GM\uc2  has agreed to the same range of hikes and talks are focusing on other matters.\par \par \uc2 A public deal announcement with \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  is expected later on Saturday afternoon or early evening, the sources said. Strikes, which included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/uaw-strike-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic walkouts}}}\uc2 , have entered week seven.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  shuttered its assembly plant in Belvidere, Illinois, early this year, leaving 1,300 workers without jobs.\par \par \uc2 The factory closure, which became a rallying cry for the union\u8217\'20\'19s bargaining campaign, will reopen contingent on expected state and local tax incentives, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president, Shawn Fain, had vowed to reverse the closure. The Biden administration and the state of Illinois have offered subsidies that could help retool the factory. Illinois acquired 170 acres of land adjacent to the assembly plant.\par \par \uc2 The tentative contract deal will have provisions on the use of temporary workers, the sources said, adding \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  has agreed to significant investment.\par \par \uc2 Fain and other senior union leaders are briefing local \uc2 UAW\uc2  chiefs by video conference, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The deal is also expected to include investments in other US plants, including the Trenton engine plant, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The Trenton complex, located south of Detroit, built six-cylinder engines. Some of the facilities date back to 1952.\par \par \uc2 About 45,000 workers out of nearly 150,000 union members at the Detroit Three eventually joined the strike, which has cost billions of dollars to the industry.\par \par \uc2 Ford Motor Company\uc2  and the negotiators of the \uc2 UAW union{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/ford-united-auto-workers-union-deal-strike-general-motors-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached a labor deal}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, pending union leadership approval.\par \par \uc2 That deal was the first tentative settlement of strikes against Ford, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/generalmotors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 General Motors}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , which makes Chrysler and \uc2 Jeep\uc2  models.\par \par \uc2 More than 45,000 union members working at the Detroit three automakers have joined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/uaw-strike-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic walkouts}}}\uc2  that began on 15 September.\par \par \uc2 Fain repeatedly accused the Detroit Three automakers of enriching executives and investors while neglecting workers, and said the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s success would help blue-collar workers throughout the country.\par \par \uc2 The Detroit automakers argued that the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s demands would significantly raise costs and put them at a disadvantage compared with EV leader \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and foreign brands such as \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2 , which are non-unionized.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231028ejas001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
