\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans continue effort to erode US child labor rules despite teen deaths\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,382 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2023\par 18:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Violations have soared but legislative efforts to strengthen protection for young workers have received little support\par \par \uc2 Child labor violations have been soaring in the US, but efforts to render solutions through legislation have received little support, and Republicans at the state level continue pushing bills that would roll back current child labor protections.\par \par \uc2 In most recent fiscal year, the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  wage and hour division {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/data/charts/child-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  835 cases of child labor violations affecting 3,876 minors, and 688 minors employed in violation of hazardous occupation, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/florida-legislature-proposes-dangerous-roll-back-of-child-labor-protections-at-least-16-states-have-introduced-bills-putting-children-at-risk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 283%}}}\uc2  increase since 2015. Civil penalties against employers totaled just under $4.3m.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Labor has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/osec/osec20230227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed }}}\uc2  to ramp up enforcement against child labor and the exploitation of migrant child labor, but the wage and hour division remains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/worker-protection-agencies-need-more-funding-to-enforce-labor-laws-and-protect-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 too underfunded}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/press/new-report-finds-a-record-low-number-of-federal-wage-and-hour-investigations-of-farms-in-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 too understaffed}}}\uc2  to protect workers adequately.\par \par \uc2 At the state level, labor departments also saw sharp increases in child labor violations last year. A record number of employers were cited for child labor violations in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.king5.com/article/money/business/businesses-washington-child-labor-violations-2022/281-cd321f5a-4e65-47e9-95d4-3c47aae07a92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington}}}\uc2  and in New York, the state labor department reported a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dol.ny.gov/news/new-york-state-department-labor-launches-campaign-educating-young-workers-about-their-rights#:~:text=New%20York%20State%20saw%20464,sharp%20increase%20since%20the%20pandemic."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 68% increase}}}\uc2  in child labor violations in 2022.\par \par \uc2 This year, harrowing child labor violations were reported by officials, including three teens who were killed on the job during the summer.\par \par \uc2 In June, 16-year-old William Hampton was killed in Lee Summit, Missouri, while working at a recycling park when he was pinned between a semi-truck and a trailer. Osha, the \uc2 federal Occupational Safety and Health Administration\uc2 , is still {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.osha.gov/ords/imis/establishment.inspection_detail?id=1675654.015"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigating}}}\uc2  the incident.\par \par \uc2 Later that same month, 16-year-old Michael Schuls was killed at a sawmill in Wisconsin while operating hazardous machinery that was illegal for the worker to operate at that age. The same employer, Florence Hardwoods, was found in violation of numerous other child labor laws and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230907"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled }}}\uc2  a fine of $190,696 for the violations.\par \par \uc2 In August, 16-year-old Duvan Thomas Perez was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/16-year-old-boy-dies-accident-mississippi-poultry-plant-rcna94963"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed}}}\uc2  while working at a poultry plant in Mississippi, a job occupation illegal for under 18-year-olds to work due to hazardous conditions.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Department of Labor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20231013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  over $30,000 in fines against Win.IT America over child labor violations that included employing an 11-year-old and 13-year-old illegally at a Kentucky warehouse, where the children performed hazardous job duties that included operating a forklift and picking warehouse orders.\par \par \uc2 Several high-profile food service corporations have also faced fines over child labor violations in 2023, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/03/kentucky-mcdonalds-child-labor-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dc.eater.com/2023/8/29/23848960/chipotle-ordered-pay-dc-child-labor-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chipotle}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230928"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chick-fil-A}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sonic}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230316"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dunkin\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcboston.com/news/local/dave-busters-to-pay-275k-in-labor-violations-settlement-mass-ag-says/3064067/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dave & Buster\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230525-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Subway}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230103"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arby\u8217\'20\'19s,}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230208-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tropical Smoothie Cafe}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/05/18/popeyes-child-labor-violation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Popeye\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230421"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Zaxby\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , while corporations such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/23/us/tyson-perdue-child-labor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tyson Foods and Perdue Farms }}}\uc2  are currently under federal investigation for alleged child labor violations in their supply chains.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, workers held a rally outside of \uc2 Tyson Foods\uc2  headquarters in Springdale, Arkansas to protest against the lack of action from the company in response to child labor violations in its supply chain and broad issues of unsafe working conditions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe child labor really concerns me and other workers, because a child doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the capacity or power to prevent danger because of the bad working conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D said a worker at a \uc2 Tyson Foods\uc2  plant in Arkansas who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe dangers we go through, such as the chemicals, the fast line speeds \u8230\'20\'26 even this past week they rearranged some lines at the plant I work at where they want to cut positions, leaving less workers to do the work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Magaly Licolli, organizer of the rally and executive director of the non-profit Venceremos, said \uc2 Tyson Foods\uc2  has not provided any solutions to child labor problems within its supply chain. She said nor has it spoken up as the state of Arkansas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/local/nw-arkansas/2023/03/13/arkansas-roll-back-child-labor-protections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  legislation to roll back numerous child labor protections in March.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTyson keeps avoiding the subject by saying they are not hiring the kids, but the fact is kids are working within their supply chain, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how Tyson is tackling this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Licolli.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI speak with workers every day. Just recently a group of catchers at \uc2 Tyson\uc2  chicken farms came to us: two of them were minors from Guatemala, and they came to Venceremos because they were not paid, and forced to work 16 hours in one shift, and the contractor did not want to pay them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said that among workers there have been increasing reports of minors working as catchers in the chicken farm industry. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://beta.tiah.org/w/catcher"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Catchers}}}\uc2  are employees who catch, handle and load chickens on farms for transport. \uc2 Tyson Foods\uc2  did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tyson Foods\uc2  claim to be a family-owned company with strong family values. But where are those values when it comes to the workers that process their chicken or the products that they sell?\u8221\'20\'1D Licolli added.\par \par \uc2 Even as the US has reported recent surges in child labor violations, efforts to improve protections and enforcement have largely been disconnected along party lines.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats at the federal level have introduced legislation to improve child labor protections and increase monetary penalties on employers, but only two Republicans have co-sponsored bills introduced in the past year.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/2388/text?s=1&r=11&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  to increase civil penalties for child labor protections was introduced by Congresswoman Hillary Scholten in March, with seven co-sponsors, including one Republican.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Senators \uc2 Brian Schatz\uc2 , a Democrat, and \uc2 Todd Young\uc2 , a Republican, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/senate-bill/3051/cosponsors?s=1&r=1&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced }}}\uc2  a bill to amend the Fair Labor Standards Act to expand protections to independent contractors and increase fines for violations.\par \par \uc2 No Republicans have signed on to co-sponsor other bills introduced by Democrats this year, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/2956/actions?s=1&r=3&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Combating Child Labor Act}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/senate-bill/637?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D&s=2&r=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Child Labor Prevention Act}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/senate-bill/1288/actions?s=2&r=5&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Child Labor Exploitation Accountability Act}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/4020/text?s=1&r=12&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Children Don\u8217\'20\'19t Belong on Tobacco Farms Act}}}\uc2 , but have supported two bills aimed at rolling back current child labor protections.\par \par \uc2 The Republican congressman \uc2 Dusty Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/5274/cosponsors?s=1&r=14&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  a bill in August, the Teenagers Earning Everyday Skills Act, with three Republican co-sponsors. The legislation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dustyjohnson.house.gov/media/press-releases/johnson-introduces-bill-increase-teenager-workforce-participation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed }}}\uc2  by the \uc2 US Chamber of Commerce\uc2 , would expand working hours for children aged 14 to 16 while school is in session.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf a high school student can play in a football game until 9pm, or play video games late into the evening, they should also be allowed to hold a job if they wish to,\u8221\'20\'1D said Johnson in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dustyjohnson.house.gov/media/press-releases/johnson-introduces-teens-act-increase-youth-workforce-participation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 The Republican senator James Risch and and Democratic congressman Jared Golden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/1397/cosponsors?s=1&r=9&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced }}}\uc2  legislation to roll back child labor protections to permit 16- and 17-year-olds to work in the logging industry, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/senate-bill/671/cosponsors?s=1&r=8&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22child+labor%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support }}}\uc2  from four Republican senators, one independent senator (Angus King), and two Republican and two Democratic congressional representatives.\par \par \uc2 At the state level, Republicans have led efforts to roll back child labor protections, with bills introduced in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/florida-legislature-proposes-dangerous-roll-back-of-child-labor-protections-at-least-16-states-have-introduced-bills-putting-children-at-risk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 16 states}}}\uc2 . States including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/03/10/1162531885/arkansas-child-labor-law-under-16-years-old-sarah-huckabee-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkansas}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/26/politics/iowa-child-labor-law-kim-reynolds/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa }}}\uc2  have enacted laws to roll back child labor protections.\par \par \uc2 In September, Florida became the 16th state to introduce such a bill after Republican Linda Chaney supported eliminating all guidelines on work hour restrictions for 16- and 17-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Sherer, the director of the Economic Analysis and Research Network (Earn) State Worker Power Initiative, said the recent Florida bill was part of a broader trend to roll back child labor protections with regard to the number of hours young people can be scheduled to work by an employer, especially during the school year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose guidelines are connected to trying to ensure that every kid has the same opportunity for education,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sherer. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the restrictions are gone under the proposed bill and the other thing that has people scratching their heads a little bit is it changes the language for 14- and 15-year-olds, it changes the word \u8216\'20\'18shall\u8217\'20\'19 to \u8216\'20\'18may\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one we talked to is clear what this would mean, but it certainly raised a red flag. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear if legislators who authored the bill are also intending to make some of those hours\u8217\'20\'19 guidelines optional for employers for teens as young as 14.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sherer added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe push to roll back the standards in that sort of context very much looks like industry groups hoping to legalize violations that they know they\u8217\'20\'19re already committing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231020ejak001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
