\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Some Halloween costumes could break strike rules, US actors\u8217\'20\'19 union warns members\b0\par\par\uc2 Kelly Burke \par \uc2 439 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2023\par 10:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s advice is to eschew characters played by real people and instead take inspiration from animated TV shows not in its remit\par \par \uc2 Spiders are in but Spider-Man is out, after the US actors\u8217\'20\'19 union Sag-Aftra warned its members that dressing up as their favourite film or television characters this Halloween could break strike rules.\par \par \uc2 Now into its fourth month, the actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike shows no sign of resolution, after talks broke down again between Sag-Aftra and the body representing studios, networks and streaming services, the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ), on 11 October.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sagaftrastrike.org/post/halloween-guidance-from-sag-aftra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a guide to its 160,000 members}}}\uc2  to ensure they don\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cinadvertently break strike rules\u8221\'20\'1D on Halloween and \u8220\'20\'1Cpromote [studio] content without a fair contract\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChoose costumes inspired by generalised characters and figures (ghost, zombie, spider etc),\u8221\'20\'1D the guide advised, adding that members should not \u8220\'20\'1Cpost photos of costumes inspired by struck content on social media\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s advice follows a number of high-profile {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/gallery/celebrity-halloween-costumes-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celebrity Halloween parties in recent years,}}}\uc2  which have become major paparazzi and social media events due to the elaborate costumes worn by A-list Hollywood figures. Past events have featured the likes of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KimKardashian/status/1586603491417464834"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kim Kardashian in costume as X-Men\u8217\'20\'19s Mystique}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CkTvKo7Oke9/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lizzo as Marge Simpson}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CVtJta-vOkK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harry Styles as Dorothy from The Wizard of Oz.}}}\par \par \uc2 It is expected that the film character Barbie and TV character Wednesday Addams will be two of the most popular Halloween costumes this year, but the union is urging members to eschew characters played by real people and instead take inspiration from animated television shows, which are not included in Sag-Aftra\u8217\'20\'19s remit.\par \par \uc2 The union directive prompted Deadpool actor Ryan Reynolds to post on X: \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to screaming \u8216\'20\'18scab\u8217\'20\'19 at my 8 year old all night. She\u8217\'20\'19s not in the union but she needs to learn\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I look forward to screaming \u8220\'20\'1Cscab\u8221\'20\'1D at my 8 year old all night. She\u8217\'20\'19s not in the union but she needs to learn\u8212\'20\'14 Ryan Reynolds (@VancityReynolds) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VancityReynolds/status/1715099072418209809?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 On 11 October, \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  walked away from negotiations and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://press.amptp.org/node/19252"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  issued a statement }}}\uc2  saying the gap between the peak film industry trade association and the actors\u8217\'20\'19 union \u8220\'20\'1Cis too great\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cconversations are no longer moving us in a productive direction\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A major sticking point remains \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s push for a \u8220\'20\'1Cviewership bonus\u8221\'20\'1D, which \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  claims will place an \u8220\'20\'1Cuntenable economic burden\u8221\'20\'1D on the industry of more than $800m (\u163\'00\'A3659m, A$1.26bn) a year.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231020ejak0008g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
