\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US pharmacy workers strike over \u8216\'20\'18dangerous\u8217\'20\'19 workloads as CVS and \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  rake in profits\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,381 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2023\par 10:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pharmacists say increased workloads and cut hours are the perfect recipe for medication errors, which can be fatal\par \par \uc2 Pharmacists and support staff at some of the US\u8217\'20\'19s biggest drugstore chains say they are at a breaking point: as the companies take on more healthcare services, both staffing levels and hours have declined, and the pressure is too much, some say.\par \par \uc2 Angered by increasing workloads and cuts to their hours, workers have walked off the job.\par \par \uc2 Twelve CVS locations in the Kansas City, Missouri, area {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ca.sports.yahoo.com/news/12-kansas-city-area-cvs-210603006.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closed}}}\uc2  on 21 and 22 September after \u8220\'20\'1Cwildcat\u8221\'20\'1D strikes, which are organized by workers without union representation or support. \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  workers held their own wildcat strikes on 9-11 October at stores around the US, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/09/business/walgreens-walkouts-cvs-pharmacy/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  closures in Oregon, Arizona, Washington and Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis has been a decades-long issue, but it\u8217\'20\'19s really been compounded and exacerbated since the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D said a CVS pharmacist in California who asked to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CWith these added services, there hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been any added staffing to support the services, and there\u8217\'20\'19s been a reduction in staffing \u8211\'20\'13 so more work, less workers to do it. \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s all the ingredients for a prescription medication error to happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The pharmacist is an organizer with the grassroots campaign PizzaIsNotWorking. The campaign, started by the Oklahoma pharmacist Bled Tanoe, aims to highlight the plight of pharmacists and dismiss the idea that staff morale-boosters \u8211\'20\'13 like free pizza \u8211\'20\'13 can fix the situation.\par \par \uc2 Prescription errors can have serious, and even deadly, consequences. In early October, a patient at a CVS in Las Vegas was given the wrong medication, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.8newsnow.com/investigators/how-could-this-happen-prescription-incident-leads-to-termination-of-womans-in-vitro-fertilization/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading}}}\uc2  to the termination of their in vitro fertilization. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10204433/#:~:text=According%20to%20the%20Food%20and,patients%20per%20year%20%5B26%5D."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 100,000 prescription errors}}}\uc2  are reported to the Food and Drug Administration annually, but those are voluntarily reported. Between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7,000 and 9,000 people}}}\uc2  in the US die every year due to medication errors.\par \par \uc2 The California pharmacist detailed the numerous duties workers in retail pharmacies have to juggle: filling long queues of prescriptions; handling phone calls with physicians, doctor\u8217\'20\'19s offices and insurance companies; working the drive-through at pharmacies that have them; and, increasingly, handling vaccinations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPharmacists aren\u8217\'20\'19t asking for more pay. They\u8217\'20\'19re not asking for more vacation. They\u8217\'20\'19re asking for more staffing, so that they can do the job that they were hired to do, which is to help patients and maintain patient safety. And right now, they can\u8217\'20\'19t do that safely,\u8221\'20\'1D the pharmacist said.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s all the ingredients for a prescription medication error\par \par \uc2 CVS pharmacist\par \par \uc2 The Ohio Board of Pharmacy recently identified {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiocapitaljournal.com/2023/07/24/patient-harmed-1800-doses-of-controlled-drugs-lost-at-cvs-pharmacy-regulator-says/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 numerous issues}}}\uc2  resulting from severe understaffing at several CVS locations in the state, including missing controlled substances and prescription medication errors. Despite understaffing woes, CVS {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/payers/cvs-reports-double-digit-revenue-growth-2022-41b-profit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  double-digit revenue growth in 2022 and a profit of $4.1bn.\par \par \uc2 According to the 2019 National Pharmacist Workforce Study, 71% of respondents reported high or extremely high workloads, and job satisfaction was at the lowest point in 20 years. The 2021 survey found that workers at pharmacies were stressed to the point they could not fulfill all duties.\par \par \uc2 A former pharmacy intern at CVS in Arizona, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of reprisal from prospective employers, explained that their store was constantly understaffed and their shifts were cut from eight hours to six, with the same workload and no added staffing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe workloads have been perpetually increasing but without increased staffing. They add more to the plate without reducing the spread of the work, they add more to the workload, expect you to meet all the requirements for the workloads and then not add staff and in some cases reduce hours,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s hard because if you make a mistake, you\u8217\'20\'19re the one that gets held accountable, but they don\u8217\'20\'19t listen to the fact you\u8217\'20\'19re working by yourself or working as fast as you can to try to assist everyone you can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The result of complaints, they argued, was being told to cut corners, such as marking uncompleted computer-based tasks as \u8220\'20\'1Cdone\u8221\'20\'1D to keep from being reprimanded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes you\u8217\'20\'19d have to just kind of estimate the numbers because you didn\u8217\'20\'19t have enough time,\u8221\'20\'1D they added.\par \par \uc2 Pharmacists aren\u8217\'20\'19t asking for more pay. They\u8217\'20\'19re not asking for more vacation. They\u8217\'20\'19re asking for more staffing\par \par \uc2 Pharmacist in California\par \par \uc2 Andrea, who requested to omit her last name for fear of retaliation from prospective employers, worked as a pharmacist at CVS in Arizona for three years but quit on 1 October due to severe short-staffing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost of those days for the last several months, I would come in two hours early, work 12-hour shifts, and work through much of my lunch break in crazy working conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 As a pharmacist, she was paid as a salaried worker and received no overtime pay. She said she had to pick up extra workloads in recent months after experienced technicians left her store and those positions were not replaced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sykes-cpa.com/best-practices-for-pharmacists-compensation/#:~:text=Pharmacists%20may%20be%20exempt%20from,less%20than%20%24684%20per%20week."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 professional status}}}\uc2  because that just causes these workloads,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, in reference to the overtime exemptions for pharmacists because they are salaried. \u8220\'20\'1CThere was so much that fell on us, and insurance companies don\u8217\'20\'19t want to make it easy. When I\u8217\'20\'19m in these kinds of conditions and forced to play games with an insurance company, unfortunately I\u8217\'20\'19m so far behind I\u8217\'20\'19m just going to fill your scripts and get you out of there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shane Jeromski, a pharmacist in California who has worked at CVS and \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 , noted that retail chains have added immunization clinics to pharmacies, increasing revenue for the retailers but without adding staffing. He said pharmacy staff were becoming \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-pressure perfume salesmen\u8221\'20\'1D because of how much they were asked to push other services on to customers. He argued there should be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9067077/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national staffing}}}\uc2  ratio standards for pharmacy workers and their workloads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPharmacy technicians are grossly underpaid for their skill level. They are the frontline workers constantly dealing with patients who are usually not happy when they\u8217\'20\'19re in the pharmacy. They\u8217\'20\'19re sick or there are so many things that can go wrong that are out of our control, it\u8217\'20\'19s always like putting out fires,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeromski. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of technicians and pharmacists are being exploited by these companies by the level of work they have to do. They\u8217\'20\'19re not asking for more pay. They\u8217\'20\'19re asking for more help.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jeromski started a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gofundme.com/f/rux92-national-pharmacist-and-technician-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GoFundMe }}}\uc2  to support pharmacy workers who lost income due to the walkouts and to support any union organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American public needs to understand how dangerous this is for them to fill their prescriptions in an environment that is unsafe, no matter how good our healthcare system is in America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeromski.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for CVS did not provide specifics on how they plan to address pharmacist concerns, but said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re committed to providing access to consistent, safe, high-quality healthcare to the patients and communities we serve and are working with our pharmacists to directly address any concerns they may have. We\u8217\'20\'19re focused on developing a sustainable, scalable action plan to support both our pharmacists and our customers, that can be put in place in markets where support may be needed so we can continue delivering the high-quality care our patients depend on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  said the disruptions occurred at a small number of pharmacies and that the company was making significant investments in wages and bonuses to attract and retain workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe last few years have required an unprecedented effort from our team members, and we share their pride in this work \u8211\'20\'13 while recognizing it has been a very challenging time. We also understand the immense pressures felt across the US in retail pharmacy right now,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson wrote in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are engaged and listening to the concerns raised by some of our team members. We are committed to ensuring that our entire pharmacy team has the support and resources necessary to continue to provide the best care to our patients while taking care of their own wellbeing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231019ejaj00109\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
