\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s too much\u8217\'20\'19: Waffle House workers push for $25 an hour\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 944 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2023\par 14:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers in US south call for higher minimum wage and end to automatic meal deduction charges from paychecks in petition\par \par \uc2 Workers at several Waffle House locations in the southern US are among the latest group of employees in the US to hold walkouts around a slate of demands for improvements to wages and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://action.ussw.org/a/wafflehouse?utm_source=Social&utm_medium=Social&utm_campaign=Social&fbclid=IwAR2wcdEG2l033VgUm5uYrb2E9Tw08tdkX-skS-ZUOrMoMb_Ck4q3MvbjwIU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition}}}\uc2  circulating by the Union of Southern Service Workers, a worker organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ussw.org/faqs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2 , includes a push for a $25 hourly minimum wage at the huge restaurant chain that is often seen as an icon of working-class Americana.\par \par \uc2 Other demands include a call to end automatic meal deduction charges from worker paychecks and an increase for security and natural disaster plans as the chain has a reputation of remaining open during extreme weather events to such an extent that the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fema.gov/blog/its-little-piece-normal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Waffle House index}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D has been a long cited storm severity metric.\par \par \uc2 That index often generates considerable publicity during natural disasters but what the chain has long touted as a convenience for customers \u8211\'20\'13 keeping locations open 24 hours a day, seven days a week through storms and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/lifestyle/looking-waffle-house-christmas-morning-200200479.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 holidays}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is being described by workers as showing a lack of respect for the labor they do and the conditions theydo it at low wages.\par \par \uc2 Waffle House has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/profile/joe-rogers-jr/#:~:text=Joe%20Rogers%20Jr.%20is%20the,revenue%20of%20over%20%241%20billion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 2,100 locations}}}\uc2  in 25 states, with an estimated revenue of $1bn annually. Because the company is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wafflehouse.com/faq/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 privately held}}}\uc2 , financials are not publicly disclosed. The longtime chairman of Waffle House and son of one of the chain\u8217\'20\'19s founders has a net worth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/profile/joe-rogers-jr/?sh=41f56c163c8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated }}}\uc2  by Forbes at $1.7bn.\par \par \uc2 Gerald Green, a cook at Waffle House in Atlanta, Georgia for about seven years, has been involved with USSW since 2022 and participated in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@raiseupthesouth/video/7276505364894420254"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally}}}\uc2  in late September 2023 at his restaurant chain, where workers spoke up to put pressure on the chain to meet their demands.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing that got me involved in organizing at Waffle House is I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen things change over time. When I joined Waffle House, things weren\u8217\'20\'19t great at the beginning but they\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten progressively worse,\u8221\'20\'1D said Green. \u8220\'20\'1CAs time has moved on, it\u8217\'20\'19s become harder and harder to have a dignified life while working at Waffle House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted one of the issues affecting workers is they have meal deductions taken from their paycheck automatically to pay for meals one might get on a shift. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want that taken away. We\u8217\'20\'19re not even guaranteed to eat the food on the shift,\u8221\'20\'1D said Green.\par \par \uc2 He also cited issues with scheduling systems that are inconsistent and often incorrect, including former workers still getting scheduled, issues with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/augusta.news.2023/reels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 general cleanliness}}}\uc2 , and a lack of general respect for workers. As a cook, Green makes around $17 an hour, but many Waffle House workers work sub-minimum wages as servers, relying on tips.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWaffle House workers are the upper echelon of the hardest-working people I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever met in my life. A lot of people are struggling. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s too much to ask for people to have a dignified life when they\u8217\'20\'19re working so hard to get people meals,\u8221\'20\'1D Green added \u8220\'20\'1CPersonally, I\u8217\'20\'19ve had an injury to my foot six months ago. Realistically, I needed a month off to heal, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t have the time to do that because I have bills to pay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The USSW has posted numerous videos in recent months of Waffle House workers reaffirming the petition\u8217\'20\'19s demands and explaining the impact their low wages and poor working conditions has on them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a stressful environment,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ebbini, a Waffle House worker in Asheville, North Carolina, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@raiseupthesouth/video/7287661163733585183"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent video }}}\uc2  posted by the USSW. \u8220\'20\'1CI would like to get paid more. I get paid $10 an hour and then I\u8217\'20\'19m supposed to get tips, but nobody really tips like that at the Waffle House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vivian Wilson, another Waffle House worker in Asheville, North Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@raiseupthesouth/video/7285024719097679135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recounted }}}\uc2  at a workers\u8217\'20\'19 rally at her restaurant location that when she complained about sexual harassment from a customer to her manager, she was told to just deal with it.\par \par \uc2 Cheryl, a Waffle House worker in Durham, North Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@raiseupthesouth/video/7283215563252305195"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  receiving a T-shirt as part of Waffle House\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/waffle-house_rock-star-grill-operator-johnnie-celebrating-activity-6570333660862574592-5AaG/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 million-dollar club}}}\uc2  for cooks who served $1m worth of Waffle House food.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re peons in their million-dollar world,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey get richer, we get poorer, sicker, broken down, and they\u8217\'20\'19re taking vacations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 John Schuessler, a Waffle House worker in South Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@raiseupthesouth/video/7286161269806091551"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explained}}}\uc2  that due to the low wages, he struggles to afford groceries, clothes for his child, are behind on mortgage payments\par \par \uc2 Pauletta Dillard, a Waffle House server in South Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@raiseupthesouth/video/7285815466726001950"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the $3 an hour pay plus tips has been roughly the same pay for the past two decades, while more work is put on workers.\par \par \uc2 Workers also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@raiseupthesouth/video/7269459074616462623"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explained }}}\uc2  the security issues they face working the third shift, where customers are often intoxicated and violence in the restaurant between customers or directed at workers has occurred and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/waffle-house-fight-avengers-austin-b2332715.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  fights}}}\uc2  at the chain have often gone viral.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been through two robberies and had guns in my face,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jessica Gantt, a Waffle House worker in Columbia, South Carolina for 24 years {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/RaiseUptheSouth/videos/1009434763759769/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who went on strike}}}\uc2  over Summer 2023 with coworkers. \u8220\'20\'1CI definitely think they can do better than $16 an hour and I\u8217\'20\'19m almost 47 with a herniated disc in my back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Waffle House did not respond to multiple requests for comment on this story.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231016ejag0010a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
