\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  and unions reach deal after healthcare workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and agency \par \uc2 307 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 October 2023\par 15:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The strike, which ran for three days, marked the largest work stoppage to date in the healthcare sector\par \par \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s healthcare workers unions have reached a tentative agreement with the company, the union said in a social media post on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The California-based care consortium and the union representing healthcare workers resumed negotiations on Thursday, more than a week after contract talks broke off at the start of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/04/healthcare-worker-strike-kaiser-permanente"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 72-hour strike  }}}\uc2  by 75,000 nurses, medical technicians and support staff.\par \par \uc2 The strike, which ran for three days, marked the largest work stoppage to date in the healthcare sector.\par \par \uc2 The dispute was focused on workers\u8217\'20\'19 demands for better pay and measures to ease chronic staff shortages and high turnover that union officials say has undermined patient care at Kaiser, a leading nonprofit hospital network and managed-care organization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA big moment for Kaiser workers! Strikes work. When working people demand to be heard, bosses have no choice but to come to the table!\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Mary Kay Henry\uc2  , president of \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  , which represents many of the workers at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MaryKayHenry/status/1712834650559684739"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X.  }}}\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 Details of the agreement have yet to be announced by the unions.\par \par \uc2 The workers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/kaiser-permanente-healthcare-strike-hospital-union-california-washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represented  }}}\uc2  by the Coalition of Kaiser Permanente Unions, were bargaining for new union contracts after their current contracts expired on 1 October. Workers demanded significant wage increases and substantive improvements to what they say has been severe understaffing in healthcare facilities that worsened throughout the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The strike hit the non-profit private healthcare provider\u8217\'20\'19s operations in California, Oregon, Washington, Colorado, Virginia and Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Unions pointed to \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s recent profits of $3bn in the first half of 2023 and decried exorbitant salaries of executives.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231013ejad001xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
