\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Amazon\uc2  staff in Coventry to strike for four days including Black Friday\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Butler \par \uc2 588 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2023\par 15:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 31\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 GMB union\uc2  says online retailer\u8217\'20\'19s planned wage rise is little comfort to staff facing \u8216\'20\'18poverty pay\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 More than 1,000 \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers at the online retailer\u8217\'20\'19s Coventry warehouse are to go on strike for four days next month, including on the busy Black Friday sales day.\par \par \uc2 The action was announced as the \uc2 GMB union\uc2  said the company \u8220\'20\'1Cmust urgently reconsider its priorities\u8221\'20\'1D, denouncing a planned pay rise for UK workers announced this week as \u8220\'20\'1Clittle comfort to the thousands of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers facing poverty pay, unsafe working conditions and workplace surveillance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The strikes will take place on 7, 8 and 9 November, and on 24 November \u8211\'20\'13 which is Black Friday, the online shopping bonanza.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said on Monday that minimum starting pay for warehouse workers would rise to \u163\'00\'A311.80 an hour, from \u163\'00\'A311 an hour, on 15 October and then increase again to a minimum \u163\'00\'A312.30 an hour in April.\par \par \uc2 The next level of workers, who receive \u163\'00\'A312 an hour, will get a pay rise of 50p next week and then an increase to \u163\'00\'A313 an hour in April \u8211\'20\'13 giving a minimum pay rise across hourly paid workers of \u163\'00\'A31 an hour by the spring.\par \par \uc2 The company said the increase would cost it \u163\'00\'A3170m and mean \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s minimum starting pay would have risen by 20% in two years, as it tries to attract 15,000 seasonal workers to help pick and pack Christmas presents.\par \par \uc2 The Amazon UK country manager, \uc2 John Boumphrey\uc2 , said the company was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud to offer [staff] competitive wages and benefits, as well as fantastic opportunities for career development, all in a safe and modern work environment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, Rachel Fagan, a GMB organiser, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our members\u8217\'20\'19 response to the failure of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  bosses to listen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fagan said the latest strike plans would bring the total number of days lost to industrial action at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Coventry warehouse to nearly 30.\par \par \uc2 In January, workers at the site \u8211\'20\'13 who have complained that they have been treated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jul/29/to-them-we-are-like-robots-inside-story-of-a-strike-at-amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Clike robots\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 began a strike, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jan/25/first-uk-industrial-action-against-amazon-is-making-an-impact-says-gmb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first time}}}\uc2  the corporation has faced industrial action in the UK.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an unprecedented and historic moment with low-paid workers taking on one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful corporations,\u8221\'20\'1D Fagan said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCoventry is the beating heart of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s distribution network; strike action here on Black Friday will ripple throughout the company\u8217\'20\'19s UK logistics. As Black Friday looms, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  must urgently reconsider their priorities or risk strike action causing widespread disruption to customers and the public.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strike action has been announced before a gathering of workers, unions, regulators, policymakers and campaigners from at least 20 countries in Manchester later this month. They plan to coordinate action to challenge \uc2 Amazon\uc2  on its treatment of workers, communities and the environment.\par \par \uc2 The first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://makeamazonpay.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Make Amazon Pay}}}\uc2  summit on 27 and 28 October is being co-convened by \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2 , a federation of unions, and activists\u8217\'20\'19 alliance \uc2 Progressive International\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The agenda will include discussions on subjects such as the warehouse worker protection legislation in the US, Barcelona\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cities-today.com/barcelona-to-impose-public-space-tax-on-delivery-firms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon tax}}}\uc2  and Spain\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/jul/30/deliveroo-unveils-plans-to-pull-out-of-spain-in-wake-of-rider-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 riders\u8217\'20\'19 law}}}\uc2 , as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/sep/26/amazon-ftc-price-inflation-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the antitrust case}}}\uc2  recently filed by the \uc2 US Federal Trade Commission\uc2  and legislation such as the EU\u8217\'20\'19s digital markets act.\par \par \uc2 Confirmed participants include Yolanda D\u237\'00\'EDaz, Spain\u8217\'20\'19s labour minister, the US senator Bernie Sanders, Paul Nowak, the general secretary of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Trades Union Congress, and Sharon Graham, the general secretary of \uc2 Unite\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231010ejaa001mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
