\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Our strike is working\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 UAW\uc2  announces progress in talks with car giants\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 568 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2023\par 20:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain says \uc2 General Motors\uc2  has made key concession on battery manufacture and does not announce additional strikes\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  has claimed its strike against the big three US automakers is working, as it announced \uc2 General Motors\uc2  had made concessions during talks.\par \par \uc2 As the strike strike enters its fourth week, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  trailed \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaking developments\u8221\'20\'1D at the negotiating table before a briefing on Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain, wearing a shirt with the slogan \u8220\'20\'1CEat the Rich\u8221\'20\'1D, started a livestream with the announcement that the threat of a strike against \uc2 GM\uc2  has led to an agreement for the company to place its electrical-battery manufacturing under the national master agreement with the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 GM\uc2  has been falling behind. Today, under the threat of a major financial hit, they leapfrogged the pack in terms of a just transition,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain. \u8220\'20\'1COur strike is working, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not there yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIn just three weeks, we have moved these companies further than anyone thought possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ford is ahead of \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  on their wage offers to the union, Fain said. He added that Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  have agreed to reinstate a cost-of-living allowance. This was lost as part of concessions made to help the industry out of the 2008 economic recession, and had yet to be reinstated.\par \par \uc2 Fain and autoworkers have positioned the strikes as a broader fight against corporate greed. They have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MikeLevin/status/1709952396011724928"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed }}}\uc2  by Democratic elected officials, who argue workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages are lagging behind exorbitant executive pay and billions of dollars in corporate profits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe billionaires and company executives think we autoworkers are just dumb. They think we don\u8217\'20\'19t get it. They think we only understand the power of a supervisor yelling at us, or an assembly line coming at us,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain. \u8220\'20\'1CWe expect results at every company, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve been crystal clear about how you catch a strike and how you avoid one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the livestream, Fain did not announce any additional strikes to the 25,000 workers currently on strike.\par \par \uc2 About 13,000 auto workers at a \uc2 General Motors\uc2  plant in Wentzville, Missouri, a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  plant in Toledo, Ohio, and a Ford plant in Wayne, Michigan kicked off the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CStand Up\u8221\'20\'1D strike against the automakers on 15 September.\par \par \uc2 The strategy is meant to keep the corporations guessing as the union continues to increase the pressure over demands for substantial wage increases. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is also calling for 2008 concessions \u8211\'20\'13 such as cost of-living adjustment increases, retirement pensions and elimination of lower-wage tiers \u8211\'20\'13 to be reinstated.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  expanded its strike on 22 September to 38 parts and distribution sites in 20 states at \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , forgoing escalations at Ford, where the contract talks have progressed further than the other two automakers.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Joe Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2  the \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket line in Michigan, become the first sitting president ever to do so.\par \par \uc2 The strikes have become heated at times, with violence erupting toward picketing workers, including a driver {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wane.com/top-stories/uaw-president-asks-public-to-join-picket-lines-calls-out-gm-stellantis-for-using-scabs/#:~:text=(WANE)%20UAW%20President%20Shawn%20Fain,members%20on%20the%20picket%20lines."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hitting}}}\uc2  five people on a picket line in Flint.\par \par \uc2 Last week the \uc2 UAW\uc2  expanded the strike with the addition of Ford\u8217\'20\'19s Chicago assembly plant and a \uc2 GM\uc2  plant in Lansing, Michigan. Action at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  was not escalated last week due to progress made in talks.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231006eja6002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
