\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Zelenskiy says deadly village missile attack was \u8216\'20\'18no blind strike\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now); Maya Yang, Charlie Moloney, Tom Ambrose and Helen Sullivan (earlier) \par \uc2 10,975 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2023\par 17:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read the latest Ukraine coverage here.Russia-Ukraine war: what we know at a glance\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s just past midnight in Kyiv. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where we stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 51 people including a six-year-old boy were killed during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/russian-attack-village-cafe-kills-people-ukraine-hroza-kharkiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a missile attack}}}\uc2  on a cafe during a wake service in a village of Hroza in the Kharkiv region on Thursday, according to Ukrainian officials. According to preliminary findings, the Russians targeted the cafe with an Iskander ballistic missile, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s minister of internal affairs, Ihor Klymenko, said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , accused Russia of \u8220\'20\'1Cbrutal\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocidal aggression\u8221\'20\'1D after the missile attack in the village of Hroza, in the Kupiansky district of the north-eastern Kharkiv province. He described it as \u8220\'20\'1Ca demonstrably brutal Russian crime \u8211\'20\'13 a rocket attack on an ordinary grocery store, a completely deliberate act of terrorism\u8221\'20\'1D, later saying it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-uk-russia-mining-black-sea?page=with:block-651f10d28f0880e74add64b0#block-651f10d28f0880e74add64b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cno blind strike\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 European leaders rallied around the Ukrainian president in the face of US jitters over defence funding. The gathering at the European Political Community (EPC) summit in Granada, Spain, gave leaders including the French president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-uk-russia-mining-black-sea?page=with:block-651edc8b8f0880e74add6198#block-651edc8b8f0880e74add6198"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the German chancellor,}}}\uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-uk-russia-mining-black-sea?page=with:block-651efec48f0880e74add63d8#block-651efec48f0880e74add63d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the British prime minister,}}}\uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 , a chance to restate their commitment to Ukraine after political turbulence in the US and Europe raised questions about continued support.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Slovakia will not send more military aid to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  for now, prime minister Ludov\u237\'00\'EDt \u211\'00\'D3dor said. Instead, the decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-uk-russia-mining-black-sea?page=with:block-651f217e8f08297bb34227c7#block-651f217e8f08297bb34227c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  will be delayed}}}\uc2  until a new government is formed following last week\u8217\'20\'19s election, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/02/who-is-robert-fico-the-pro-russian-leader-poised-to-head-slovakias-coalition-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saw a victory}}}\uc2  for \uc2 Robert Fico\uc2 , a populist, pro-Russian three-time former prime minister who campaigned on a promise to end military aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , wants to give a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-uk-russia-mining-black-sea?page=with:block-651f1c238f0880e74add6518#block-651f1c238f0880e74add6518"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor\u8221\'20\'1D speech}}}\uc2  on support for Ukraine, the White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said, without specifying when that would happen. She described the Hroza missile attack as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-uk-russia-mining-black-sea?page=with:block-651f06128f0880e74add6422#block-651f06128f0880e74add6422"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chorrifying\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ramped up his nuclear rhetoric, saying his country had successfully tested the nuclear-powered, nuclear-capable Burevestnik strategic cruise missile, as he suggested Russia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/vladimir-putin-escalates-nuclear-rhetoric-with-threat-to-resume-testing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could resume nuclear testing }}}\uc2  for the first time in more than three decades.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Putin also suggested that the plane crash that killed Wagner mercenary chief \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2  in August was caused by hand grenadesdetonating inside the aircraft, not by a missile attack. \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-uk-russia-mining-black-sea?page=with:block-651ef7948f08584119dd07f8#block-651ef7948f08584119dd07f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fragments of hand grenades}}}\uc2  were found in the bodies of those killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/27/wagner-boss-yevgeny-prigozhin-killed-in-plane-crash-russia-investigative-committee-confirms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in the crash}}}\uc2 . There was no external impact on the plane \u8211\'20\'13 this is already an established fact,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, and the Russia-Ukraine war blog today. Thank you for following, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be back tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Slovakia freezes military aid for Ukraine after pro-Russian election win\par \par \uc2 Slovakia will not send more military aid to Ukraine for now, prime minister Ludov\u237\'00\'EDt \u211\'00\'D3dor said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the decision will be delayed until a new government is formed following last week\u8217\'20\'19s election, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Slovakia\u8217\'20\'19s president has asked \uc2 Robert Fico\uc2 , a populist, pro-Russian three-time former prime minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/02/who-is-robert-fico-the-pro-russian-leader-poised-to-head-slovakias-coalition-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who campaigned }}}\uc2  on a promise to end military aid to Ukraine, to try to form a coalition government after his party came top in weekend elections.\par \par \uc2 Before falling apart last year, the country\u8217\'20\'19s previous government was a staunch backer of Ukraine, donating arms, including its fleet of Soviet-era MiG-29 fighter jets.\par \par \uc2 But Fico has vowed to withdraw Slovakia\u8217\'20\'19s military support for Ukraine, and his pro-Moscow stance has sparked fears Slovakia will join Hungary and its authoritarian leader \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  in challenging the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s consensus on support for Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the sidelines of an EU summit in Granada, \u211\'00\'D3dor said his administration would leave the question of more military aid to the next government. He added:\par \par \uc2 In what form will depend on the government, but I do not think that, at the least, anyone will stop the commercial part of aid.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to deliver 'major' speech on Ukraine support, says White House\par \par \uc2 The US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , wants to give a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor\u8221\'20\'1D speech on support for Ukraine, the White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said during her briefing today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants to give a major speech on this,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said, without specifying when that would happen. She added:\par \par \uc2 We are going to continue to make sure that we meet the battlefield needs that Ukraine has, using existing resources and using those resources provided by Congress.\par \par \uc2 Biden on Wednesday said he would deliver a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor\u8221\'20\'1D speech about funding for Ukraine and \u8220\'20\'1Cwhy it\u8217\'20\'19s critically important for the United States and our allies that we keep our commitment\u8221\'20\'1D, in response to an NBC question.\par \par \uc2 He told reporters:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to make the argument that it\u8217\'20\'19s overwhelmingly in the interest of the United States of America that Ukraine succeed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is considering using US state department grants to send additional military aid to Ukraine, according to a Politico report.\par \par \uc2 The White House is weighing a range of options as it scrambles to find funds after Congress on Saturday approved a last-minute spending bill that did not include the $6bn in military assistance that Ukraine said it urgently needed.\par \par \uc2 The administration has warned for weeks that funds allocated for aid to the Ukrainian war effort have nearly been exhausted.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is another means by which we may be able to find funding for that\u8221\'20\'1D but did not elaborate.\par \par \uc2 The report states:\par \par \uc2 One option under consideration is using foreign military financing \u8212\'20\'14 a program run by the State Department that provides grants or loans to help partner countries purchase weapons and defense equipment \u8212\'20\'14 intended for Ukraine and other countries impacted by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s full-scale invasion, said the two officials.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US ambassador to Ukraine, \uc2 Bridget Brink\uc2 , has called the Hroza strikes \u8220\'20\'1Cbarbaric acts of violence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet on Thursday, Brink echoed White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s condemnation of the strikes on the village cafe as \u8220\'20\'1Chorrifying\u8221\'20\'1D and said:\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s horrific attack today on a village store in Hroza has killed over 50 civilians, including a 6 year old child. We will support Ukraine in holding Russia accountable for such barbaric acts of violence.\par \par \uc2 enltrRussia\u8217\'20\'19s horrific attack today on a village store in Hroza has killed over 50 civilians, including a 6 year old child. We will support Ukraine in holding Russia accountable for such barbaric acts of violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ambassador \uc2 Bridget A. Brink\uc2  (@USAmbKyiv) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USAmbKyiv/status/1709991783386505648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  says Hroza attack was 'no blind strike'\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  condemned the Russian missile attack in Hroza on Thursday, saying that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cno blind strike\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA deliberate missile strike on a village in Kharkiv region on an ordinary store and cafe,\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy said while attending the European Political Community in Granada, Spain, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Russian troops could not have been unaware of where they were hitting. This was no blind strike,\u8217\'20\'19 he said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier at the summit, Zelenskiy warned that other European countries will be at risk if Russia wins the war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to win in Ukraine so that Putin cannot scale this aggression to someone, someone else, and it is realistic. That\u8217\'20\'19s why the key things are our unity, the unity and solidarity of all of Europe must be unwavering,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  high commissioner for human rights has condemned the attack on the village of Hroza that killed at least 51 people\par \par \uc2 Volker T \u252\'00\'FCrk said that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cshocked and saddened by today\u8217\'20\'19s attack \u8211\'20\'13 one of the deadliest in 20 months \u8211\'20\'13 which struck the village of Hroza in Kharkiv region\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDozens dead, including a child. Our human rights monitors will visit the site to gather information. Accountability is key,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/volker_turk?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @volker_turk}}}\uc2  shocked and saddened by today\u8217\'20\'19s attack \u8211\'20\'13 one of the deadliest in 20 months \u8211\'20\'13 which struck the village of Hroza in Kharkiv region. Dozens dead, including a child. Our human rights monitors will visit the site to gather information. Accountability is key.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 UN Human Rights (@UNHumanRights) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UNHumanRights/status/1709975552818364615?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has called Canada\u8217\'20\'19s former parliament speaker an \u8220\'20\'1Cidiot\u8221\'20\'1D after the parliament gave a standing ovation to a veteran who fought in Ukraine with a Nazi military unit that has been accused of war crimes\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the speaker of the Canadian parliament says that during World War II this Canadian-Ukrainian or Ukrainian-Canadian Nazi fought against the Russians, he cannot help but understand that he fought on the side of Hitler,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin said, Agence France-Presse reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s assume he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know this,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin added, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CBut if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know that Hitler and his minions fought against Russia during the war, then he\u8217\'20\'19s an idiot. It means he just didn\u8217\'20\'19t go to school.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt looked absolutely disgusting that everyone applauded this Nazi, especially the president of Ukraine, who has Jewish blood in his veins,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin said.\par \par \uc2 Following the incident, which occurred during the Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Canada last month, the Canadian prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  apologized, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a horrendous violation of the memory of the millions of people who died in the Holocaust.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says missile attack on Kharkiv village cafe is 'horrifying'\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , described the missile attack that hit a cafe in the village of Hroza in the Kharkiv region as \u8220\'20\'1Chorrifying\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking during her briefing with reporters, she said the attack was \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly horrifying for the people of Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what is happening in Ukraine every day,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  calls the Russian air strike today in Ukraine "horrifying."\par \par \uc2 At least 51 people died when a missile hit a shop and cafe in the small village of Hroza, home to just a few hundred residents. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QYEclXw6pC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QYEclXw6pC}}}\par \par \uc2 ?? \uc2 Sky\uc2  501 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nePf6jg0md"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nePf6jg0md}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sky News (@SkyNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SkyNews/status/1709986802868642057?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , has posted a video showing his meeting this afternoon with the British prime minister, \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The pair were seen embracing as they met at the European Political Community summit in Granada in southern Spain.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters after the meeting, Sunak said they discussed the \u8220\'20\'1Chorrific\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/russian-attack-village-cafe-kills-people-ukraine-hroza-kharkiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  attack in}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/russian-attack-village-cafe-kills-people-ukraine-hroza-kharkiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hroza}}}\uc2 , which he said \u8220\'20\'1Cillustrates Russia\u8217\'20\'19s barbarity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrDuring our meeting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RishiSunak?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RishiSunak}}}\uc2  and I discussed efforts to secure lasting global support for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine and the UK will continue and expand defense cooperation.\par \par \uc2 We also discussed grain export routes and agreed on the need to protect freedom of navigation in the Black Sea. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4EmLs976JK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4EmLs976JK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1709974567182074192?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Rescue Committee\uc2  has released a statement condemning the missile attack in Hroza earlier today\par \par \uc2 At least 51 people were killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/russian-attack-village-cafe-kills-people-ukraine-hroza-kharkiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the attack}}}\uc2 , including a six-year-old boy, Ukrainian officials said. President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  has described it as \u8220\'20\'1Ca demonstrably brutal Russian crime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Targeting civilians \u8220\'20\'1Cgoes against the principles of humanity\u8221\'20\'1D, the IRC\u8217\'20\'19s Ukraine country director, Marysia Zapasnik, said.\par \par \uc2 The IRC said it had witnessed an increased number of attacks on critical infrastructure, even in places that had previously been considered relatively safe. \u8220\'20\'1CIntense shelling and deaths caused by landmines and other unexploded ordnance are now a daily reality,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 As temperatures plummet, Ukraine will likely suffer from intensified barrages of missile strikes, and a more widespread destruction. The combination of ongoing conflict, destroyed infrastructure, and harsh weather conditions can make life incredibly tough for the people in affected areas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 A summary of today's developments as our evening coverage begins\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fragments of hand grenades were found in the bodies of the victims of a plane crash in August that killed the former \uc2 Wagner group\uc2  mercenary chief \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2 , \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 German police and customs officers on Thursday searched several properties in southern Germany, which a source familiar with the matter told Reuters belonged to a Russian national targeted by \uc2 European Union\uc2  sanctions over Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Putin said on Thursday that Russia had successfully tested a potent new strategic missile and declined to rule out the possibility it could carry out weapons tests involving nuclear explosions for the first time in more than three decades.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Russian missile struck a cafe and grocery store in a village in north-eastern Ukraine on Thursday, killing at least 51 people as they held a memorial service, Ukrainian officials said, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , told more than 40 European leaders gathered in Spain he was confident of the US\u8217\'20\'19s continued support, and asked for their continued assistance and more arms to help him fight against Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Spain has offered new air defense and anti-drone systems to Ukraine to protect its energy and port infrastructures, a government source told Reuters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , on Thursday suggested that the plane crash that killed the Wagner mercenary chief, \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2 , in August was caused by hand grenades detonating inside the aircraft, not by a missile attack.\par \par \uc2 The private Embraer jet on which Prigozhin was travelling to St Petersburg crashed north of Moscow on 23 August, killing all 10 people onboard, including two other top Wagner figures, Prigozhin\u8217\'20\'19s four bodyguards and a crew of three.\par \par \uc2 Putin suggested the plane was blown up from inside, saying that the head of \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s investigative committee\uc2  had reported to him a few days ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFragments of hand grenades were found in the bodies of those killed in the crash,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin told a meeting of the Valdai Discussion Club in the Black Sea resort of Sochi.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere was no external impact on the plane \u8211\'20\'13 this is already an established fact,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin said, seemingly rubbishing assertions by unidentified US officials who said shortly after the crash that they believed it had been shot down.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  speaking at the annual meeting of the Valdai Discussion Club in the Black Sea resort of Sochi on Thursday. Photograph: Sergei Guneyev/AP\par \par \uc2 Putin did not give any more details about how a grenade or grenades could have been detonated, but said he thought investigators were wrong to not have carried out alcohol and drug tests on the bodies of those who died in the crash given that quantities of cocaine had been found at Wagner\u8217\'20\'19s office in St Petersburg in the past.\par \par \uc2 The investigators of the crash have yet to report publicly on the cause.\par \par \uc2 Prigozhin\u8217\'20\'19s mutiny posed the biggest challenge to Putin\u8217\'20\'19s rule since the former KGB spy came to power in 1999. Western diplomats say it exposed the strains on Russia of the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Putin says fragments of hand grenades found in remains of plane crash that killed Wagner chief Prigozhin\par \par \uc2 Fragments of hand grenades were found in the bodies of the victims of a plane crash in August that killed the former \uc2 Wagner group\uc2  mercenary chief \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2 , \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The crash in August came two months after Prigozhin\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/24/after-yevgeny-prigozhins-death-many-ask-how-he-survived-for-so-long"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 short-lived mutiny}}}\uc2  in which Wagner troops captured a defence headquarters in Rostov and marched on Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Suspicions swiftly centred on the Russian president, with US and western officials saying it was very likely he was the architect of the incident, as Prigozhin\u8217\'20\'19s armed revolt had ranked as the most serious challenge to the Russian leader in his 23-year hold on power.\par \par \uc2 More details soon \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The UK prime minister, \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 , said he had discussed with the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , an attack in Ukraine on Thursday that Kyiv said was a Russian missile strike leaving 51 people dead.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe discussed this horrific attack that has just happened. It just illustrates Russia\u8217\'20\'19s barbarity,\u8221\'20\'1D Sunak told reporters after a meeting with Zelenskiy at a summit of the European Political Community in Spain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Russian] president Putin can say all he likes. There is one person responsible for this illegal unprovoked war, and it is him \u8230\'20\'26 That\u8217\'20\'19s why the UK has been steadfast in supporting Ukraine and will continue to do so,\u8221\'20\'1D Sunak added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sanctioned Russian oligarch at center of German police raid named\par \par \uc2 German police and customs officers on Thursday searched several properties in southern Germany, which a source familiar with the matter told Reuters belonged to a Russian national hit by \uc2 European Union\uc2  sanctions over Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The source said Russian oligarch \uc2 Alisher Usmanov\uc2  was the target of the operation, a Russian-Uzbek businessman who was sanctioned after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere can be no reason for suspicion against Mr Usmanov, who has always duly declared the personal property that was lawfully acquired by him, in addition to disclosing the funds with which he acquired these assets,\u8221\'20\'1D said a spokesperson for Usmanov in response to a Reuters\u8217\'20\'19 request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson added that Usmanov was not the owner of the trust he founded and had no right to control or manage its assets. \u8220\'20\'1CAs such, he has no way of knowing what is currently happening to the property owned by the trust.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A special commission labelled \u8220\'20\'1CMatryoshka\u8221\'20\'1D, set up by the German customs authority\u8217\'20\'19s sanctions office, said in a statement that officers searched properties in greater Munich and Tegernsee in Bavaria.\par \par \uc2 In September 2022, German police searched Usmanov\u8217\'20\'19s villa in the upmarket holiday town of Rottach-Egern on the shores of Lake Tegernsee. A court later deemed the raids unlawful.\par \par \uc2 The German customs authority\u8217\'20\'19s special commission said it was acting on court search warrants. It said it could not give further details on the operation for tactical reasons.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was updated on 6 October 2023 to include further comment from \uc2 Alisher Usmanov\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson regarding the property having been placed in a trust.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The French president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , said on Thursday that he felt among \uc2 EU\uc2  partners a willingness to continue to support Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a very deep, very strong commitment because we all know that we are talking about Europe and about the very possibility of lasting peace on our continent,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters during a European Political Community summit in Granada, Spain.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The attack on a village shop in Hroza, Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 which has killed at least 51 people \u8211\'20\'13 is among the most deadly during the conflict with Russia. But it is not the first time a strike \u8211\'20\'13 which Kyiv has attributed to Russia \u8211\'20\'13 has killed a large number of civilians.\par \par \uc2 Officials in the besieged city of Mariupol said at least 300 people were believed to have been killed in the bombing on 16 March last year of Mariupol\u8217\'20\'19s Drama Theatre, which had been marked with white paint as containing sheltering children. It became the deadliest single attack since Moscow launched its invasion of Ukraine more than a month earlier.\par \par \uc2 Five children were among at least 50 people killed when a missile hit the Kramatorsk railway station on 8 April last year. The Kremlin stood accused of carrying out a \u8220\'20\'1Cmonstrous\u8221\'20\'1D war crime after a powerful Tochka-U rocket landed outside the main station building where 4,000 people were waiting to be evacuated. The authorities had urged residents to leave the region before a Russian military assault.\par \par \uc2 At least 43 people died when a missile strike hit a five-story apartment block in Chasiv Yar, in eastern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , on 9 July last year. According to Kyiv, the residential building was hit by Russian rockets fired from truck-borne systems. A nine-year-old victim was found in the rubble two days after the attack.\par \par \uc2 A civilian convoy of cars heading to pick up relatives trying to flee Russian-occupied territory in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  was hit by Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s forces near the city of Zaporizhzhia on 30 September last year. Initial reports said dozens of people had been killed and injured, but the casualty figure reached at least 30 people dead and 88 wounded. Footage posted on social media showed a horrific scene with dead and injured people lying on a road on the south-eastern outskirts of the city.\par \par \uc2 Six children were among 46 people killed when an apartment building in the Ukrainian city of Dnipro was split in two with its middle reduced to rubble after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jan/14/russia-carries-out-two-mass-rocket-strikes-on-ukraine-killing-at-least-five-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Russian missile strike}}}\uc2  on 15 January this year. One of the dead was boxing coach Mykhailo Korenovskyi, the only member of his family who had been home at the time.\par \par \uc2 Also, in early May, at least 23 people were killed in Kherson when Russia launched a wave of missile and drone attacks on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , killing 16 as Moscow tested the strength of the country\u8217\'20\'19s air defences in intensified fighting. Russian attacks on the city hit the main supermarket and also the railway station.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Putin says Russia has tested nuclear-powered missile, declines to rule out testing nuclear explosion\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  said on Thursday that Russia had successfully tested a potent new strategic missile and declined to rule out the possibility it could carry out weapons tests involving nuclear explosions for the first time in more than three decades.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president said for the first time that Moscow had successfully tested the Burevestnik, a nuclear-powered and nuclear-capable cruise missile with a potential range of many thousands of miles.\par \par \uc2 He also told an annual gathering of analysts and journalists that Russia had almost completed work on its Sarmat intercontinental ballistic missile system, another key element of its new generation of nuclear weapons.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  in Sochi on Thursday. Photograph: Sputnik/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Putin, who has repeatedly reminded the world of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear might since launching his invasion of Ukraine on 24 February 2022, said no one in their right mind would use nuclear weapons against Russia.\par \par \uc2 If such an attack was detected, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Csuch a number of our missiles \u8211\'20\'13 hundreds, hundreds \u8211\'20\'13 would appear in the air that not a single enemy would have a chance of survival\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Russia has not conducted a test involving a nuclear explosion since 1990, the year before the collapse of the Soviet Union, but Putin declined to rule out the possibility it could resume such testing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Germany is \u8220\'20\'1Cworking on\u8221\'20\'1D providing Ukraine with an additional Patriot air defence system, the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , has said.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy had what he described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfruitful\u8221\'20\'1D meeting with the German chancellor, \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , at a gathering of European leaders in Spain on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CGermany is working on providing Ukraine with an additional Patriot system for the winter months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m grateful for Germany\u8217\'20\'19s support in defending our freedom and people. This is also the defence of Europe and our shared values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Patriot system is one of an array of sophisticated air-defence units supplied by the west to help Ukraine repel a Russian campaign of aerial attacks.\par \par \uc2 enltrFruitful meeting with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Bundeskanzler?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Bundeskanzler}}}\uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Germany is working on providing Ukraine with an additional \u8220\'20\'1CPatriot\u8221\'20\'1D system for the winter months.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m grateful for Germany\u8217\'20\'19s support in defending our freedom and people. This is also the defense of Europe and our shared values. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xv8k0bXNw3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xv8k0bXNw3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1709959056897585618?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has lost more than 90,000 troops since the start of its counteroffensive in early June, the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Putin also said Kyiv had lost 557 tanks and approximately 1,900 armoured vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Putin was giving a keynote speech at a meeting of the Valdai Discussion Club in the Russian Black Sea resort of Sochi.\par \par \uc2 He re-emphasised that he was \u8220\'20\'1Csure\u8221\'20\'1D Russia would achieve its goals in Ukraine and said its mission was to \u8220\'20\'1Cde-Nazify\u8221\'20\'1D the country. The Russian president has consistently claimed the war is a special millitary operation aimed at combatting Nazis in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 No 10 has stated the UK will stand with Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cfor as long as it takes\u8221\'20\'1D, after a meeting between \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  and the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the meeting of the European Political Community, the prime minister \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraged leaders to work together to supply further defence weapons\u8221\'20\'1D to Ukraine, his office said on X.\par \par \uc2 enltrAt the EPC today, Prime Minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RishiSunak?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RishiSunak}}}\uc2  has:\par \par \uc2 ? Announced \u163\'00\'A3500 million in winter support payments\par \par \uc2 ? Delivered \u163\'00\'A310 million for household electricity\par \par \uc2 ? Encouraged leaders to work together to supply further defence weapons\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll stand with Ukraine for as long as it takes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l9sW5nWcgR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/l9sW5nWcgR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 UK Prime Minister (@10DowningStreet) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/10DowningStreet/status/1709945170161271196?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , described the missile strike on a village which reportedly left at least 51 dead, including a six-year-old boy, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrutal terrorist attack\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, Zelenskiy said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a fully deliberate, demonstrative, and brutal terrorist attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy condolences to all those who have lost their loved ones! Assistance is being provided to the wounded. Russian terror must be stopped. All those who help Russia circumvent sanctions are criminals. Those who continue to support Russia are all supporting evil.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia needs this and similar terrorist attacks for one reason only: to make its genocidal aggression the new normal for the entire world. And I thank every leader and every nation that supports us in the defence of life!\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are now focused with European leaders, in particular, on how to strengthen our air defence, reinforce our troops, and protect our country from terror. Terrorists will face retaliation. One that is both just and powerful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRussian missile struck an ordinary grocery store in the Kupiansk district of the Kharkiv region. This was a fully deliberate, demonstrative, and brutal terrorist attack.\par \par \uc2 As of now, more than 51 people have been reported dead. My condolences to all those who have lost their loved\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yxIW2Xwy35"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yxIW2Xwy35}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1709948264072556939?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kyiv has turned the Black Sea region into a no-go zone for Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s bristling warships.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s foreign correspondent in Odesa analyses a moment of humiliation for Moscow and its implications:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/how-ukraine-reclaimed-black-sea-from-russian-forces"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A new form of warfare\u8217\'20\'19: how Ukraine reclaimed the Black Sea from Russian forces}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Death toll in Hroza rises to 51\par \par \uc2 A Russian missile struck cafe and grocery store in a village in north-eastern Ukraine on Thursday, killing at least 51 people as they held a memorial service, Ukrainian officials said according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Officials posted footage of dazed-looking rescue workers clambering through smouldering rubble. Some photos showed bodies lying alongside slabs of concrete and twisted metal, and others showed rescue workers carrying away bodies.\par \par \uc2 Emergency workers search the victims of the deadly Russian rocket attack that killed more than 50 people in the village of Hroza near Kharkiv, Ukraine, Thursday, 5 October 2023. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 The attack was the deadliest in the Kharkiv region since Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion more than 19 months ago, a spokesperson for the Kharkiv regional military administration told Ukrainian public broadcaster Suspilne.\par \par \uc2 It also appeared to be one of the biggest civilian death tolls in any single Russian strike since the start of the war.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president has accused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocidal aggression\u8221\'20\'1D after a missile hit a crowded rural cafe, killing at least 48 people including a six-year-old boy.\par \par \uc2 Read a full report on the Russian attack on Hroza from the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s foreign correspondent Luke Harding.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/russian-attack-village-cafe-kills-people-ukraine-hroza-kharkiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russian attack on village cafe kills at least 48 people in Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Read through the events of today\u8217\'20\'19s European leaders\u8217\'20\'19 summit, held amid tensions over aid to Ukraine, in our live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/european-leaders-summit-granada-migration-ukraine-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 European leaders meet for summit amid tensions over migration and aid to Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , spoke with the president of the European Council, \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2 , at a meeting of European leaders in Spain.\par \par \uc2 The meeting saw influential figures in Europe, such as the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , express their ongoing support for Ukraine in its war effort against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy said of his meeting with Michel: \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine is grateful for the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strong and lasting support, as well as the practical assistance of \uc2 EU\uc2  member states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe recent meeting of \uc2 EU\uc2  foreign ministers in Kyiv had significant symbolic and practical meaning. It underlined the unwavering EU support and strengthened our bilateral and multilateral ties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI updated Charles on the progress of our counteroffensive and Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s priority defence needs. We count on the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and its member states\u8217\'20\'19 further military aid, as well as the stable support within the European Peace Fund.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe also discussed the peace formula and our preparations for the Global Peace Summit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI met with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CharlesMichel?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CharlesMichel}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ukraine is grateful for the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strong and lasting support, as well as the practical assistance of \uc2 EU\uc2  member states.\par \par \uc2 The recent meeting of \uc2 EU\uc2  foreign ministers in Kyiv had significant symbolic and practical meaning. It underlined the unwavering EU\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DeFjGPHKb8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DeFjGPHKb8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1709944255987478531?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Footage shows rescue workers clambering through smouldering rubble after a Russian attack killed at least 49 people, including a six-year-old boy, in a village in the Kharkiv region of north-eastern Ukraine on 5 October, Ukrainian officials said.\par \par \uc2 The Kharkiv regional governor, Oleh Synehubov, said a cafe and a shop had been attacked in the village of Hroza, in the Kupyansk district of Kharkiv, where many civilians had been at the time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Putin claims Ukraine war shows west has 'lost touch with reality'\par \par \uc2 The Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , said on Thursday that the United States was seeking to impose its crumbling hegemony across the world and that the war in Ukraine showed how far the west had lost touch with reality.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe did not start the so-called war in Ukraine. On the contrary \u8211\'20\'13 we are trying to finish it,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin told a meeting of the Valdai Discussion Club in the Black Sea resort of Sochi.\par \par \uc2 The west had caused the war because the US was a \u8220\'20\'1Chegemon\u8221\'20\'1D which considered itself the only arbiter of truth on the planet, said the Kremlin chief.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  in Sochi on Thursday. Photograph: Mikhail Metzel/Sputnik/Kremlin/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Putin said the leaders of the west had lost \u8220\'20\'1Ca sense of reality\u8221\'20\'1D because of what he cast as Washington\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccolonial thinking\u8221\'20\'1D. He questioned what right the US had to lecture any other country.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022 unleashed a war that has devastated swathes of eastern and southern Ukraine, killed or injured hundreds of thousands of people and triggered the biggest rupture in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s ties with the west for six decades.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Death toll in Hroza rises to 49\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s interior minister has now said a Russian attack killed at least 49 people, including a six-year-old boy, in a death count that continues to rise.\par \par \uc2 The deaths occurred as the victims gathered in a cafe for a memorial service in a village in north-eastern Ukraine on Thursday, the minister added.\par \par \uc2 A cafe and a shop were struck early in the afternoon in the village of Hroza in the Kharkiv region, regional governor Oleh Synehubov said, adding that many civilians had been there at the time.\par \par \uc2 The interior minister, Ihor Klymenko, said residents of the small village of about 330 people had been holding a memorial service in the cafe that was hit.\par \par \uc2 Emergency workers search for victims of the Russian rocket attack in the village of Hroza near Kharkiv, Ukraine. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom every family, from every household, there were people present at this commemoration. This is a terrible tragedy,\u8221\'20\'1D Klymenko told Ukrainian television.\par \par \uc2 Seven people were also in hospital after the attack, which appeared to be the most devastating Russian strike on a residential area in weeks.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  on Thursday reiterated his position that Russia did not start the war in Ukraine but launched what it calls a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial military operation\u8221\'20\'1D to try to stop it.\par \par \uc2 In his yearly speech to the Valdai Discussion Club, being held in Sochi, Putin said Russia, the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest country by area, had no need to take territory from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 He said the conflict was not therefore imperial or territorial but about the global order, and that the west, which had lost its hegemonic power and always needed an enemy, had lost touch with reality.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , met the French president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , amid a meeting of European leaders in Spain.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy said: \u8220\'20\'1CStrengthening Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s air defence, as well as the security of the Odesa region and the Black Sea, is critical to ensure European and global stability. We are working together toward this end.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of our previous agreements to strengthen Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defence are being put into action. There will be more good news for our warriors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thank President Macron and the French people for their firm and steady support for Ukraine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrGreat meeting with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EmmanuelMacron?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @EmmanuelMacron}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Strenghtening Ukraine's air defense, as well as the security of the Odesa region and the Black Sea, is critical to ensure European and global stability. We are working together toward this end.\par \par \uc2 All of our previous agreements to strengthen\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iAy4HYWNxf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iAy4HYWNxf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1709919766092108042?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian officials have said a Russian attack on a village in the north-east of the country has killed 48 people and injured at least six more.\par \par \uc2 The presidential chief of staff, \uc2 Andriy Yermak\uc2 , and Kharkiv governor, Oleh Syniehubov, said Russian forces shelled a shop and a cafe in the village of Hroza in the Kharkiv region at about 1pm, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 A six-year-old boy was among those killed in the attack, Syniehubov said, and one child was also among the wounded.\par \par \uc2 Local sources say the cafe was crowded because a memorial lunch was being held for a villager who recently died.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s air force said that the country\u8217\'20\'19s air defences intercepted 24 out of 29 Iranian-made drones that Russia launched at the southern Odesa, Mykolaiv and Kirovohrad regions.\par \par \uc2 Andriy Raykovych, head of the Kirovohrad regional administration, said an infrastructure facility in the region was struck and emergency services were deployed to extinguish a fire. He said there were no casualties.\par \par \uc2 The attack came as Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  arrived in Granada in southern Spain to attend a summit of the European Political Community, which was formed in the wake of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Death toll in Hroza rises to 48\par \par \uc2 Andriy Yermak\uc2 , a spokesperson for Zelenskiy, says the death toll from the Russian strike in Kharkiv region is now 48.\par \par \uc2 Writing on X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2 , he said:\par \par \uc2 A Russian missile hit a civilian object in the village of Hroza, Kupiansk district. So far, we know that 48 lives were lost, a 6-year-old boy among them. There are also 6 injured, including a young girl. Rescue operations are ongoing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zelensky says 47 dead in Ukraine after Russian attack on village\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , has said 47 people have been killed in a Russian attack on a village in the north-eastern region of Kharkiv.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy said on Telegram on Thursday that a missile had hit a food shop.\par \par \uc2 It comes amid other drone strikes overnight in which a hospital was reportedly targeted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said he met the Armenian prime minister, \uc2 Nikol Pashinyan\uc2 , on Thursday on the sidelines of the European Political Community summit in Spain, and discussed the security situation in the South Caucasus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine is interested in the region\u8217\'20\'19s stability and friendly relations with its nations,\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy said on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe also discussed our bilateral cooperation and interregional economic projects.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrDuring our first-ever meeting, Armenian Prime Minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NikolPashinyan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NikolPashinyan}}}\uc2  and I focused on the security situation in the South Caucasus. Ukraine is interested in the region\u8217\'20\'19s stability and friendly relations with its nations. We also discussed our bilateral cooperation and\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xtOB2XvXsl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xtOB2XvXsl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1709910162134180078?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russia targeted Ukraine with drones in another massive attack early Thursday as President Zelenskyy travelled to Spain to rally support from western allies at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/europe-summit-armenia-azerbaijan-ukraine-russia-211a0ca2914d555047bcbcddc3f06d23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summit of 50 European leaders}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s air force said the country\u8217\'20\'19s air defences intercepted 24 out of 29 Iranian-made drones that Russia launched at the southern Odesa, Mykolaiv and Kirovohrad regions.\par \par \uc2 Andriy Raykovych, the head of the Kirovohrad regional administration, said that an infrastructure facility in the region was struck and emergency services were deployed to put out a fire. He said there were no casualties.\par \par \uc2 It was also reported by the Kyiv Independent that a Russian strike against Beryslav in Kherson Oblast damaged a hospital and injured two medical workers, with that outlet citing local governor Oleksandr Prokudin.\par \par \uc2 enltr?? Russia attacks hospital in Beryslav in Kherson Oblast, injures 2.\par \par \uc2 A Russian strike against Beryslav in Kherson Oblast damaged a hospital and injured two medical workers, Governor Oleksandr Prokudin reported on Oct. 5.\par \par \uc2 ?? Governor Oleksandr Prokudin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JwYGENBlQG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JwYGENBlQG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Kyiv Independent (@KyivIndependent) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyivIndependent/status/1709900182882570553?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The attack came as Zelenskyy arrived in Granada in southern Spain to attend a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/eu-ukraine-summit-armenia-serbia-granada-823a8734716f0fc717a61adbacff1c65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summit of the European Political Community}}}\uc2 , which was formed in the wake of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s February 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/russia-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 invasion of Ukraine}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Spain has offered new air defence and anti-drone systems to Ukraine to protect its energy and port infrastructures, a government source told Reuters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zelensky tells European leaders he is 'confident in America' to support Ukraine\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , told more than 40 European leaders gathered in Spain he was confident of America\u8217\'20\'19s continued support, and asked for their continued assistance and more arms to help him fight against Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 In an emotional speech, Zelenskiy said schoolchildren in Kharkiv in east Ukraine were learning remotely or attending classes underground in subway stations because of air raids.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUntil there is a fully effective air defence system, children cannot attend school,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the European Political Community summit hosted in Spain\u8217\'20\'19s Granada, 4,000km west of Kharkiv.\par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  arrives to attend the European Political Community summit at the Palacio de Congreso in Granada, southern Spain, on 5 October. Photograph: Thomas Coex/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 He voiced confidence in continued US support despite what he called a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical storm\u8221\'20\'1D there recently after aid to Ukraine did not make the cut for a last-minute Congress deal to avoid a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am confident in America. They are strong people with strong institutions, and a strong democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy said \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  should not be allowed to beef up his military or else Russia could attack beyond Ukraine by 2028.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet only Putin\u8217\'20\'19s ambitions be a ruin, not our countries, not our cities. Children of every country deserve to be safe. Everywhere in the country, not just in the subway, not just in underground shelters, but everywhere. We must make it possible. We must ensure that Ukraine wins.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Watch the Ukrainian president insist that US backing for Ukraine is not faltering, as he arrives at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/european-political-community"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 European Political Community}}}\uc2  summit in Granada.\par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said it was a difficult election period for the US and some voices were \u8220\'20\'1Cvery strange\u8221\'20\'1D, but he was confident of bipartisan support in Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Spain offers air defence and anti-drone systems to Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Spain has offered new air defence and anti-drone systems to Ukraine to protect its energy and port infrastructures, a government source told Reuters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Spanish army\uc2  will also train Ukrainian soldiers to use these news systems as well as provide more demining equipment, the source added.\par \par \uc2 It comes as Ukraine said on Thursday that over 26,000 people, including many civilians, were still unaccounted for since Russia launched its full-scale invasion last year.\par \par \uc2 On 25 September Odesa port infrastructure was reportedly hit by a massive drone and missile attack overnight. Photograph: Defense Forces of the South/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 The number of officially missing people is difficult to estimate, as Russian forces still occupy around a fifth of the country and neither side regularly releases data on military casualties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs of now, more than 26,000 people are wanted and are missing under special circumstances. Of these, 11,000 are civilians and about 15,000 are military personnel,\u8221\'20\'1D deputy interior minister Leonid Tymchenko said on national television.\par \par \uc2 This only includes people whose data has been officially verified, interior ministry spokesperson Mariana Reva told AFP, adding that the \u8220\'20\'1Cfigures could grow\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Russian mercenary group Wagner in 2022 signed a contract with a Chinese company to acquire two satellites and use their images, aiding its intelligence work as the organisation sought to push Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, according to a document seen by AFP.\par \par \uc2 The contract was signed in November 2022, over half a year into Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine in which the \uc2 Wagner group\uc2  under its founder, \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2 , was playing a key role on the battlefield.\par \par \uc2 The satellite images were also used to assist Wagner\u8217\'20\'19s operations in Africa and even its failed mutiny in June which has led now to the de-facto break up of the group followed by the death of Prigozhin and other key figures in an air crash in August, a European security source told AFP.\par \par \uc2 A man lights a candle at a makeshift memorial for Wagner private mercenary group chief \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2  in central Moscow. Photograph: Natalia Kolesnikova/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 According to a contract seen by AFP written in English and Russian and signed on 15 November 2022, the company Beijing Yunze Technology Co Ltd sold two high resolution observation satellites belonging to the Chinese space giant Chang Guang Satellite Technology (CGST) to Nika-Frut, a company then part of Prigozhin\u8217\'20\'19s commercial empire.\par \par \uc2 The over $30m (\u163\'00\'A324.7m) price was for the satellites themselves and additional services.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters is reporting that Spain will offer air defence, anti-drone systems to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The agency attributes the news to a Spanish government source at the city of Granada, amid a summit of the European Political Community.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Western supporters of Ukraine are exploring options to send seized Russian assets to assist with its war efforts, the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff said today.\par \par \uc2 Andriy Yermak\uc2  posted on X that: \u8220\'20\'1CThe US and the EU are looking for legal options that would allow Ukraine to transfer $300bn (\u163\'00\'A3247m) of frozen Russian assets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a very positive signal. Whoever kills, destroys, violates the norms of international law and the \uc2 UN\uc2  charter must lose. This is a question of justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ukltr??? ?? ?? ??????? ???????? ??????????, ??? ? ????????? ???????? ??????? $300 ???? ??????????? ?????????? ???????.\par \par \uc2 ?? ???? ?????????? ??????. ???, ??? ??????, ??????, ??????? ????? ???????????? ????? ?? ??????? ???, ??? ????????.\par \par \uc2 ?? ??????? ??????????????.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Andriy Yermak\uc2  (@AndriyYermak) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndriyYermak/status/1709812306324885745?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40am BST\par \par \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  said on Thursday she was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery confident\u8221\'20\'1D the US would maintain support for Ukraine despite Republican infighting over the issue that has cast doubt over further aid.\par \par \uc2 European leaders gathering in the Spanish city of Granada where she made her remarks are expected to assure Ukraine of long-term support after US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  voiced fears about continuing aid to Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  today arrived at the summit of the European Political Community \u8211\'20\'13 a forum established last year following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine to foster cooperation among more than 40 countries from Norway to Albania.\par \par \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  speaks to the media in Granada. Photograph: Fermin Rodriguez/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.23am BST\par \par \uc2 German police raid several properties owned by sanctions-hit Russian national\par \par \uc2 A special unit of police and customs officials have raided several properties of a Russian national in the southern state of Bavaria, officials said Thursday, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 The unidentified Russian is subject to sanctions and asset freezes by the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , German customs officials said.\par \par \uc2 The EU, the US and other western nations have imposed sanctions against Russia in response to Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s war against Ukraine. These include travel bans and asset freezes of a number of Russian government members and certain Russian businesspeople.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDue to tactical reasons related to the investigation no further information can be provided,\u8221\'20\'1D German customs officials said.\par \par \uc2 Several luxury cars have been confiscated from a villa on the Tegernsee lake in Rottach-Egern, German news agency dpa reported.\par \par \uc2 In September 2022, a special unit of about 250 police officers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-putin-germany-money-laundering-munich-e307849eb29c8c09087c827fdbf4a6c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raided two dozen properties across Germany}}}\uc2  linked to Russian oligarch \uc2 Alisher Usmanov\uc2 , a close ally of Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , on suspicion of money laundering and violations of EU sanctions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21am BST\par \par \uc2 James Cleverly\uc2 , the UK foreign secretary, has claimed Putin is \u8220\'20\'1Cstopping food getting to the world\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable\u8221\'20\'1D, over allegations Russia may use sea mines to target civilian shipping in the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, the site formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Cleverly said: \u8220\'20\'1CDeclassified intelligence released today shows that Russia may use sea mines to target civilian shipping in the Black Sea.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPutin is stopping food getting to the world\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe world is watching.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cleverly had earlier accused Russia of \u8220\'20\'1Cpernicious targeting\u8221\'20\'1D of civilian shipping.\par \par \uc2 enltrDeclassified intelligence released today shows that Russia may use sea mines to target civilian shipping in the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 Putin is stopping food getting to the world's most vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 The world is watching.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 James Cleverly\uc2 ???? (@JamesCleverly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamesCleverly/status/1709861135166374012?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Morning summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said the main task at meetings during the European Political Community Summit was to preserve unity in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2 . Zelenskiy is the Spanish city of Granada for a forum to discuss cooperation among more than 40 countries established after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  admitted Wednesday he was worried that political turmoil in Washington could threaten US aid to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , urging Republicans to stop their infighting and back \u8220\'20\'1Ccritically important\u8221\'20\'1D assistance for Kyiv. Biden said that he would soon be giving a major speech on the need to support Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fight against the Russian invasion after the chaos in Washington alarmed US allies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two people were killed in Russian shelling of the southern Ukrainian city of Kherson, the head of the Ukrainian president\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Thursday. \uc2 Andriy Yermak\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, said on Telegram that one of the dead was a utility worker who trimmed trees.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Britain has accused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  of plotting to sabotage civilian vessels loaded with Ukrainian grain by planting sea mines on the approaches to the country\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea ports. Based on what it said was declassified intelligence, the UK said Russia did not want to directly attack merchant ships using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s newly created humanitarian corridor with missiles, but instead try to destroy them covertly.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin has said questions about Russian naval operations should be directed to the defence ministry after the Wall Street Journal reported that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  had withdrawn the bulk of its Black Sea fleet from its main base in annexed Crimea. The WSJ said the move had been a response to Ukrainian attacks. Russia seized and unilaterally annexed Crimea from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  in 2014. Kyiv has vowed to restore its control over the peninsula and the other territories that Russia has captured, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US has supplied {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  with more than a million rounds of Iranian ammunition confiscated in the Gulf late last year. The transfer of the ordnance followed a civil forfeiture case pursued by the justice department to gain ownership on the grounds that the bullets were seized as they were being smuggled to Yemeni Houthi forces in violation of a \uc2 UN\uc2  arms embargo.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia is planning a naval base on the Black Sea coast of the breakaway Georgian region of Abkhazia, the leader of the region was quoted on Thursday as saying by the Izvestiya newspaper, a day after meeting president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . \uc2 Aslan Bzhania\uc2 , the self-styled president of the Russian-backed breakaway region, said an agreement had been signed for a permanent naval base in the Ochamchira region.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 VolodymyrZelenskiyis working to provide Ukraine with more air defence systems as winter approaches. Last winter, Russian forces deliberately targeted Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure, knocking out power and gas at a time when heating was necessary. More air defence systems could work in preventing that from happening again.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Award-winning Ukrainian freelance journalist Victoria Roshchyna, has not been heard from since 3 August. She had been reporting from a Russia-occupied territory of Ukraine, the International Women\u8217\'20\'19s Media Foundation (IWMF) said today. Roshchyna had been reporting from the frontlines of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine since the war began in February 2022, and was previously captured by Russian forces in March 2022 and held for 10 days in Berdiansk.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russian former state TV journalist Marina Ovsyannikova, who burst into a news broadcast with a placard that read \u8220\'20\'1CStop the war\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re lying to you\u8221\'20\'1D, has been sentenced to eight and a half years in jail in absentia on Wednesday. Ovsyannikova was found guilty of \u8220\'20\'1Cspreading knowingly false information about the Russian armed forces\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a statement posted by the court on Telegram. Ovsyannikova, 45, fled Russia with her daughter for an unspecified European country a year ago after escaping from house arrest, according to her lawyer, saying she had no case to answer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine increased its road shipments of agricultural goods in September, according to Spike Brokers, a commercial agent broker on the grain and oil market of Ukraine. In September, 514,000 metric tons of agricultural goods were exported by lorries, while in August, 506,000 tons were exported. The increase is still down from the year before, which saw 639,000 tons in September 2022.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Tom Ambrose, for now. My colleague Charlie Moloney will be along shortly to continue bringing you the latest from Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said on Thursday the main task at meetings during the European Political Community Summit was to preserve unity in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy is the Spanish city of Granada for a forum to discuss cooperation among more than 40 countries established after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe main challenge is to save unity in Europe not only in the EU but in all of Europe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Zelenskiy, warning of Russian \u8220\'20\'1Cdisinformation attacks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08am BST\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin has said questions about Russian naval operations should be directed to the defence ministry after the Wall Street Journal reported that Russia had withdrawn the bulk of its Black Sea fleet from its main base in annexed Crimea.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ said the move had been a response to Ukrainian attacks. Russia seized and unilaterally annexed Crimea from Ukraine in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Kyiv has vowed to restore its control over the peninsula and the other territories that Russia has captured, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov declined to comment on the story, or on reports that Russia had signed a deal for a permanent naval base on the Black Sea coast of the breakaway Georgian region of Abkhazia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Two people were killed in Russian shelling of the southern Ukrainian city of Kherson, the head of the Ukrainian president\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Andriy Yermak\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, said on Telegram that one of the dead was a utility worker who trimmed trees.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44am BST\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said on Thursday he had arrived in the Spanish city of Granada to take part in the European Political Community summit, a forum to foster cooperation among more than 40 countries established after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will pay special attention to the Black Sea region as well as our joint efforts to strengthen global food security and freedom of navigation,\u8221\'20\'1D he said on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s key priority was to strengthen its air defences as winter approaches.\par \par \uc2 You can follow our live coverage of the Granada summit here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/oct/05/european-leaders-summit-granada-migration-ukraine-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 European leaders meet for summit amid tensions over migration and aid to Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29am BST\par \par \uc2 A Ukrainian drone operator flies a UAV to locate Russian army positions near the frontline village of Robotyne in the Zaporizhzhia region. Photograph: Roman Pilipey/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44am BST\par \par \uc2 A little more detail on that planned Russian naval base off the coast of the Black Sea via Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The news agency is reporting:\par \par \uc2 Russia plans a naval base on the Black Sea coast of the breakaway Georgian region of Abkhazia, the leader of the region was quoted on Thursday as saying by the Izvestiya newspaper, a day after meeting president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Aslan Bzhania\uc2 , the self-styled president of the Russian-backed breakaway region, said an agreement had been signed for a permanent naval base in the Ochamchira region.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have signed an agreement, and in the near future there will be a permanent base of the Russian Navy in the Ochamchira district,\u8221\'20\'1D Bzhania told Izvestiya.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is all aimed at increasing the level of defence capability of both Russia and Abkhazia, and this kind of interaction will continue,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are also things I can\u8217\'20\'19t talk about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Russia recognized Abkhazia and another breakaway region, South Ossetia, as independent states in 2008 after Russian troops repelled a Georgian attempt to retake South Ossetia in a five-day war which ended on August 12, 2008.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal reported that Russia had withdrawn the bulk of its Black Sea Fleet from its main base in annexed Crimea due to Ukrainian attacks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Russia is planning a naval base on the Black Sea coast of the breakaway Georgian region of Abkhazia, the leader of the region has told the Izvestiya newspaper.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37am BST\par \par \uc2 US leaders expected to assure Ukraine of long-term support\par \par \uc2 European leaders are expected to assure Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  of long-term support on Thursday after US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  voiced fears that Republican infighting in Congress could hurt American policy on continuing aid to Kyiv, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy is expected to attend a summit in the Spanish city of Granada of the European Political Community \u8211\'20\'13 a forum to foster cooperation among more than 40 countries established last year following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 His attendance was not announced in advance for security reasons. Officials familiar with the plans said he would take part in the summit, giving him the chance to press for more urgently needed military aid, such as air defence systems.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy said in a video message on Wednesday evening: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are preparing for intensive international activities \u8211\'20\'13 this week and next week should be productive for Ukraine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Granada gathering also gives leaders such as French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , German chancellor \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  and British prime minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  a chance to restate their commitment to Ukraine after political turbulence in both the US and Europe raised questions about continued support.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18worried\u8217\'20\'19 that turmoil in Washington could disrupt US aid to Ukraine\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  admitted Wednesday he was worried that political turmoil in Washington could threaten US aid to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , urging Republicans to stop their infighting and back \u8220\'20\'1Ccritically important\u8221\'20\'1D assistance for Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Biden said that he would soon be giving a major speech on the need to support Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fight against the Russian invasion after the chaos in Washington alarmed US allies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt does worry me,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told reporters when asked whether the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/kevin-mccarthy-house-speaker-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ousting of Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy}}}\uc2  by hardliners in his own party could derail more funds for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s war effort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I know there are a majority of members of the House and Senate of both parties who have said that they support funding Ukraine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A last-gasp deal in Congress to avoid a \uc2 US government\uc2  shutdown at the weekend contained no fresh funding for Ukraine, and hopes for a quick resolution have been further complicated by McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s exit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/joe-biden-washington-turmoil-kevin-mccarthy-impact-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18worried\u8217\'20\'19 that turmoil in Washington could disrupt US aid to Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13am BST\par \par \uc2 US transfers confiscated Iranian ammunition to Ukraine\par \par \uc2 ftanThe United States has supplied {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  with more than a million rounds of Iranian ammunition confiscated in the Gulf late last year.\par \par \uc2 The transfer of the ordnance followed a civil forfeiture case pursued by the justice department to gain ownership on the grounds that the bullets were seized as they were being smuggled to Yemeni Houthi forces in violation of a \uc2 UN\uc2  arms embargo.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith this weapons transfer, the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s forfeiture actions against one authoritarian regime are now directly supporting the Ukrainian people\u8217\'20\'19s fight against another authoritarian regime,\u8221\'20\'1D the US attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , said on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to use every legal authority at our disposal to support Ukraine in their fight for freedom, democracy and the rule of law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/us-supplies-ukraine-with-ammunition-seized-from-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supplies Ukraine with a million rounds of ammunition seized from Iran}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06am BST\par \par \uc2 UK accuses Russia of planning to mine Black Sea\par \par \uc2 Britain has accused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  of plotting to sabotage civilian vessels loaded with Ukrainian grain by planting sea mines on the approaches to the country\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea ports.\par \par \uc2 Based on what it said was declassified intelligence, the UK said Russia did not want to directly attack merchant ships using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s newly created humanitarian corridor with missiles, but instead try to destroy them covertly.\par \par \uc2 Russia would then seek to blame {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  for the loss of any shipping in an attempt to evade responsibility, the British Foreign Office continued, and the UK said it was going public in order to deter Moscow from carrying out the plan.\par \par \uc2 James Cleverly\uc2 , the UK foreign secretary, accused Russia of the \u8220\'20\'1Cpernicious targeting\u8221\'20\'1D of civilian shipping: \u8220\'20\'1CThe world is watching \u8211\'20\'13 and we see right through Russia\u8217\'20\'19s cynical attempts to lay blame on Ukraine for their attacks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/04/uk-says-russia-plotting-to-sabotage-ukrainian-grain-tankers-with-sea-mines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK says Russia plotting to sabotage Ukrainian grain tankers with sea mines}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to our live coverage of the war in Ukraine. This is Helen Sullivan with the latest.\par \par \uc2 Our top stories this morning: Britain has accused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  of plotting to sabotage civilian cargo ships loaded with Ukrainian grain by planting sea mines on the approaches to the country\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea ports.\par \par \uc2 And the United States has supplied {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  with more than a million rounds of Iranian ammunition confiscated in the Gulf late last year.\par \par \uc2 The transfer of the ordnance followed a civil forfeiture case pursued by the justice department to gain ownership on the grounds that the bullets were seized as they were being smuggled to Yemeni Houthi forces in violation of a \uc2 UN\uc2  arms embargo.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more on these stories shortly.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 VolodymyrZelenskiyis working to provide Ukraine with more air defence systems as winter approaches. Last winter, Russian forces deliberately targeted Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure, knocking out power and gas at a time when heating was necessary. More air defence systems could work in preventing that from happening again.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  admitted Wednesday he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/05/joe-biden-washington-turmoil-kevin-mccarthy-impact-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worried that political turmoil in Washington could threaten US aid to Ukraine}}}\uc2 , urging Republicans to stop their infighting and back \u8220\'20\'1Ccritically important\u8221\'20\'1D assistance for Kyiv. Biden added that he would soon be giving a major speech on the need to support Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fight against the Russian invasion after the chaos in Washington alarmed US allies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s navy said on Wednesday that 12 more vessels were ready to enter a Black Sea shipping corridor on their way towards Ukrainian ports, and that 10 other vessels were ready to depart from the country\u8217\'20\'19s ports. Navy spokesperson Dmytro Pletenchuk made his remarks as Ukraine tries to defy a de facto Russian blockade on Ukrainian exports via the Black Sea after Moscow pulled out of a deal in July that had allowed Kyiv to safely export grain.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Award-winning Ukrainian freelance journalist Victoria Roshchyna, has not been heard from since 3 August. She had been reporting from a Russia-occupied territory of Ukraine, the International Women\u8217\'20\'19s Media Foundation (IWMF) said today. Roshchyna had been reporting from the frontlines of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine since the war began in February 2022, and was previously captured by Russian forces in March 2022 and held for 10 days in Berdiansk.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russian former state TV journalist Marina Ovsyannikova, who burst into a news broadcast with a placard that read \u8220\'20\'1CStop the war\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re lying to you\u8221\'20\'1D, has been sentenced to eight-and-a-half years in jail in absentia on Wednesday. Ovsyannikova was found guilty of \u8220\'20\'1Cspreading knowingly false information about the Russian armed forces\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a statement posted by the court on Telegram. Ovsyannikova, 45, fled Russia with her daughter for an unspecified European country a year ago after escaping from house arrest, according to her lawyer, saying she had no case to answer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine increased its road shipments of agricultural goods in September, according to Spike Brokers, a commercial agent broker on the grain and oil market of Ukraine. In September, 514,000 metric tons of agricultural goods were exported by lorries, while in August, 506,000 tons were exported. The increase is still down from the year before, which saw 639,000 tons in September 2022.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231005eja5000mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
