\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Over 75,000 workers poised for largest healthcare strike in US history\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 768 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2023\par 11:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  workers push for improvements to staffing levels and wage increases after union contract expires\par \par \uc2 More than 75,000 healthcare workers at the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest non-profit private healthcare provider, \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  , are poised to strike on 4 October in the largest healthcare strike in US history.\par \par \uc2 The workers\u8217\'20\'19 union contract expired at the weekend and staff are pushing for significant improvements to staffing levels and wage increases that account for recent high inflation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt just seems like there is no concern for short-staffing and patient care. It\u8217\'20\'19s mind blowing to see \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  that was once an industry leader that liked to call themselves the gold standard of care, be so out of touch with employees, with their patients, and their more focused on putting profits over patient care,\u8221\'20\'1D said Henry Perez, an intensive care unit secretary at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  in Modesto, California, for about four years.\par \par \uc2 The strike will hit hundreds of facilities in California, Oregon, Washington, Colorado, Virginia and Washington DC. The Coalition of \uc2 Kaiser Permanente Unions\uc2  noted that if they don\u8217\'20\'19t see movement at the bargaining table in response to the strike, another longer strike that includes additional workers in Washington will be called.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey always praised us as healthcare heroes during the pandemic and now they\u8217\'20\'19re treating us like zeros by not bargaining in good faith,\u8221\'20\'1D said Perez.\par \par \uc2 He explained that working in an emergency care unit, there are days where he has to do the work of two, three or four other unit assistants, and short staffing has led to patients having long waits for assistance which poses a significant safety issue for them and claimed the problem has only worsened due to the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn top of having my unit I will have the entire hospital, which is 102 patients I\u8217\'20\'19m responsible for and it causes burnout, it causes mental anguish, it causes stress. I see my nurses I support and we\u8217\'20\'19re constantly running on fumes because of staffing,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Kaiser Permanente{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.kaiserpermanente.org/who-we-are/fast-facts#:~:text=Our%20company,plans%2C%20serving%2012.7%20million%20members."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serves  }}}\uc2  12.7 million members in California, Washington, Oregon, Georgia, Hawaii, Washington DC, Maryland and Virginia. The non-profit has reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unioncoalition.org/2023-oct-strike-notice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $3bn  }}}\uc2  in profits in the first half of 2023 and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courthousenews.com/kaiser-permanente-union-workers-picket-at-health-care-facilities-across-the-west/#:~:text=The%20coalition%20says%20that%20despite,and%202022%20to%20%2458.9%20billion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid  }}}\uc2  at least 49 corporate executives salaries exceeding $1m annually.\par \par \uc2 Keven Dardon, a patient access representative at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Sunnyside medical center in Clackamas, Oregon, for 14 years, said that prior to the Covid-19 pandemic his department was staffed with about 60 employees and now has been operating with less than 40 after cuts to the department, which has resulted in long lines and delays for patients trying to check into their appointments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really taken a toll in the hospital setting and in the medical offices that we have here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dardon. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for. Our frontline employees are demanding \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  executives come to the table, we\u8217\'20\'19ve proposed the things that would fix the staffing issue, we\u8217\'20\'19ve made tons of proposals, but because our executives just aren\u8217\'20\'19t listening to us, they are just not coming to the table to even entertain those proposals.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Melara, a teleservice representative for \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  in Sacramento, California, argued that \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  has been growing membership, but hasn\u8217\'20\'19t kept up staffing levels to handle it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want our patients to be safe and we want them to get the best care that they need,\u8221\'20\'1D said Melara. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one wants to strike. But we have to stand in solidarity because the executives that are making millions of dollars aren\u8217\'20\'19t thinking about anyone else but their own profit and their own increasing wages and not thinking about the rest of us, who are the patients and the staff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  argued they lead total compensation in all markets where they operate and disputed short staffing crisis claims from workers and the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the acute shortage of health care workers nationally, we have been able to hire more than 50,000 frontline employees in the last two years: 29,000 people in 2022, and another 22,000 so far this year. Included in this year\u8217\'20\'19s new hires are more than 9,800 people hired into jobs represented by the coalition,\u8221\'20\'1D said a \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  spokesperson in an email.\par \par \uc2 They also noted they are continuing to bargain with the coalition to avert a strike but have contingency plans in place to continue providing care during the strike.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231003eja30018r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
