\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Fed up\u8217\'20\'19 US autoworkers expand strikes against \uc2 GM\uc2  and Ford\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 542 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2023\par 16:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain says members \u8216\'20\'18fed up with corporate greed\u8217\'20\'19 as another 7,000 workers to strike at \uc2 GM\uc2  and Ford plants\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  escalated its strike against the big three US automakers on Friday as the industrial action entered its third week.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/uaw.union/videos/338429235319253"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 livestream update}}}\uc2  on the strike on Friday, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, said another 7,000 workers would be joining the action. About 25,000 workers are now on strike.\par \par \uc2 Fain said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are fed up with corporate greed and we are fed up with corporate excess. We are fed up with breaking our bodies for companies that take more and more and give less and less.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fain said bargaining with Ford and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  had not made meaningful progress in the past week, adding Ford\u8217\'20\'19s Chicago assembly plant and a \uc2 GM\uc2  plant in Lansing, Michigan, to the strike. Action at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  was not escalated this week due to progress made in talks.\par \par \uc2 The strike has become a hot-button issue in political circles with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  visiting Michigan this week to address autoworkers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis strike is absolutely about the worker and listening to the worker,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley Stevens, a Democrat representing Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s 11th congressional district, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThis strike has opened up new channels to hear from workers in ways that we haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen in a very long time in the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stevens served as chief of staff to the US Auto Rescue Task Force under the Obama administration and has appeared on the strike picket lines in support of autoworkers. She recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stevens.house.gov/media/press-releases/congresswoman-haley-stevens-d-mi-introduces-union-auto-workers-job-protection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reintroduced}}}\uc2  a bill to protect union autoworkers in Congress.\par \par \uc2 She said the concessions autoworkers made to help the auto industry recover from the 2008 economic recession have not been returned. She also praised the work auto employees did to get the industry through the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time to recognize that work, and their fair share of the profit, and ensure that anyone who works at the automakers is treated fairly, and dealt in to the profits and to the transition that\u8217\'20\'19s under way,\u8221\'20\'1D Stevens added.\par \par \uc2 Shaun Collier, a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  assembly worker in Sterling Heights, Michigan, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe big three have been making record profits, giving themselves increases, while us \uc2 UAW\uc2  members are the ones doing all of the work, putting wear and tear on our bodies, missing our kids\u8217\'20\'19 extracurricular activities because we are forced to be here to build a product we can\u8217\'20\'19t even afford.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll we want is a livable wage, a work-life balance, and job security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2  the \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket line in Michigan on Tuesday, the first sitting president ever to do so.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact of the matter is you guys, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 you saved the automobile industry back in 2008 and before. You made a lot of sacrifices, gave up a lot. The companies were in trouble. Now they are doing incredibly well, and guess what? You should be doing incredibly well too,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Trump held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally}}}\uc2  at a non-union auto parts plant outside of Detroit on Wednesday, coinciding with the Republican presidential primary debate.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230929ej9t002ek\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
