\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Where do each of the US Republican candidates stand on labor and unions?\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 1,718 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2023\par 19:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump and seven other Republicans face the same challenge \u8211\'20\'13 US support for unions is at a high but the GOP historically doesn\u8217\'20\'19t condone them\par \par \uc2 In a bid to recapture the favor of blue-collar rust belt voters, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  traveled to Michigan on Wednesday to address a crowd of autoworkers at a rally near Detroit. The former president billed his prime-time speech as a gesture of solidarity with striking autoworkers.\par \par \uc2 The event doubled as a distraction from the night\u8217\'20\'19s Republican primary debate, where other candidates discussed how they would help striking autoworkers.\par \par \uc2 On two very different stages, Trump and the seven other Republicans faced the same challenge. American support for labor unions is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/398303/approval-labor-unions-highest-point-1965.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at a 57-year-high}}}\uc2 , and union members \u8211\'20\'13 especially the thousands of autoworkers currently on strike \u8211\'20\'13 are a coveted voting bloc that could help secure the White House in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Except there\u8217\'20\'19s one problem: the Republican party doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like unions.\par \par \uc2 In the decades since \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, GOP lawmakers championed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/25/republicans-working-class-voter-unions-worker-protections-organize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cright to work\u8221\'20\'1D laws}}}\uc2  designed to limit union membership. In 2021, congressional Republicans overwhelmingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/202170"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted against}}}\uc2  a bill that would make it easier for workers to form unions.\par \par \uc2 Some candidates have already antagonized unions, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/tim-scott-asked-auto-strikes-praises-firing-striking-federal-workers-rcna105716"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senator Tim Scott}}}\uc2  last week suggesting that the striking autoworkers ought to be fired.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 strike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/us-auto-workers-strike-uaw-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is growing}}}\uc2 . This week, Biden became the first sitting president to join the picket line, shifting the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s calculus of which Republican is most likely to win the general election.\par \par \uc2 The eight Republican candidates attempted to reconcile GOP policy and politics on Wednesday, with uneven results.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where each Republican candidate stands on labor and unions.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 In a move that \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain described as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN/status/1706801528260939853"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a pathetic irony}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally for striking workers was hosted at a nonunion auto plant in Macomb county.\par \par \uc2 Still, some voters and political experts in the region praised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decision to skip the second primary debate in favor of a Michigan rally.\par \par \uc2 Chris Jackowiak, an Illinois political strategist at a \u8220\'20\'1Ccenter-right\u8221\'20\'1D campaign consultant group called Cor Strategies, said the move helped distinguish Trump from the remaining slate of GOP candidates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a real contrast to see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaking to union workers in Detroit when everybody else is at Ronald union-buster Reagan\u8217\'20\'19s presidential library in California,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackowiak told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 In Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s speech, the former president tapped the same talking points that propelled him to the White House in 2016. He pointed to electric vehicles \u8211\'20\'13 not auto industry CEOs \u8211\'20\'13 as the real enemy of striking workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn day one, I will terminate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s electric vehicle mandate, and I will cancel every job-killing regulation that is crushing American autoworkers,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The speech repeated many of the sentiments expressed by big three executives earlier this month. After the strike\u8217\'20\'19s launch, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/16/business/electric-vehicles-uaw-gm-ford-stellantis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ford CEO Jim Farley told the New York Times}}}\uc2  that worker demands for increased wages would \u8220\'20\'1Cforce Ford to scrap its investment in electric vehicles\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  argues that auto companies do not have to choose between electric vehicles and workers rights.\par \par \uc2 Trump also raised the specter of foreign outsourcing, another tactic that helped him court rust belt voters in 2016. On Wednesday, the former president said electric vehicles \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be manufactured in foreign lands that you couldn\u8217\'20\'19t care less about\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It was a compelling warning for the 2016 electorate, yet some political experts in the midwest wonder if the message will translate to the 2024 race, especially as Biden doubles down on his claim to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/02/joe-biden-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most pro-union president\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jackowiak said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 appeal to midwest voters, including union members, was in part thanks to his careful self-branding as a political outsider that could fix Washington corruption for working-class families.\par \par \uc2 That pro-worker label that Trump ascribed himself might be harder to secure now, after four years in the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s always going to be the anti-establishment figure, but now he went from someone who was viciously opposed to the Republican party to somebody who is the de facto leader of the Republican party,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackowiak said.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s populist veneer was damaged, in part, by the legacy of his presidency. At a 2017 rally in Youngstown, Ohio, Trump pledged to protect the manufacturing jobs at the nearby \uc2 General Motors\uc2  auto plant in \uc2 Lordstown\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those jobs have since vanished. In late 2018, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2018/dec/27/general-motors-ohio-auto-car-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 General Motors abruptly announced}}}\uc2  it would cut roughly 14,000 jobs and idle five factories in North America, including the \uc2 Lordstown\uc2  location, which permanently closed the following year.\par \par \uc2 Union folks are not going to forget that [\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ] makes promises and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t deliver\par \par \uc2 Michael Traugott of the \uc2 University of Michigan\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe told people, \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t move, don\u8217\'20\'19t sell your home, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to save this plant,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Traugott, a political science professor at the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Union folks are not going to forget that he makes promises and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t deliver.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina senator is among the most vocal Republican critics of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike.\par \par \uc2 The autoworkers\u8217\'20\'19 union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23988920-tim-scott-nlrb-complaint"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a complaint}}}\uc2  against Scott with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  after the senator suggested that the striking workers ought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/republican-hopefuls-split-on-how-to-curry-favor-with-striking-uaw-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lose their jobs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want more benefits, working fewer hours. That is simply not going to stand,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said on Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate stage.\par \par \uc2 In a bizarre segue, Scott attempted to switch topics from the autoworkers\u8217\'20\'19 strike to regulation of the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 Scott has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UUEOu63W9aA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blasted teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions}}}\uc2 . During the first presidential debate in August, Scott said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe only way we change education in this nation is to break the backs of the teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When Los Angeles teachers went on strike earlier this year, Scott blamed teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scott.senate.gov/media-center/press-releases/amid-la-teacher-strike-scott-pushes-for-legislation-to-expand-school-choice-to-low-income-students-affected-by-school-closures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March}}}\uc2  statement about the California strike, the senator said teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions are \u8220\'20\'1Cdodging accountability, denying parental rights and failing to meet the academic standards America\u8217\'20\'19s students deserve\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday night, Ramaswamy attempted to criticize the \uc2 UAW\uc2  without alienating large swaths of union voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have a lot of patience for union bosses,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI do have a lot of sympathy for the workers, however.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Opposition to unions appears to be a centerpiece of Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 The presidential hopeful echoed Scott\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions during the first primary debate in August. He pledged to end teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions \u8220\'20\'1Cat the local level\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUZxa9ZBKbM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April campaign video}}}\uc2 , Ramaswamy said the US should abolish both teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions and the Department of Education.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the former vice-president said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cstand with workers all across America\u8221\'20\'1D, through right-to-work laws, an anti-union policy that groups like the \uc2 UAW\uc2  resoundingly opposes.\par \par \uc2 As governor of Indiana, Pence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casetext.com/case/sweeney-v-pence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended the state\u8217\'20\'19s right-to-work laws}}}\uc2  from legal challenge by union leaders.\par \par \uc2 Pence also signed a law that blocked local governments from raising worker benefits \u8211\'20\'13 like the minimum wage and sick leave \u8211\'20\'13 above the federal minimum.\par \par \uc2 As a member of Congress, Pence voted against a bill that would have made it harder for employers to retaliate against unionized workers.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\par \par \uc2 The former South Carolina governor proudly calls herself \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/republican-hopefuls-split-on-how-to-curry-favor-with-striking-uaw-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a union buster}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you have the most pro-union president and he touts that he is emboldening the unions, this is what you get,\u8221\'20\'1D she told Fox News last week. \u8220\'20\'1CThe union is asking for a 40% raise, the companies have come back with a 20% raise \u8211\'20\'13 I think any of the taxpayers would love to have a 20% raise and think that\u8217\'20\'19s great.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yet her embrace of the \u8220\'20\'1Cunion buster\u8221\'20\'1D moniker appeared to vanish on the debate stage on Wednesday. Instead of criticizing unions, Haley said the strike happened because of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s mismanagement of the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are paying higher gas prices, higher grocery prices,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s focus on what it takes to get more cash in the pockets of workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley suggested that workers would not be striking if inflation hadn\u8217\'20\'19t put a strain on American families.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2017/feb/15/boeing-south-carolina-union-collective-bargaining"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a 2012 speech}}}\uc2  as governor of South Carolina, Haley pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake the unions understand full well that they are not needed, not wanted and not welcome in the state of South Carolina\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In 2015, she fought to stop workers at the state\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Boeing\uc2  plant from unionizing.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor hesitated to comment on the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike, both on and off the debate stage.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis criticized the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s push for electric vehicles in an interview with an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-J94rDkXGBY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa television news station}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 In May, DeSantis signed a bill into law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/13/florida-teachers-woke-law-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that aims to weaken the teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions}}}\uc2  and other public-employee unions.\par \par \uc2 In 2017, he joined a coalition of House Republicans who introduced a federal right-to-work bill, which would have starved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2017/feb/02/republicans-unions-right-to-work-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already shrinking US unions of funding}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\par \par \uc2 The former New Jersey governor and short-lived Trump confidant remained quiet during the debate\u8217\'20\'19s discussion of unions.\par \par \uc2 Like DeSantis, Christie has been hesitant to weigh in on the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike.\par \par \uc2 But Christie shares his fellow Republican candidates\u8217\'20\'19 disdain for teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions. During the 2016 presidential election, he compared the New Jersey teachers\u8217\'20\'19 union to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.edweek.org/policy-politics/n-j-gov-chris-christie-calls-teachers-union-mafia-signs-education-bills/2016/09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the mafia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He made headlines in 2015 after suggesting that the federal teachers\u8217\'20\'19 union should be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2015/08/02/sotu-tapper-christie-national-teachers-union-deserves-a-punch-in-the-face.cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cpunched in the face\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As governor of New Jersey, Christie {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/jun/30/chris-christie-presidency-new-jerseyans-liar-bully"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gutted the state pension system}}}\uc2  for public employees, including teachers.\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\par \par \uc2 Burgum\u8217\'20\'19s fledgling campaign has struggled to retain relevance in recent months, and Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate was no exception.\par \par \uc2 After Fox News moderators prepared to move on from the topic of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike, the former North Dakota governor chimed in with a more muted version of his fellow Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 statements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason why people are striking in Detroit is because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interference with capital markets,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He criticized the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s support of electric vehicle manufacturing, and alluded to an existential threat from China.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis strike is at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s feet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, Burgum has not shared his view on unions.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230928ej9s00236\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
