\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Signs touting \u8216\'20\'18auto workers for Trump\u8217\'20\'19 at Michigan rally found to be fake \u8211\'20\'13 report\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in Washington \par \uc2 482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2023\par 15:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 At least two people holding signs saying \u8216\'20\'18union members for Trump\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18auto workers for Trump\u8217\'20\'19 turned out to be neither\par \par \uc2 When Donald Trump gave a speech in Michigan on Wednesday, seeking to capitalise on the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike, at least two crowd members holding signs saying \u8220\'20\'1Cunion members for Trump\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cauto workers for Trump\u8221\'20\'1D turned out to be neither.\par \par \uc2 The Detroit News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2023/09/27/donald-trump-returns-auto-industry-strike-uaw-ev-taking-center-stage-presidential-election-joe-biden/70960155007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1COne individual in the crowd who held a sign that said \u8216\'20\'18union members for Trump\u8217\'20\'19 acknowledged that she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a union member when approached by a reporter after the event.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnother person with a sign that read \u8216\'20\'18auto workers for Trump\u8217\'20\'19 said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t an auto worker when asked for an interview. Both people didn\u8217\'20\'19t provide their names.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The paper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2023/09/27/donald-trump-returns-auto-industry-strike-uaw-ev-taking-center-stage-presidential-election-joe-biden/70960155007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  between 400 and 500 people attended the event, at a non-unionised automotive parts supplier in Clinton Township.\par \par \uc2 Trump skipped a Republican debate in California to visit Macomb county. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/politico-nightly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico }}}\uc2  pointed out why, saying Macomb \u8220\'20\'1Coccupies a unique role on the political map.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf the more than 3,000 counties in the US, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to find one that\u8217\'20\'19s a better barometer of the atmospheric conditions affecting the 2024 election [than] Macomb county, with its high percentage of \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 The blue-collar suburb is often referred to as a bellwether, though \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s more like an indicator species in biology, offering important clues on the environmental health of an ecosystem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One attendee at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech who was an auto worker, Doug King, 55, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2023/09/27/donald-trump-returns-auto-industry-strike-uaw-ev-taking-center-stage-presidential-election-joe-biden/70960155007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Detroit News}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe four years under Trump were the best years that we had in the auto industry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump told workers negotiations between the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t mean as much as you think\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Railing against the shift to electric vehicles, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2023/09/27/donald-trump-returns-auto-industry-strike-uaw-ev-taking-center-stage-presidential-election-joe-biden/70960155007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CYou can be loyal to American labour or you can be loyal to the environmental lunatics. But you can\u8217\'20\'19t really be loyal to both. It\u8217\'20\'19s one or the other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Kevin Munoz, called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech \u8220\'20\'1Cincoherent\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cpathetic\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crecycled\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump went to Michigan a day after Biden. On Tuesday, in a historic moment in neighbouring Wayne county, Biden joined a \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket line and expressed support for striking workers.\par \par \uc2 The president did so at the invitation of the union president, Shawn Fain. Fain did not meet Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commondreams.org/news/fain-trump-billionaire-class#:~:text=%22He%20serves%20the%20billionaire%20class,manufacturer%20in%20Clinton%20Township%2C%20Michigan."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling CNN}}}\uc2  the former president, the Republican presidential frontrunner, \u8220\'20\'1Cserves the billionaire class\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see no point in meeting with him because I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the man has any bit of care about what our workers stand for, what the working class stands for,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe serves the billionaire class and that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s wrong with this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230928ej9s002e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
