\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump urges \uc2 UAW\uc2  to endorse him in speech at non-union car parts maker\b0\par\par\uc2 Tom Perkins in Clinton Township, Michigan \par \uc2 715 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2023\par 13:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Frontrunner in Republican primary speaks at Michigan car parts firm one day after Biden joined autoworkers\u8217\'20\'19 picket line\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tried to woo US autoworkers in a rambling speech in Michigan on Wednesday night that took potshots at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , electric vehicles and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  while pushing culture war issues and fell far short of supporting the core issues that have many car workers currently on strike.\par \par \uc2 The speech came a day after \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/uaw-strike-biden-visit-update-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to striking United Auto Workers}}}\uc2  members on a picket line nearby. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s historic appearance was the first time that a sitting president has walked a picket line.\par \par \uc2 Trump dismissed that as a \u8220\'20\'1Cphoto op\u8221\'20\'1D at Drake Enterprises, a non-unionised car parts maker in Macomb county, a few miles from where Biden spoke to striking employees picketing a Ford facility.\par \par \uc2 The former US president and other prominent Republicans have consistently attacked unions but many are now being more supportive of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike. Trump is the overwhelming frontrunner in the Republican 2024 nomination race and Michigan and other rust belt states are seen as crucial battlegrounds in the race for the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour leadership should endorse me and I will not say a bad thing about them again,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump, though he did not substantively address the issues at stake in the strike beyond expressing support for getting better wages.\par \par \uc2 At one stage Trump said that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/who-is-shawn-fain-uaw-strike-union-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shawn Fain}}}\uc2 , should endorse him and called him \u8220\'20\'1Ca good man \u8230\'20\'26 he\u8217\'20\'19s got to endorse Trump\u8221\'20\'1D. In the run-up to the visit Fain, however, has been withering in his opinion of Trump and declined to meet him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see no point in meeting with him because I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the man has any bit of care about what our workers stand for, what the working class stands for,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/27/us/politics/shawn-fain-trump-uaw.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit. \u8220\'20\'1CHe serves a billionaire class, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s wrong with this country.\u8221\'20\'1D Biden had attended the \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket at Fain\u8217\'20\'19s invitation.\par \par \uc2 Several hundred people attended the speech, which was timed to coincide with the latest Republican presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you look at the thousands of people outside, why couldn\u8217\'20\'19t you get a bigger plant?\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump.\par \par \uc2 The crowd appeared to be in the hundreds and while the speech took place, it thinned to less than a hundred as the rain came down. At one moment Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who has a long history of exaggerating crowd sizes at his events \u8211\'20\'13 falsely claimed that there were \u8220\'20\'1C10,000\u8221\'20\'1D people outside the venue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust get your union guys, your leaders, to endorse me and I will take care of the rest,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CUnder a Trump presidency, gasoline engines will be allowed and sex changes for children will be banned. Is that OK?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump consistently attacked electric vehicles (EVs) and said US autoworkers would lose their jobs if the country made the shift to EVs. He pledged to support gas-powered cars. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will drill baby drill and it will have zero environmental difference,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Michigan is a crucial battleground for the 2024 election. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lost the state to Trump in 2016 but Biden took it back from Trump in 2020. It looks set to be a hard-fought race next year.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the speech, the crowd shouted \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CFuck \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Christopher Demopolis, 35, who works in heating and cooling, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see why he won\u8217\'20\'19t win Michigan next time around \u8211\'20\'13 a lot of this is going to determine it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, motioning to the lively crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump supports the workers, Biden supports the leaders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Debbie Swolfs, a retired caterer who also owned a cleaning business, ran through a litany of complaints of life under Biden: inflation, gas prices, illegal immigrants, the move to electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need Trump back!\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CDo you remember how wonderful things were three years ago? I want that back,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBiden is compromised by China and he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to be impeached \u8211\'20\'13 he needs to be put in handcuffs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 28 September 2023 to correct Christopher Demopolis\u8217\'20\'19s occupation.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230928ej9s000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
