\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pitch for autoworker votes in car heartland is short on autoworkers\b0\par\par\uc2 Tom Perkins in Clinton Township, Michigan \par \uc2 707 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2023\par 04:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The ex-president gave a rambling speech at a car parts firm but it was unclear how many of the small crowd were autoworkers\par \par \uc2 As the rain came down a small crowd was still left outside Drake Enterprises, a non-union automotive manufacturing plant in Clinton Township, Michigan, on Wednesday night waiting for former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to take our country back! Let Biden sleep in his hospital bed! We want guns! We want Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D shouted one of the 50 or so people still waiting as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade pulled away from the sodden event. He declined to give his name.\par \par \uc2 Trump spoke at the plant a day after President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had joined a picket line in nearby Wayne in support of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 strike against Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s big three auto companies.\par \par \uc2 Before the speech began, hundreds of Trump supporters lined the street in an industrial park, erupting in cheers as the former president\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade pulled in.\par \par \uc2 The gathering had all the festive, and sometimes chaotically surreal, energy that is often part of Trump rallies. Supporters banged on drums, breaking to yell \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom!\u8221\'20\'1D and drawing loud cheers from up and down the street. Many were draped in Trump 2024 flags. Another flag showed Trump as a Rambo-like figure holding a grenade launcher. Passing traffic blared their horns in support.\par \par \uc2 Inside the event, Trump gave a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/donald-trump-michigan-uaw-autoworkers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rambling speech for more than an hour.}}}\uc2  Union workers should support him because electric cars would take their jobs, said Trump. China and other foreign powers were the real enemy, not low wages or incompetent bosses. \u8220\'20\'1CYour current negotiations don\u8217\'20\'19t mean as much as you think,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump.\par \par \uc2 By Trump standards, the crowd was small but there was no doubting their enthusiasm and they did not seem to mind the twisting word salad of the speech as it touched on trans rights, the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , grudges against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s current 2024 Republican opponents.\par \par \uc2 Clinton Township is in Macomb county, a crucial battleground in 2024\u8217\'20\'19s election, and the one thing that Trump and Biden have in common is a recognition that voters here are crucially important in the race for the White House.\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly given the nature of the event, the crowd was firmly behind Trump.\par \par \uc2 Ed Sands, a 73-year-old retired auto supplier employee, said Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only one who gives a shit about working people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , Obama \u8211\'20\'13 they were all terrible for Macomb county, jobs went to China, south, and you see all these people here today because Trump will bring them back,\u8221\'20\'1D Sands added.\par \par \uc2 The former US president\u8217\'20\'19s return to office is all but guaranteed, Sands said. \u8220\'20\'1CLook around you, look at these people. Do you think he is going to lose? Do you?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christopher Demopolis, 35, who works in heating and cooling, echoed that sentiment, and said his \uc2 UAW\uc2  base will play a role. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see why he won\u8217\'20\'19t win Michigan next time around \u8211\'20\'13 a lot of this is going to determine it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, motioning to the lively crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump supports the workers, Biden supports the leaders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Though the focus of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s event was on auto unions, it was unclear how many union members were there. Several of those who spoke with the Guardian said they were small business owners, or work for small businesses, but their numbers in this swing county are high.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the thing \u8211\'20\'13 there are people who are union, but there\u8217\'20\'19s also a whole bunch of us who are not and who work for small businesses, and we are more pro-Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D said Laura, who lives in nearby Mount Clemens, she declined to give her last name.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech came a day after a New York judge ruled that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s business fortune was built on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/trump-liable-fraud-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rampant fraud and blatant lies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 None of that seemed to faze his supporters. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t care if he didn\u8217\'20\'19t pay taxes,\u8221\'20\'1D said a supporter who declined to give his name. \u8220\'20\'1CHe shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even have to pay taxes!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230928ej9s000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
