\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Las Vegas hospitality workers vote to authorize strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 498 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2023\par 17:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Two sides still \u8216\'20\'18far apart\u8217\'20\'19 after months of negotiations with the largest three gaming companies in Las Vegas\par \par \uc2 Hospitality workers in Las Vegas have voted to authorize a strike if their union does not reach a contract deal with dozens of hotels on the Las Vegas strip.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of workers attended the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.culinaryunion226.org/news/press/strike-vote-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike vote}}}\uc2  on Tuesday at the Thomas & Mack Center on the University of Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 Las Vegas (UNLV) campus. The union slogan headlining the event was: \u8220\'20\'1COne job should be enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of the 53,000 members, 95% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Culinary226/status/1706893595616428398?t=BavXA4LndRn4tFi0feD5Ag&s=19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  in favor of authorizing the strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCompanies are generating record profits, and we demand that workers aren\u8217\'20\'19t left behind and have a fair share of that success,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ted Pappageorge, secretary-treasurer for the Culinary Union, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs companies reduce labor, there are less workers who have even more responsibilities and are doing more work instead of spending quality time with their families, and that has to change. Workers have built this industry and made it successful and that\u8217\'20\'19s why we are demanding that workers share in that prosperity,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Pappageorge said the two sides were still \u8220\'20\'1Cfar apart\u8221\'20\'1D after months of negotiations with the largest three gaming companies in Las Vegas.\par \par \uc2 Among the asks from the union include \u8220\'20\'1Cwinning the largest wage increases ever negotiated in the history of the Culinary Union\u8221\'20\'1D amid high inflation rates in recent years, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ktnv.com/news/the-cost-of-living-in-las-vegas-may-never-be-the-same"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high cost of living}}}\uc2  in Las Vegas, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.8newsnow.com/news/local-news/mgm-officially-lays-off-18k-furloughed-workers-amid-pandemic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furloughs}}}\uc2  during the beginning of the Covid pandemic that greatly affected hospitality workers.\par \par \uc2 The union is also pushing for reducing housekeeping workloads, mandating daily room cleaning, which was eliminated throughout much of the hotel industry during the pandemic, expanding safety protections for workers on the job, and adding clarifying language to a no-strike clause that gives casino workers the right to respect picket lines and does not prevent the union from taking action against non-union restaurants on casino properties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy job got so much harder since the pandemic and I\u8217\'20\'19m in constant pain at work. When I get home I feel guilty that I don\u8217\'20\'19t have energy to spend time with my son, help him with his homework, or even cook dinner some nights,\u8221\'20\'1D said Evangelina Alaniz, a guest room attendant at the Bellagio and a Culinary Union member for 18 years. \u8220\'20\'1COften, I have to go to bed so I have enough strength to go to work the next day and serve the guests.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union has not yet set a strike deadline, but workers are currently working under expired contracts at 22 locations among \uc2 MGM Resorts\uc2 , \uc2 Caesars Entertainment\uc2 , and Wynn/Encore Resorts. Negotiations began in April, with contract extension agreed upon in June that expired in early September as the union noted a lack of substantial progress.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, 25,000 hospitality workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.culinaryunion226.org/2018#:~:text=Las%20Vegas%2C%20NV%20(11%2F,subcontracting%2C%20technology%2C%20and%20immigration."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to authorize a strike, with contracts settled with employers soon after the vote.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230927ej9r001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
