\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 A meat processer killed a 16-year-old. Yet US lawmakers want more child labor\b0\par\par\uc2 Akin Olla \par \uc2 980 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2023\par 16:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Adult workers are demanding a fairer slice of corporate profits \u8211\'20\'13 so child labor is a way to increase and undercut the labor pool\par \par \uc2 This July the body of 16-year-old Duvan Tomas Perez \u8220\'20\'1Cbecame entangled\u8221\'20\'1D in meat processing machinery in Mississippi, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wdam.com/2023/07/20/should-not-have-been-hired-mar-jac-releases-new-info-following-teens-death/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to a statement from \uc2 Mar-Jac Poultry\uc2 , the company where the boy was working. Perez was too young to be working there, according to Mar-Jac, which blamed an outside staffing company for failing to verify Perez\u8217\'20\'19s age and identity. Perez was not the first worker to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/07/20/1188959743/meatpacking-death-teenager-mississippi-poultry-plant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 die}}}\uc2  at the plant in recent years, and he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/child-deaths-labor-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not the first}}}\uc2  16-year-old to die at work in the US this summer.\par \par \uc2 American legislators should be working to crack down on child labor, here and abroad, but instead, politicians \u8211\'20\'13 including Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/child-labor-laws-under-attack/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least}}}\uc2  11 states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wptv.com/news/state/could-florida-become-next-state-to-loosen-child-labor-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  or passed bills that weaken child labor laws. At a time when adult workers are demanding a fairer slice of the increasingly behemoth pie of corporate profits, child labor is a capitalist work-around to increase the labor pool and lower the wages of all those who have to work for a living.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m embarrassed to be writing an anti-child labor article in the year 2023, as if this is some Charles Dickens novel leaking gruel and cruel men. It is not as if child labor had ever disappeared, of course; children around the world toil in fast-fashion sweatshops and among the mountains of garbage in other countries but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2019-05-29/the-rich-world-s-electronic-waste-dumped-in-ghana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 produced}}}\uc2  by Silicon Valley. This is unfortunately where capitalism is heading, and has always been heading: children competing with their parents for jobs amid the ruins of societies we sacrificed for profit. But for awhile it seemed like child labor might have escaped the empire to live primarily in its colonial subjects.\par \par \uc2 Child labor was once as rampant in the US as it is in the countries of the developing world. In 1900, one out of five American children \u8211\'20\'13 including children as young as 10 \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2017/article/history-of-child-labor-in-the-united-states-part-1.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were employed}}}\uc2 . A quarter of textile workers in the American south were under the age of 16. In the north, factories relied on child labor so heavily that some areas suffered from \u8220\'20\'1Cboy shortages\u8221\'20\'1D that led to corporate agents traveling the country in search of orphaned children to put to work.\par \par \uc2 It is difficult to calculate the total number of legal and illegal child workers in the US today. In the agricultural industry alone, there are likely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://afop.org/cif/learn-the-facts/#AFOP_estimates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of thousands}}}\uc2  of children, largely from Central America. A \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/25/us/unaccompanied-migrant-child-workers-exploitation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  earlier this year found that many US brands directly or indirectly use child labor, including Lucky Charms, Nature Valley, Ford and J Crew.\par \par \uc2 While some of that work is legal, the federal government, at least, has been cracking down on illegal child labor. The number of minors in child labor violations has increased by 283% since 2015, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/press/with-child-labor-violations-on-the-rise-new-report-shows-that-child-labor-laws-are-under-attack-in-states-across-the-country/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 . According to the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/03/01/american-child-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over}}}\uc2  800 companies illegally employed children in the past fiscal year, and one meatpacking company was fined for employing children across 13 different plants.\par \par \uc2 Legal child labor may seem like an odd turn of phrase but child labor isn\u8217\'20\'19t at all banned in the US. The 1938 Fair Labor Standards Act created a federal minimum wage and banned children under 16 from \u8220\'20\'1Chazardous\u8221\'20\'1D work, but left agricultural workers out of many of its reforms. This is why so many children are \u8220\'20\'1Clegally\u8221\'20\'1D employed, and why many agricultural workers in the US do not have a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nationalaglawcenter.org/state-compilations/agpay/minimumwage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right to a minimum wage}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These policies allowed the US to maintain its long history of relying on slavery and near slavery for its agricultural wealth and give companies the ability to replace adult workers with children when adult workers demand decent pay \u8211\'20\'13 an increasingly common occurrence since Covid reminded workers of how important they are, and how little they are valued.\par \par \uc2 The pandemic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/covid-pandemic-emergency-workforce-jobs-recession-rcna83412"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed}}}\uc2  over a million Americans, many of them workers or potential workers, and brought on a wave of retirements that left an even larger hole in the labor market. Holes like this can increase the value of individual workers and allow them to negotiate for higher wages, a trend that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://history.wustl.edu/news/how-black-death-made-life-better"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 followed}}}\uc2  the bubonic plague in Europe. The meat-processing company where Duvan was working alluded to the underlying conditions that landed the company with child workers: \u8220\'20\'1CDue to an unprecedentedly tight labor market, Mar-Jac MS relies on staffing companies to fill positions at its facility,\u8221\'20\'1D a statement the company issued in July said.\par \par \uc2 While some companies are turning towards automation, others are turning towards taking our teens from schools and into factories. Instead of cutting CEOs\u8217\'20\'19 record salaries, corporate leaders \u8211\'20\'13 and their political allies \u8211\'20\'13 are fighting to maintain low wages by any means necessary.\par \par \uc2 Iowa has moved to allow children as young as 14 to work in industrial laundries and meat coolers, as well as created a special license to allow some 14-year-olds to drive up to 50 miles for work between 5am and 10pm. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2023/01/24/measures-seek-to-change-nebraskas-new-voter-approved-minimum-wage-provisions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebraska}}}\uc2  has moved to join other states in allowing employers to pay people under 20 less than minimum wage \u8211\'20\'13 as low as $4.25 an hour. These laws are being pushed by groups such as \uc2 Americans for Prosperity\uc2 , various chambers of commerce, and restaurant associations aiming to hire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/21/business/child-labor-alcohol/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 younger bartenders}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some legislators characterize the work that killed Duvan as potential sources of revenue for struggling immigrant families. But this is a macabre policy solution birthed by a sanguinary system. Instead of putting children to work, we ought to ask ourselves if a system that cannot rid itself of child labor is worth keeping.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Akin Olla is a contributing opinion writer at the Guardian US\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230927ej9r00136\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
