\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden joins picket line to tell \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikers: \u8216\'20\'18You deserve a significant raise\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Tom Perkins in Wayne, Michigan, and Robert Tait in Washington \par \uc2 798 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par 19:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 24\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President makes historic solidarity visit to Detroit-area plant day before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  amid dispute between union and carmakers\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  became the first sitting US president to appear on a picket line on Tuesday, joining a protest outside a Michigan car plant in solidarity with striking members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2 , which is locked in an escalating dispute with America\u8217\'20\'19s three biggest carmakers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/who-is-shawn-fain-uaw-strike-union-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shawn Fain}}}\uc2 , was the first to greet Biden after he arrived in Michigan on Air Force One, and he joined him in the presidential limousine for a ride to the picket line.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact of the matter is you guys \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 you saved the automobile industry back in 2008 and before. You made a lot of sacrifices, gave up a lot. The companies were in trouble. Now they are doing incredibly well and guess what? You should be doing incredibly well too,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, addressing the cheering crowd through a bullhorn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou deserve a significant raise and other benefits. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get back what we lost,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the enemy isn\u8217\'20\'19t some foreign company miles away. It\u8217\'20\'19s right here in our own area \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s corporate greed,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said as Biden, wearing a \uc2 UAW\uc2  baseball cap with the words \u8220\'20\'1CUnion Yes\u8221\'20\'1D on the side, looked on. Biden later put his arm around one of the red T-shirt-wearing \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the weapon we produce to fight that enemy is the liberators, the true liberators \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s the working-class people,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain added.\par \par \uc2 Standing on the picket line Larry Hearn, a 61-year-old \uc2 UAW\uc2  committee member, called Biden\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1Cmonumental and history-making\u8221\'20\'1D visit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re out here on the frontline taking the brunt for everybody, losing money,\u8221\'20\'1D Hearn said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe support feels good. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need him to get in our business and secure us a contract, but his support is enough, it hits home with people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden bills himself as the most pro-union president in history. No other sitting president has joined a picket line, according to Nelson Lichtenstein, a longtime labor historian at the \uc2 University of California, Santa Barbara\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is genuinely new \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s ever happened before, a president on a picket line,\u8221\'20\'1D Lichtenstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/why-biden-uaw-strike-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CCandidates do it frequently and prominent senators, but not a president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US president\u8217\'20\'19s visit comes a day before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his expected Republican opponent in next year\u8217\'20\'19s poll, visits Detroit \u8211\'20\'13 the historic centre of the US car industry \u8211\'20\'13 to address workers in different industries in his own pitch for the strikers\u8217\'20\'19 support.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who won Michigan with the help of union members\u8217\'20\'19 support in his 2016 election victory over \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  before losing it four years later in his defeat to Biden, is not expected to visit a picket line.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCrooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is killing the United Autoworkers with his WEAK stance on China and his ridiculous insistence on All Electric Cars, every one of which will be made in China, saw that I was going to Michigan this week (Wednesday!), so the Fascists in the White House just announced he would go there tomorrow,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump posted on his Truth Social website this week.\par \par \uc2 Biden voiced support for the strike by Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  workers, which was entering its 12th day on Tuesday, when it started on 15 September and had announced he was dispatching his labour secretary, Julie Su, and Gene Sperling, a senior White House adviser, to help the union reach a settlement with company bosses.\par \par \uc2 That plan was withdrawn after criticism from Fain, who has also flatly rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts at wooing the support of union members.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who won significant union support in 2016 and needs to regain it if he is to prevail next year, has said workers are being betrayed by their leadership and also by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s environmentally friendly policy of encouraging the three American car giants to convert to making electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has withheld an endorsement of Biden so far, but union leadership has been critical of Trump, who has sought to capitalize on the strike and siphon support from the majority Democratic unions. Trump visits a non-union shop tomorrow, which was not lost on those outside the Wayne plant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs long as Biden is going to come here then do something to help working people when he returns to Washington, then he is welcome,\u8221\'20\'1D said Walter Robinson, a 57-year-old quality inspector. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is going to have to do that if he wants our endorsement. I think he will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230926ej9q0018k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
