\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  leader fighting to defend autoworkers from \u8216\'20\'18corporate greed\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 959 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par 12:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain, who started work as an electrician for Chrysler in 1994, vowed to reform the union and take the fight to bosses\par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain isn\u8217\'20\'19t messing around. Just six months into his job as president of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 , he is leading US car workers in their biggest strike in a generation and on Tuesday secured a historic first: getting a sitting US president to join the pickets.\par \par \uc2 The 54-year-old is the grandson of two \uc2 UAW\uc2  retirees and won the union\u8217\'20\'19s presidency in a close-fought election in March. From the get-go he has taken an aggressive, uncompromising stance as the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has negotiated new contracts with Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s big three automakers.\par \par \uc2 Before his election, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/31/business/uaw-autoworkers-union-corruption.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rife with corruption}}}\uc2 . Senior figures, including the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/local/michigan/2022/07/21/ex-uaw-gary-jones-dennis-williams-corruption-released-prison/10120167002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gary Jones}}}\uc2 , were jailed for embezzlement. The scandal led to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first-ever election by direct vote rather than by a convention of delegates. Fain won on a promise of internal reform and external action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our shot for true reform of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , to put the power and control of our union back in the hands of the membership by electing leaders who will be held accountable by the membership,\u8221\'20\'1D his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://shawnfainforoneuaw.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  campaign page}}}\uc2  said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rochsent.com/opinion/kokomo-native-shawn-fain-s-uaw/article_c2450f35-e096-5f8c-8698-65108d68ecd1.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Born}}}\uc2  and raised in Kokomo, Indiana, he got his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://shawnfainforoneuaw.com/about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 start}}}\uc2  working at a Chrysler plant as an electrician in 1994. He served in local union roles before serving for 10 years as a \uc2 UAW\uc2  international representative, a role in which he spoke out against concessions made by the union during the 2008 economic recession. \u8220\'20\'1CYou might as well get a gun and shoot yourself in the head,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kokomotribune.com/news/local_news/kokomo-locals-say-no-to-contract/article_a7c17a15-4430-5709-8496-454231d1e817.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 UAW\uc2  at the time.\par \par \uc2 His anger at that deal has not abated. In August, when \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  (as Chrysler is now known) made one of its first contract offers to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , Fain threw it in the trash on a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  live feed. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s where it belongs \u8211\'20\'13 in the trash \u8211\'20\'13 because that\u8217\'20\'19s what it is,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Fain also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/21/uaw-big-three-automakers-union-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused the usual handshake}}}\uc2  with the big three\u8217\'20\'19s CEOs that has been the traditional start of contract negotiations for decades. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no point in having a big pomp and ceremony where we act like we\u8217\'20\'19re friends, and we\u8217\'20\'19re working together, when we\u8217\'20\'19re not,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain. \u8220\'20\'1CThe membership comes first. That\u8217\'20\'19s our job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fain has clearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/uaw-shawn-fain-president-strike-detroit-159a2745faf1f88e330c2ae94408dfa3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlined}}}\uc2  the grievances of union membership with the automakers. Concessions made in previous contracts since the 2008 economic recession have to go, he has said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to work with the companies. I want to have a good relationship,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut if they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to treat our members with respect and not give them their due, then we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have issues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  boss has effectively contrasted those concessions with the record profits and soaring pay enjoyed by the car companies and their executives.\par \par \uc2 The big three US automakers have showered shareholders with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/e8414a40-e80f-4dea-b237-7de56cc4e06c?shareType=nongift&fbclid=IwAR3Z_oPXOm-uKh0PoReGuMt2RnS1g5eExV06VL2xDMeeNVqmjRB-XBhoTug"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly $85bn}}}\uc2  in dividends and stock buybacks since the 2008 economic recession and auto bailouts, while autoworker wages have fallen with inflation taken into account.\par \par \uc2 The automakers have come out of the Covid-19 pandemic with record profits, with combined totals of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/e8414a40-e80f-4dea-b237-7de56cc4e06c?shareType=nongift&fbclid=IwAR3Z_oPXOm-uKh0PoReGuMt2RnS1g5eExV06VL2xDMeeNVqmjRB-XBhoTug"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over $70bn }}}\uc2  in 2021 and 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey pretend that the sky will fall if we get our fair share of a quarter of a trillion dollars the big three has made over the past decade,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain in a recent video released by the \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z2sgkOVS_Ko"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 titled}}}\uc2  Corporate Greed. \u8220\'20\'1COne of our workers would have to work 400 years to make what a CEO makes in one year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But while his rhetoric has been head-on, his tactics have been more subtle and owe more to Sun Tzu\u8217\'20\'19s The Art of War. Fain surprised the automakers in announcing a \u8220\'20\'1Cstand up\u8221\'20\'1D strike strategy in which local unions would be called up to strike by the \uc2 UAW\uc2  as the majority of the workforce would continue reporting to work.\par \par \uc2 The tactic left the automakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2023/09/19/uaw-strike-auto-plants/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guessing incorrectly}}}\uc2  where strikes would first begin while conserving the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strike fund to pay its members. It is also the first time in the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s history that the union is on strike at all three automakers. Following some movement in negotiations with Ford, Fain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/us-auto-workers-strike-uaw-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanded}}}\uc2  the strike last week to 38 parts and distribution sites across 20 states at \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His strategy and rhetoric, aimed broadly at wealth inequality and corporate greed, has garnered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2023/09/25/uaw-president-fain-compared-to-reuther-while-running-multiple-strikes/70954743007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparisons}}}\uc2  to Walter Reuther, who served as president of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  from 1946 to 1970 and oversaw an aggressive expansion of the labor movement in the 1950s and 60s.\par \par \uc2 But perhaps the most unusual outcome of Fain\u8217\'20\'19s campaign so far has been its impact on Washington. Joe Biden joins the picket line on Thursday \u8211\'20\'13 a historic first for a sitting president. His most likely 2024 rival, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , will address autoworkers in Michigan on Thursday, though the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/19/politics/fain-trump-detroit/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strongly criticized}}}\uc2  Trump. Polling suggests both candidates are right to back the workers \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/americans-broadly-support-auto-hollywood-strikes-reutersipsos-poll-2023-09-21/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 58% of Americans support}}}\uc2  the strike with 32% against, according to a Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe corporate media is scared. The billionaire class is scared and the big three is scared,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lphRMZF4Wmk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video posted}}}\uc2  on the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest live stream last week. \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to make you think you don\u8217\'20\'19t deserve your fair share. They want you to be afraid because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid. They\u8217\'20\'19re afraid because they see their system, where the billionaires keep everything, crumbling. The world is watching and the people are on our side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230926ej9q001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
