\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Biden joins stars in hailing \u8216\'20\'18deal\u8217\'20\'19 to end Hollywood writers strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,755 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par 10:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Writers Guild of America says tentative agreement on pay and conditions \u8216\'20\'18due to the willingness of this membership to exercise its power\u8217\'20\'19. Plus, how to deal with garlic breath, according to scientistsDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The tentative deal reached between Hollywood and studio executives has been received well by those on strike and others within the industry.\par \par \uc2 Members from the Writers Guild of America (WGA), who took on the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wga-writers-strike-demands-d403f5b4666f20e2ce3e379bcaef5f2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands}}}\uc2  that included better pay and residuals, and safeguards on the use of artificial intelligence, shared their collective relief.\par \par \uc2 The WGA said on Sunday: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have reached a tentative agreement on a new 2023 MBA, which is to say an agreement in principle on all deal points, subject to drafting final contract language. What we have won in this contract \u8211\'20\'13 most particularly, everything we have gained since 2 May \u8211\'20\'13 is due to the willingness of this membership to exercise its power, to demonstrate its solidarity, to walk side-by-side, to endure the pain and uncertainty of the past 146 days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The organization called the deal \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptional\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  say about the deal? The president issued a statement on the strike\u8217\'20\'19s imminent end and praised the power of collective bargaining. \u8220\'20\'1CThis agreement, including assurances related to artificial intelligence, did not come easily. But its formation is a testament to the power of collective bargaining. There simply is no substitute for employers and employees coming together to negotiate in good faith toward an agreement that makes a business stronger and secures the pay, benefits, and dignity that workers deserve.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is the Hollywood writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike really over? While there is still much that is unclear \u8211\'20\'13 the nature of the deal, which needs to be ironed out in contractual language and ratified by union leadership and its 11,500 members, has yet to be revealed \u8211\'20\'13 the picture of a post-strike Hollywood is coming into focus. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/sep/25/is-hollywood-writers-strike-over-deal-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is what we know so far}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Staggering\u8217\'20\'19 green growth gives hope for 1.5C, says global energy head\par \par \uc2 The prospects of the world staying within the 1.5C limit on global heating have brightened owing to the \u8220\'20\'1Cstaggering\u8221\'20\'1D growth of renewable energy and green investment in the past two years, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/sep/26/staggering-green-growth-gives-hope-for-15c-says-global-energy-head"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chief of the world\u8217\'20\'19s energy watchdog has said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fatih Birol\uc2 , the executive director of the \uc2 International Energy Agency\uc2  and the world\u8217\'20\'19s foremost energy economist, said much more needed to be done though the rapid uptake of solar power and electric vehicles was encouraging.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the scale of the challenges, I feel more optimistic than I felt two years ago,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSolar photovoltaic installations and electric vehicle sales are perfectly in line with what we said they should be, to be on track to reach net zero by 2050, and thus stay within 1.5C. Clean energy investments in the last two years have seen a staggering 40% increase.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Birol also noted that greenhouse gas emissions from the energy sector were \u8220\'20\'1Cstill stubbornly high\u8221\'20\'1D, and that the extreme weather seen around the world this year had shown the climate was changing \u8220\'20\'1Cat frightening speed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else did the report say? The \uc2 IEA\uc2 , in a report entitled Net Zero Roadmap, published this morning, also called on developed countries with 2050 net zero targets to bring them forward by several years. Some already have closer dates, such as Germany with 2045 and Austria and Iceland with 2040 \u8211\'20\'13 and for many developing countries are much later, at 2060 in the case of China, and 2070 in India\u8217\'20\'19s case.\par \par \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  refuses to quit and says $480,000 in cash was for personal use\par \par \uc2 Insisting he would not resign after being indicted on corruption charges, the embattled New Jersey Democratic senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/25/bob-menendez-will-not-resign-indictment-bribery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bob Menendez told reporters}}}\uc2  the $480,000 in cash found in a safe, clothing and closets at his home was kept there for emergency personal use.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CFor 30 years, I have withdrawn thousands of dollars in cash from my personal savings accounts, which I have kept for emergencies and because of the history of my family facing confiscation in Cuba.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The senator\u8217\'20\'19s parents are from Cuba and he was born in New York. Last week, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not lost on me how quickly some are rushing to judge a Latino and push him out of his seat.\u8221\'20\'1D In Union City, New Jersey, on Monday, Menendez spoke in English and in Spanish. A group of people he said were \u8220\'20\'1Ceveryday people and constituents who know me\u8221\'20\'1D stood behind him as he spoke.\par \par \uc2 The senator continued: \u8220\'20\'1CNow this may seem old-fashioned, but these were monies drawn from my personal savings accounts based on the income that I have lawfully derived over those 30 years. I look forward to addressing other issues in trial.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is Menendez accused of? Under an indictment unsealed last week, Menendez and his wife, Nadine Menendez, 56, were accused of using his seat in the Senate, as chair of the foreign relations committee, to benefit the government of Egypt.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Actor David McCallum, who became a teen heartthrob in the hit series The Man from U\par \par \uc2 ncle in the 1960s and was the eccentric medical examiner in the popular television show NCIS 40 years later, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/sep/25/david-mccallum-man-from-uncle-ncis-dies-age-90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has died}}}\uc2 . He was 90. McCallum died on Monday of natural causes, surrounded by family, \uc2 CBS\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  warned at least three Americans active in the Sikh community that their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/26/indian-government-sikh-activist-hardeep-singh-nijjar-murder-canada-fbi-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lives were in danger}}}\uc2  in the immediate aftermath of the murder of a Sikh activist in Canada\par \par \uc2 in June. The Canadian prime minister, \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 , has blamed the apparent assassination on the Indian government.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The National Transportation Safety Board\uc2  said it has opened an investigation into a \uc2 JetBlue\uc2  flight that experienced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/25/jetblue-investigation-florida-flight-severe-turbulence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sudden severe turbulence}}}\uc2  yesterday, injuring seven passengers and a crew member. The injured were taken to hospital for evaluation and treatment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A third person has been charged in the death of a toddler apparently poisoned by fentanyl in\par \par \uc2 a New York City daycare center, as the search continues for the alleged ringleader of the drug-peddling operation. Renny Antonio Parra Paredes, 38, was charged with narcotics distribution resulting in death.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hopes are fading for the \u8220\'20\'1Cre\par \par \uc2 awakening\u8221\'20\'1D of India\u8217\'20\'19s moon lander after Indian scientists were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/26/india-chandrayaan-3-vikram-lander-pragyan-sleep-mode-failure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unable to }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/26/india-chandrayaan-3-vikram-lander-pragyan-sleep-mode-failure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 communicat}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/26/india-chandrayaan-3-vikram-lander-pragyan-sleep-mode-failure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 e with the spacecraft}}}\uc2  since it went into shutdown mode to survive the freezing lunar night\par \par \uc2 s. There is a 50% chance that the devices could endure the low temperatures.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Antarctic sea ice shrinks to lowest annual maximum level on record, data shows\par \par \uc2 Antarctica is likely to have broken the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/26/antarctic-sea-ice-shrinks-to-lowest-annual-maximum-level-on-record-data-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record for the lowest annual maximum amount of sea ice}}}\uc2  around the continent, beating the previous low by a million square kilometres. The new mark is the latest in a string of records for the region\u8217\'20\'19s sea ice, as scientists fear global heating could have shifted the region into a new era of disappearing ice with far reaching consequences for the world\u8217\'20\'19s climate and sea levels.\par \par \uc2 Each September, Antarctica\u8217\'20\'19s sea ice reaches its maximum extent. The average between 1981 and 2010 was 18.71m sq km. But the US National Snow and Ice Data Center said preliminary analysis suggested the sea ice reached a maximum of 16.96m sq km on 10 September and had fallen since then.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: I survived three days in a capsized boat on the ocean floor \u8211\'20\'13 praying in my air bubble\par \par \uc2 Harrison Okene was sitting on the toilet \u8211\'20\'13 surely the worst place to be as disaster strikes \u8211\'20\'13 when a freak wave hit the tugboat he was working on, and turned it upside down. Now he was on the floor, and the toilet was above him. \u8220\'20\'1CI was trying to open the door to get out, when the toilet fell and hit me on the head,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. He just had time to see blood pour from the wound before the lights went off. \u8220\'20\'1CEverywhere was dark.\u8221\'20\'1D The bathroom began to fill with water. \u8220\'20\'1CIt didn\u8217\'20\'19t take long,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1COne minute, two minutes\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and he felt the boat touch the seabed. Thirty metres (100ft) below the surface, it came to rest.\par \par \uc2 Okene had no choice but to listen in the dark as the shouts of his colleagues fell silent. His throat throbbed and his tongue peeled. Ten years on, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/sep/26/i-survived-three-days-in-a-capsized-boat-on-the-ocean-floor-praying-in-my-air-bubble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he explains why he loves the sea more than ever}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and decided to become a diver,\par \par \uc2 Climate check: \u8216\'20\'18Whatever it takes\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 students at 50 US high schools launch climate initiative\par \par \uc2 Students at more than 50 high schools across the US are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/sep/25/green-new-deal-schools-climate-initiative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposing a Green New Deal for Schools}}}\uc2 , demanding that their districts teach climate justice, create pathways to green jobs after graduation and plan for climate disasters, among other policies. The campaign, coordinated by the Sunrise Movement, a youth-led climate justice collective, is a reaction to rightwing efforts to ban or suppress climate education and activism at schools. The national effort could include teach-ins and walkouts, as well as targeted petitions to school boards and districts in the coming weeks, organizers with Sunrise told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are prepared to do whatever it takes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adah Crandall, 17, an organiser for the Sunrise Movement based in Portland, Oregon.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Eat yog\par \par \uc2 urt to ward off garlic breath, say scientists\par \par \uc2 If you have ever skipped the garlic for fear of romantic rejection, take note: you can have your date and eat garlic \u8211\'20\'13 provided you {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2023/sep/25/scientists-eating-yoghurt-can-prevent-garlic-breath"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow up with a spoonful of yogurt}}}\uc2 . Research suggests the fat and protein that yogurt contains prevents almost all of the smelly volatile compounds in garlic from escaping into the air. Manpreet Kaur and Prof Sheryl Barringer at the \uc2 Ohio State University\uc2  in Columbus, US, tested the capacity of yogurt \u8211\'20\'13 and the water, fat and protein in it \u8211\'20\'13 to neutralize the sulfurous compounds that give raw and cooked garlic its characteristic odor. Their results, published in the journal Molecules, suggested yogurt alone reduced 99% of the most odor-producing volatiles in raw garlic. They found higher-fat yogurt was better than lower-fat yogurt.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230926ej9q0013b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
