\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to the \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket line is historic \u8211\'20\'13 and may pay off politically\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,324 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par 10:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president standing \u8216\'20\'18in solidarity\u8217\'20\'19 with striking autoworkers is a powerful gesture that could resonate with key blue-collar voters\par \par \uc2 In the more than 150 years since workers first formed labor unions in the United States, no American president has ever stood \u8220\'20\'1Cin solidarity\u8221\'20\'1D with workers on a picket line. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has vowed to do exactly that with striking autoworkers in Michigan on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is genuinely new \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s ever happened before, a president on a picket line,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nelson Lichtenstein, a longtime labor historian at the \uc2 University of California, Santa Barbara\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CCandidates do it frequently and prominent senators, but not a president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit to the picket line, labor experts say, will give him a political boost in Michigan and other industrial swing states and might also help nudge the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 and automakers to a quicker settlement. But some experts say his visit could backfire if the walkout drags on for months or seriously hurts the nation\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s predecessors were often far more hostile toward strikers. In 1894, Grover Cleveland dispatched federal troops to help shut down a railroad strike; during the Korean war in 1952, \uc2 Harry Truman\uc2  seized the nation\u8217\'20\'19s steel mills in response to a steelworkers\u8217\'20\'19 strike; and in 1981, \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  fired 11,345 striking air traffic controllers.\par \par \uc2 Biden has said he will be the most pro-union president ever, and visiting a picket line is indeed unprecedented for a president\par \par \uc2 Meg Jacobs of \uc2 Princeton University\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBiden has said he will be the most pro-union president ever, and visiting a picket line is indeed unprecedented for a president,\u8221\'20\'1D said Meg Jacobs, a labor historian at \uc2 Princeton University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike is the first to hit all three big US car manufacturers simultaneously. The union has emphasized the huge profits Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  have made since the 2008/2009 recession and claimed little has been passed on to workers.\par \par \uc2 CEO pay at the big three has increased by 40% since 2013 as profits have soared. GM\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2 , the highest-paid CEO of the three, pocketed $28.97m last year. Meanwhile, auto manufacturing workers have seen their average real hourly earnings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/uaw-automakers-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fall 19.3% since 2008}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The union\u8217\'20\'19s messaging has so far won popular support, with 58% of Americans backing the strike according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/americans-broadly-support-auto-hollywood-strikes-reutersipsos-poll-2023-09-21/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters/Ipsos poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president, Shawn Fain, called for everyone \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom our friends and families {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/us-auto-workers-strike-uaw-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all the way up to the president}}}\uc2  of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cjoin us on the picket line\u8221\'20\'1D. Hours later, Biden tweeted, \u8220\'20\'1CTuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/POTUS/status/1705325183697932561?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll go to Michigan to join the picket line}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D saying he planned to \u8220\'20\'1Cstand in solidarity with the men and women\u8221\'20\'1D of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jacobs said the picket line visit could have important political benefits for Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a smart move. There\u8217\'20\'19s no way for him to win the presidency without industrial states like Michigan,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacobs said. \u8220\'20\'1CBiden has to do well in the important industrial swing states that \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lost to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016 [Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 all of which Biden won back in 2020]. Going to the picket line signals a commitment to working families, to the working class. It signals to workers in those states that he is authentic about this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Trump campaign attacked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan to join the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikers, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing more than a cheap photo-op\u8221\'20\'1D and saying it was inspired by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to speak in Detroit to union members on Wednesday. A week ago, Trump campaign sources said the former president would give a speech to 500 workers, including many \uc2 UAW\uc2  members, on 27 September at the same time the second Republican presidential debate is held. Labor experts said it was highly unusual for a former president to arrive in a city that\u8217\'20\'19s the center of a major strike with the intention of somehow intervening and making political gains. Trump is expected to attack Biden over his plan to bring about a quick transition to electric vehicles, a move that Trump says will endanger autoworkers\u8217\'20\'19 jobs.\par \par \uc2 All this shows that Biden and Trump are vying for an important political group, blue-collar workers, and that helps explain Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit. \u8220\'20\'1CBiden realizes that constituency is important,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacobs said.\par \par \uc2 Marick Masters, an auto industry expert at \uc2 Wayne State University in Detroit\uc2 , said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan to join a picket line was an astute way to counter Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Detroit speech. \u8220\'20\'1CIn his visit, Trump is trying to energize his base and embarrass Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D Masters said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut Biden coming to a picket line here will make it harder for Trump to embarrass Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Masters said there was an easy way for Biden to trump his predecessor, who hasn\u8217\'20\'19t indicated that he would join a picket line: \u8220\'20\'1CAll Biden has to say is \u8216\'20\'18I came and stood by you. Someone else who occupied this office didn\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Masters agreed that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit could give him a needed political boost. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of autoworkers are blase when it comes to Biden. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get a great deal of enthusiasm. But his visit could generate support,\u8221\'20\'1D Masters said. \u8220\'20\'1C[Union members] will go the extra mile and be more willing to campaign for him and vote for him. It could very well make the difference\u8221\'20\'1D in the industrial swing states \u8220\'20\'1Cif there is a close election and it\u8217\'20\'19s a redo of 2020.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit could still backfire, said Masters, if the strike drags on for months or is seen as pushing the nation into recession. But if it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t: \u8220\'20\'1CI think this show of commitment will inspire a lot of union members and they won\u8217\'20\'19t forget this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Some labor experts see Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit as mainly symbolic as far as the contract talks are concerned. They say that notwithstanding his pro-union rhetoric, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have much leverage.\par \par \uc2 Art Wheaton\uc2 , director of labor studies at \uc2 Cornell University\uc2 , said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure whether Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit would help speed a settlement, but he didn\u8217\'20\'19t doubt that it would help him politically. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know if it persuades GM [or the other automakers] to move faster,\u8221\'20\'1D Wheaton said.\par \par \uc2 As for the political angle, Wheaton said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to be on the union side, saying, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m for the working person, I\u8217\'20\'19m publicly siding with the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\u8217\'20\'19 It takes away one talking point from Trump that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s not doing anything. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s standing up with the workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Biden\u8217\'20\'19s move may be unprecedented, Princeton\u8217\'20\'19s Jacobs said she still saw Franklin Roosevelt as the most pro-union president in history. \u8220\'20\'1CI think FDR deserves the title as the most friendly toward labor,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacobs said. \u8220\'20\'1CWithout the Wagner Act [the landmark 1935 law that the New Deal Congress enacted to create a federally guaranteed right to unionize and bargain collectively], we wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and the labor protections we have today. I think Biden is very much a New Deal Democrat. He sees labor in the same way. It\u8217\'20\'19s not new that he talks about corporations\u8217\'20\'19 record profits and translating record profits into record gains for workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If ever there was a moment for a Democratic president to join a picket line, this is probably it, said UC Santa Barbara\u8217\'20\'19s Lichtenstein. \u8220\'20\'1CToday the Democratic party is probably more united on labor issues than any time since the New Deal, and even then, the whole southern Democratic contingent was hostile toward labor,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CEven with Kennedy and Johnson, there was a whole anti-labor contingent in the Democratic party. But right now is a rare moment when labor is very popular, and it usually isn\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230926ej9q0018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
