\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Exceptional\u8217\'20\'19: Hollywood writers hail tentative deal to end strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 935 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par 21:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Writers Guild of America says agreement on pay and conditions \u8216\'20\'18due to the willingness of this membership to exercise its power\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/sep/25/hollywood-writers-strike-end-wga-deal-details-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tentative deal }}}\uc2  reached between Hollywood and studio executives has been received well by those on strike and others within the industry.\par \par \uc2 Members from the Writers Guild of America (WGA), who took on the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ) with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wga-writers-strike-demands-d403f5b4666f20e2ce3e379bcaef5f2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands}}}\uc2  that included better pay and residuals, and safeguards on the use of artificial intelligence, shared their collective relief.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wgacontract2023.org/announcements/negotiations-update-tentative-agreement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  issued on Sunday, the WGA said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have reached a tentative agreement on a new 2023 MBA, which is to say an agreement in principle on all deal points, subject to drafting final contract language.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we have won in this contract \u8211\'20\'13 most particularly, everything we have gained since 2 May \u8211\'20\'13 is due to the willingness of this membership to exercise its power, to demonstrate its solidarity, to walk side-by-side, to endure the pain and uncertainty of the past 146 days. It is the leverage generated by your strike, in concert with the extraordinary support of our union siblings, that finally brought the companies back to the table to make a deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The organization called the deal \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptional\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Joe Biden issued a statement on the strike\u8217\'20\'19s imminent end and praised the power of collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI applaud the Writers Guild of America and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  for reaching a tentative agreement that will allow writers to return to the important work of telling the stories of our nation, our world \u8211\'20\'13 and of all of us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis agreement, including assurances related to artificial intelligence, did not come easily. But its formation is a testament to the power of collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere simply is no substitute for employers and employees coming together to negotiate in good faith toward an agreement that makes a business stronger and secures the pay, benefits, and dignity that workers deserve. I urge all employers to remember that all workers \u8211\'20\'13 including writers, actors, and auto workers \u8211\'20\'13 deserve a fair share of the value their labor helped create.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Also on Monday, California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , called the writers a vital part of the state\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia\u8217\'20\'19s entertainment industry would not be what it is today without our world-class writers. For over 100 days, 11,000 writers went on strike over existential threats to their careers and livelihoods \u8211\'20\'13 expressing real concerns over the stress and anxiety workers are feeling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am grateful that the two sides have come together to reach an agreement that benefits all parties involved, and can put a major piece of California\u8217\'20\'19s economy back to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a show of solidarity, fellow union the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  congratulated the WGA on their win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Teamsters\uc2  congratulate \uc2 WGA East\uc2  and \uc2 WGA West\uc2  writers on their militancy and unwavering solidarity, winning a tentative agreement after almost five months on strike! The WGA strike has inspired workers everywhere to stand up against corporate greed and anti-worker technology. #1u,\u8221\'20\'1D the group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Teamsters/status/1706301755871391838"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  wrote on X}}}\uc2 , previously known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The actor Mark Ruffalo also wrote on X: \u8220\'20\'1CBravo! WGA proves when we fight we win. #Unionize. Congratulations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bravo! WGA proves when we fight we win. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Unionize?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Unionize}}}\uc2 . Congratulations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WGAWest?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WGAWest}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WGAEast?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WGAEast}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WGAStrike?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WGAStrike}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/faBlQrPDeZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/faBlQrPDeZ}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Ruffalo (@MarkRuffalo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarkRuffalo/status/1706306656047407156?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Mindy Kaling, an actor, and writer and producer of several projects including The Office and The Mindy Project, also joined the picket line. Upon the announcement of the tentative deal, she posted on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CTENTATIVE AGREEMENT B******! CAN\u8217\'20\'19T WAIT TO GO BACK TO WORK AND SEE MY PEOPLE!!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Referencing her old show, she quoted Michael Scott, who said: \u8220\'20\'1CI love my employees even though I hit one of you with my car.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Talkshows were suspended during the strike, including Jimmy Kimmel Live, The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, The Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon, Late Night with Seth Meyers and Last Week Tonight with John Oliver.\par \par \uc2 Together, hosts from these shows collaborated on a limited series podcast called Strike Force Five, with all proceeds benefiting their out-of-work staff. Now that an agreement has been reached, the shows are expected to resume as early as October.\par \par \uc2 Plans for The Drew Barrymore Show to resume in the midst of the strike drew ire from the WGA and its supporters, but now that the strike is over, the show is also likely to resume production soon.\par \par \uc2 Representatives from the show did not immediately respond to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Fellow strikers from \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 , the largest labor union representing performers and broadcasters, congratulated their colleagues on their win, but expressed hope for their own deal with the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  soon.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sagaftra/status/1706170038393442647"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on X, \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CTo our fellow union siblings who serve on the WGA negotiating committee, we extend our heartfelt congratulations on securing a tentative agreement with the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2 . We applaud your dedication, diligence and unwavering solidarity over the last five months and are proud to stand shoulder to shoulder with you as creative partners in the entertainment industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe look forward to reviewing the terms of the WGA and \uc2 AMPTP\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tentative agreement. And we remain ready to resume our own negotiations with the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  as soon as they are prepared to engage on our proposals in a meaningful way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUntil then, we continue to stand strong and unified. In solidarity, the Sag-Aftra TV/theatrical/streaming negotiating committee #SagAftraStrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230925ej9p0028w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
