\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \u8216\'20\'18Tentative\u8217\'20\'19 deal reached to end 146-day Hollywood writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,335 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par 09:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After five days of negotiations with studios and streaming services, union says it has a deal for members to vote on. Plus, meet the oldest fish in captivity\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood writers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/sep/25/hollywood-writers-strike-end-wga-deal-details-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poised to end their nearly five-month strike}}}\uc2  after reaching a tentative agreement with studios, the writers\u8217\'20\'19 union and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  said on Sunday night, though the full details of agreement still have to be formally approved.\par \par \uc2 The deal came after five marathon days of renewed talks by negotiators for the Writers Guild of America (WGA) and an alliance of studios, streaming services and production companies, and must be approved by the guild\u8217\'20\'19s board and members before the strike officially ends.\par \par \uc2 The terms of the deal were not immediately announced, but the WGA called the deal \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptional \u8211\'20\'13 with meaningful gains and protections for writers in every sector of the membership\u8221\'20\'1D in an email to members.\par \par \uc2 Four top industry executives \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 , of \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO, \uc2 David Zaslav\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2  co-CEO \uc2 Ted Sarandos\uc2  and \uc2 NBCUniversal\uc2  Studio group chair, \uc2 Donna Langley\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 joined negotiations this week, helping to break the months-long impasse.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happens now? Union leaders are expected to vote on the full terms of the new three-year contract on Tuesday, according to the union\u8217\'20\'19s email to members, which was posted on social media.\par \par \uc2 AOC joins calls for \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to resign from Senate over corruption charges\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  has joined the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/24/bob-menendez-new-jersey-senator-corruption-alexandria-ocasio-cortez"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls for Bob Menendez to resign}}}\uc2 , after the Democratic US senator from New Jersey was charged with accepting gold bars, a \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  and other gifts as bribes.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on Sunday, Ocasio-Cortez said the charges against Menendez were \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely serious\u8221\'20\'1D and he should step down.\par \par \uc2 A growing number of Democrats are calling for Menendez, who has represented New Jersey in the Senate since 2006, to resign.\par \par \uc2 Menendez is accused of using his position to aid Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian government and pressuring federal prosecutors to drop a case against a friend.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  became the first US Senate Democrat to suggest Menendez should quit, while a Democratic New Jersey congressman announced he would run against Menendez in next year\u8217\'20\'19s primary election.\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  visits peanut festival seven months after entering hospice care\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  and his wife, Rosalynn, made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/25/jimmy-carter-visits-plains-peanut-festival-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a surprise appearance at a peanut festival}}}\uc2  in their Georgia home town, the \uc2 Carter Center\uc2  wrote in a social media post on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president, who was once a peanut farmer, and his wife were seen in a video riding through the Plains Peanut festival in a black SUV.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeautiful day for President & Mrs. Carter to enjoy a ride through the Plains Peanut Festival! And just a week before he turns 99,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Carter Center\uc2  wrote on X after sharing the video taken by a spectator.\par \par \uc2 The former president is 98 and has been in home hospice care since February. He turns 99 on 1 October. The former first lady has since been diagnosed with dementia. The couple this summer marked their 77th wedding anniversary, extending their record as the nation\u8217\'20\'19s longest-married first couple.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What health issues does Carter have? In recent years, he has suffered from several health issues including melanoma that spread to his liver and brain, although he was said to have responded well to treatment. Last month their grandson, Josh Carter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/20/jimmy-carter-rosalynn-carter-final-chapter-grandson-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said the former first couple were \u8220\'20\'1Cstill holding hands\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  but that it was clear they were \u8220\'20\'1Cin the final chapter\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Megan Rapinoe ended her international career in familiar fashion: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/sep/25/megan-rapinoe-retirement-final-game-uswnt-soccer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victorious and mischievous}}}\uc2 . The star and her USA teammates defeated South Africa 2-0 in a friendly at Soldier Field in Chicago, ending her near two-decade career in which she won 203 caps, two World Cups and an Olympic gold medal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An independent Russian news outlet whose founder was hacked in Germany\par \par \uc2 this year through military-grade spyware has said it believes a European state was most likely behind the cyber-attack, raising questions about an EU member state\u8217\'20\'19s possible use of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/25/latvia-russia-meduza-phone-hack-galina-timchenko"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blacklisted cyberweapon}}}\uc2  against a journalist.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A hiker died after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/25/north-carolina-blue-ridge-parkway-glassmine-falls-fatal-fall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plunging off a waterfall overlook}}}\uc2  along the Blue Ridge parkway in North Carolina during the weekend, according to the \uc2 US National Park Service\uc2 . Nancy Sampson was sightseeing at the park on Saturday when she tumbled over a cliff around the Glassmine Falls overlook.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The speaker of Canada\u8217\'20\'19s House of Commons has apologised for praising an individual at a parliamentary meeting who fought for a Nazi military unit during the second world war. Lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/25/canadas-house-speaker-apologises-after-praising-ukrainian-veteran-who-fought-for-nazis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave 98-year-old Yaroslav Hunka a standing ovation}}}\uc2  when speaker Anthony Rota drew attention to him.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18I like him even better now\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s true believers keep the faith\par \par \uc2 Wearing a shirt festooned with countless images of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Leverne Martin was looking cheerful for a man who had set off from Poplar Bluff, Missouri, at 9pm and driven through the night, arriving in Dubuque, Iowa, at 5.30am. When did he intend to sleep? \u8220\'20\'1CAs soon as President Trump is back in the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D the 55-year-old handyman replied without missing a beat. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t get him back in 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue, where he belongs, we\u8217\'20\'19re in a mess, man. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m voting for President Trump. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I drove nine hours.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like so many fans in so many towns and cities over nearly a decade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/24/donald-trump-supporters-rally-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an overwhelmingly white crowd had come to cheer on Trump}}}\uc2 , elected US president in 2016, beaten by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 and clear frontrunner for the Republican nomination in 2024.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/24/washington-post-abc-poll-trump-10-points-over-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poll showing Trump up 10 points over Biden for 2024 election criticized}}}\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 introducing Southern Frontlines \u8211\'20\'13 news on the climate crisis from Latin America and the Caribbean\par \par \uc2 Latin America and the Caribbean are witnessing devastating effects of the climate crisis \u8211\'20\'13 from the degradation of the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and rampant biodiversity loss to forest fires, drought, glacial melt and ever more violent hurricanes. People already disadvantaged by unjust policies are now disproportionately affected by the extreme weather, fuelled by current and historic use of fossil fuels in wealthy nations. As the climate crisis deepens, so do humanitarian crises, rights abuses and global inequality.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2023/sep/25/introducing-southern-frontlines-news-on-the-climate-crisis-from-latin-america-and-the-caribbean"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian launches today Southern Frontlines}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 reporting on climate justice in Latin America and the Caribbean, a series on and from the most vulnerable communities in this region. We will be looking at the toll on people\u8217\'20\'19s health and livelihoods and highlighting the voices of those who are fighting back in the most dangerous countries in the world to be environmental defenders.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Methuselah arrived in the US in 1938. She\u8217\'20\'19s now the oldest fish in captivity\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s super-gentle, and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get overly excited. She enjoys eating earthworms, fruits and vegetables, and slowly moving around her tank. Her favorite food \u8211\'20\'13 at least for what is in season now \u8211\'20\'13 is a fig, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/24/lungfish-australia-methuselah-san-francisco"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Katharine Gammon}}}\uc2 . If Methuselah sounds like a grand old dame, it\u8217\'20\'19s because she is: she is the oldest living fish in captivity, aged somewhere upwards of 92 and potentially as high as 101 years. She arrived on a steamship from Australia along with 230 other fish to the Steinhart aquarium in San Francisco in 1938 as a young, small fish. And Methuselah\u8217\'20\'19s story unfolded in a typical way, for a fish in an aquarium: she grew. Humans came to look at her. She peered back through glass at humans. She\u8217\'20\'19s now the oldest fish in captivity.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230925ej9p0015r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
